var e={label:`Nintendo · official series history`,url:`https://www.nintendo.com/en-gb/Campaigns/The-Legend-of-Zelda-40th-Anniversary/The-Legend-of-Zelda-40th-Anniversary-Game-History-3186350.html`},t=(e,t,n,r,i,a)=>({id:e,title:t,objective:n,steps:r,tip:i,...a?{boss:a}:{}}),n=[{slug:`the-legend-of-zelda`,title:`The Legend of Zelda`,year:1986,platform:`Famicom Disk System / NES`,era:`classic`,intro:`A sword, an open wilderness and eight scattered pieces of wisdom. Keep a map of the discoveries that turn wandering into a route.`,edition:`First Quest, original game. First released in Japan in 1986; the western NES cartridge followed in 1987. Second Quest layouts differ.`,scope:`Main-story route through all nine levels; not a room-by-room map or collectible checklist.`,essentials:[`Find the Bow and buy arrows; shots spend rupees.`,`Keep bombs for walls and a potion for Death Mountain.`,`Five hearts qualify for the White Sword; twelve for the Magical Sword.`],chapters:[t(`eagle`,`A sword and the Eagle`,`Claim the first Triforce fragment.`,[`Take the sword from the starting cave.`,`Follow the river north to the island entrance of Level 1.`,`Find the Bow, collect keys and reach Aquamentus.`],`Sword beams work only at full health.`,`Stand away from its three fireballs and strike its head.`),t(`moon-manji`,`The Moon and the Manji`,`Open routes across the water.`,[`Clear Level 2 in the eastern woodland; collect the Magical Boomerang.`,`Enter Level 3 in the southwestern region.`,`Find the Raft before taking the third fragment.`],`Bombs can quickly remove clustered enemies.`,`Feed Dodongo bombs; bomb Manhandla when its heads cluster.`),t(`snake`,`The Snake`,`Obtain the Stepladder.`,[`Use the Raft at the western dock to reach Level 4.`,`Collect the Stepladder from its underground room.`,`Cross narrow water gaps and reach Gleeok.`],`The ladder bridges short gaps; it does not grant swimming.`,`Strike Gleeok's attached heads while avoiding detached ones.`),t(`lizard`,`The Lizard`,`Find the Recorder.`,[`Pass through the Lost Hills by repeatedly taking the northern exit.`,`Enter Level 5 and explore bombable connections.`,`Collect the Recorder before confronting Digdogger.`],`Refill bombs before the mountain journey.`,`Play the Recorder, then attack the reduced creature.`),t(`dragon`,`The Dragon`,`Secure fragment six.`,[`Travel to Level 6 near the graveyard region.`,`Work around Wizzrobe attacks and retrieve the Magical Rod.`,`Keep the Bow, arrows and rupees ready for Gohma.`],`Do not spend your final rupees before an arrow-dependent boss.`,`Shoot Gohma's eye when it opens.`),t(`demon`,`The Demon`,`Drain the concealed entrance.`,[`Buy Food before visiting the western pond without a fairy.`,`Play the Recorder there to expose Level 7.`,`Give Food to the hungry Goriya and explore for the Red Candle.`],`The Red Candle permits repeated flames within one screen.`,`Use the familiar Aquamentus strategy: avoid fire and strike its head.`),t(`lion`,`The Lion`,`Complete the Triforce of Wisdom.`,[`Burn the concealed entrance bush in the southeastern woods.`,`Search Level 8 for the Magical Key and Book of Magic.`,`Defeat Gleeok and take the eighth fragment.`],`The Magical Key removes the need to buy more dungeon keys.`,`Keep moving between attacks on Gleeok's heads.`),t(`death-mountain`,`Death Mountain`,`Prepare the weapon that can finish Ganon.`,[`Bomb the entrance at Spectacle Rock in the northern mountains.`,`Use all eight fragments to pass the entrance guardian.`,`Search the maze's bombable walls and stair passages for Silver Arrows and the Red Ring.`],`Both upgrades matter more than rushing straight to Ganon.`),t(`ganon`,`The final arrow`,`Rescue Zelda.`,[`Enter Ganon's chamber with the sword and Silver Arrows equipped.`,`Strike his invisible position while avoiding fireballs.`,`When he becomes vulnerable, fire a Silver Arrow; collect the Triforce and free Zelda.`],`Use your potion before a desperate final hit.`,`The sword creates the opening; the Silver Arrow supplies the finishing blow.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Zelda Dungeon · original-game walkthrough`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-legend-of-zelda-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · The Eagle`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-legend-of-zelda-walkthrough/level-1-the-eagle/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Recorder mechanics`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/wiki/Guide%3AHow_Does_the_Recorder_Work_in_The_Legend_of_Zelda%3F`}]},{slug:`adventure-of-link`,title:`Zelda II: The Adventure of Link`,year:1987,platform:`Famicom Disk System / NES`,era:`classic`,intro:`A journey measured in towns, techniques and dangerous roads. Palace treasures matter as much as the crystals placed after each victory.`,edition:`Original NES adventure; first released in Japan in 1987. Western release dates and some mechanics differ from the Disk System version.`,scope:`A practical six-palace route and Great Palace finale, including essential town abilities.`,essentials:[`Collect all four additional Magic Containers before seeking Thunder.`,`Learn Life and refill in towns before long crossings.`,`Take each palace's treasure before placing its crystal.`],chapters:[t(`parapa`,`Parapa Palace`,`Light the way beyond the first palace.`,[`Visit Rauru and learn Shield.`,`Cross the northeastern cave and desert to Parapa Palace.`,`Recover the Candle, defeat Horsehead and place the first crystal.`],`Change between high and low shield positions against armed enemies.`,`Jump and strike Horsehead's uncovered head; Shield reduces mistakes.`),t(`death-mountain`,`Towns and Death Mountain`,`Recover the Hammer.`,[`Recover Ruto's stolen trophy to learn Jump; learn Life in Saria.`,`Visit Bagu in the forest, then obtain passage across Saria's river.`,`Work through Death Mountain's caves to the Hammer; collect the nearby Magic Container.`],`The Candle makes these caves readable. Return to town when supplies run low.`),t(`midoro`,`Midoro Palace`,`Pass through breakable stone.`,[`Use the Hammer to reopen western shortcuts.`,`Enter the palace in Midoro Swamp.`,`Collect the Handy Glove, defeat Helmethead and place the second crystal.`],`Detours for experience are safer than repeatedly losing a nearly complete level.`,`Strike Helmethead's heads, then the exposed body; avoid the floating heads.`),t(`island`,`Island Palace`,`Reach eastern Hyrule.`,[`Visit Mido; use Jump to reach the teacher of the downward thrust.`,`Learn Fairy and enter the graveyard route to Island Palace.`,`Recover the Raft, defeat Rebonack and place the third crystal.`],`Fairy form can bypass narrow passages but cannot fight normally.`,`Downward-thrust onto Rebonack's horse, then fight his dismounted form.`),t(`maze`,`Maze Palace`,`Obtain the Boots and Reflect.`,[`Use the Raft at the eastern dock and visit Nabooru.`,`Find the kidnapped child on Maze Island and return him in Darunia to learn Reflect.`,`Collect the Boots in Maze Palace and reach Carock.`],`Darunia also offers the upward thrust through a roof-accessible house.`,`Cast Reflect and return Carock's spells with your shield.`),t(`ocean`,`Ocean Palace`,`Get the Flute.`,[`Use the Boots on the ocean path east of Nabooru.`,`Enter Ocean Palace and recover the Flute.`,`Defeat Gooma and place the fifth crystal.`],`Only specific ocean paths are walkable.`,`Stay just beyond Gooma's mace; jump in to strike and retreat.`),t(`hidden`,`Hidden Palace`,`Place the sixth crystal.`,[`Play the Flute at the River Devil to open the southern route.`,`Find New Kasuto, learn Spell and reveal the Magical Key; seek Thunder in Old Kasuto with full magic capacity.`,`Use the Flute at Three-Eye Rock, recover the palace's Cross, then defeat Barba and place the crystal.`],`The Cross reveals otherwise invisible enemies.`,`Use Jump and downward thrust against Barba's head as it rises; avoid the lava.`),t(`great-palace`,`The Great Palace`,`Claim the Triforce of Courage.`,[`Place all six crystals, then cross the Valley of Death.`,`Navigate the Great Palace while preserving enough magic for Thunder.`,`Defeat Thunderbird, then confront Shadow Link and awaken Zelda.`],`A game over inside this palace allows a restart at its entrance.`,`Cast Thunder to expose Thunderbird's face. For Shadow Link, vary sword height and punish openings instead of spending offensive magic.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Adventure of Link route`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-adventure-of-link-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Midoro and Death Mountain`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-adventure-of-link-walkthrough/midoro-palace/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Great Palace`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-adventure-of-link-walkthrough/great-palace/`}]},{slug:`a-link-to-the-past`,title:`The Legend of Zelda: A Link to the Past`,year:1991,platform:`Super Famicom / Super NES`,era:`classic`,intro:`Two Hyrules share one geography. When one blocks your path, investigate the other.`,edition:`Super NES quest, Japan 1991. GBA Four Swords bonus content is excluded.`,scope:`Main-story dungeons, essential unlocks and final-battle preparation.`,essentials:[`Bring medicine and preserve magic.`,`Collect the Ice Rod before Turtle Rock.`,`Some Dark World dungeons permit alternative orders.`],chapters:[t(`rescue-east`,`Rescue and Eastern Palace`,`Earn the first pendant.`,[`Enter the castle and escort Zelda through the sewers.`,`Meet Sahasrahla east of Kakariko.`,`Find Eastern Palace's Bow and defeat the Armos Knights.`],`Collect Sahasrahla's Pegasus Boots afterward.`,`Shoot the knights; dodge the final one's jumps.`),t(`desert`,`Desert Palace`,`Lift pale rocks.`,[`Dash into the library shelf for the Book of Mudora.`,`Read the desert inscription to enter.`,`Collect the Power Glove and light the final torches.`],`Desert ledges connect separate entrances.`,`Strike Lanmolas' heads as they emerge.`),t(`hera`,`Tower of Hera`,`Keep your form across worlds.`,[`Escort the mountain's old man for the Magic Mirror.`,`Use the mountain portal and Mirror to reach the tower.`,`Retrieve the Moon Pearl and defeat Moldorm.`],`Falling resets Moldorm's fight.`,`Strike its tail; protect your footing.`),t(`agahnim`,`Master Sword and castle`,`Enter the Dark World.`,[`Take the Master Sword from the Lost Woods with three pendants.`,`Return to the castle and break its magical barrier.`,`Climb to Agahnim and return his energy attacks.`],`Lightning cannot be volleyed back; move aside.`),t(`dark-palace`,`Palace of Darkness`,`Claim the Hammer.`,[`Pay Kiki to open the eastern palace.`,`Use bombs and switches to reach the Hammer.`,`Break Helmasaur King's mask and rescue the first maiden.`],`Keep enough rupees for Kiki.`,`Hammer the mask, then attack the exposed green weak point.`),t(`swamp`,`Swamp Palace`,`Get the Hookshot.`,[`Buy Zora's Flippers.`,`Drain the Light World watergate, then enter its Dark World counterpart using the Mirror route.`,`Retrieve the Hookshot and manipulate the floodgates.`],`The palace depends on changing both worlds.`,`Pull Arrghus's orbiting creatures away with the Hookshot, then strike its body.`),t(`skull`,`Skull Woods`,`Recover the Fire Rod.`,[`Explore the forest's separate holes and skull entrances.`,`Take the Fire Rod from the large chest.`,`Burn the final entrance's obstruction and reach Mothula.`],`Keep magic for torches and combat.`,`Fire Rod blasts hurt Mothula; watch the moving floor and spikes.`),t(`thieves`,`Thieves' Town`,`Obtain the Titan's Mitt.`,[`Enter beneath the village statue.`,`Bomb the cracked upper floor to admit sunlight below.`,`Retrieve the Mitt and escort the captive into that light.`],`The apparent rescue reveals the boss.`,`Strike Blind's active head, then avoid the detached heads.`),t(`ice`,`Ice Palace`,`Release the fifth maiden.`,[`Lift Lake Hylia island's dark rock to reach the portal.`,`Melt the entrance guard with the Fire Rod.`,`Solve the block-and-switch route to Kholdstare.`],`Save magic for the boss.`,`Melt its shell, then attack the three eyes.`),t(`mire`,`Misery Mire`,`Find the Cane of Somaria.`,[`Activate the Flute in Kakariko and fly to the desert ledge.`,`Enter the Dark World and use Ether at the medallion mark.`,`Retrieve the Cane and use its blocks on switches.`],`Keep the Boots available for long gaps.`,`Clear Vitreous's smaller eyes before attacking the large one.`),t(`turtle`,`Turtle Rock`,`Rescue the final maiden.`,[`Use Quake at the eastern mountain entrance.`,`Create platforms with Somaria and recover the Mirror Shield.`,`Carry both elemental rods to Trinexx.`],`The Ice Rod is found outside the dungeon.`,`Freeze the fire head, burn the ice head, then strike the moving body's weak point.`),t(`tower`,`Ganon's Tower`,`Prepare the final confrontation.`,[`After crystals five and six, escort the Big Bomb to the Pyramid crack.`,`Upgrade the Bow to Silver Arrows at the fairy.`,`With seven crystals, climb Ganon's Tower and defeat Agahnim again.`],`Restock magic and potions before climbing.`),t(`ganon`,`Beneath the Pyramid`,`Finish the battle.`,[`Follow Ganon into the Pyramid.`,`Dodge his attacks; use spin attacks if your Master Sword is unupgraded.`,`Relight the torches, stun him and fire Silver Arrows.`],`Falling resets the fight.`,`Keep the arena lit during the Silver Arrow phase.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Palace of Darkness and linked chapter index`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/a-link-to-the-past-walkthrough/dark-palace/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Swamp Palace`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/a-link-to-the-past-walkthrough/swamp-palace/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Ganon's Tower`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/a-link-to-the-past-walkthrough/ganons-tower/`}]},{slug:`links-awakening`,title:`The Legend of Zelda: Link's Awakening`,year:1993,platform:`Game Boy`,era:`handheld`,intro:`Eight instruments, one impossible island. Every new movement tool opens another path through Koholint—and another question about the dream.`,edition:`1993 Game Boy main quest. DX adds the optional Color Dungeon. Switch 2019 changes controls and adds Chamber Dungeons; those features are not required here.`,scope:`Eight-dungeon route and Wind Fish finale, with the necessary trading and music milestones.`,essentials:[`On Game Boy, assign tools to A and B; sword and shield are not permanently mapped.`,`Continue the trading sequence for the Magnifying Lens; buy the Bow before the finale.`,`Learn the Ballad of the Wind Fish from Marin.`],chapters:[t(`tail`,`Tail Cave`,`Find the first instrument.`,[`Take your shield from Tarin and recover the sword on the beach.`,`Bring the forest mushroom to the witch; use Magic Powder on the raccoon for the Tail Key.`,`Enter Tail Cave and collect Roc's Feather.`],`Jump over pits and low enemies.`,`Strike Moldorm's tail; stay away from the edge.`),t(`bottle`,`Bottle Grotto`,`Lift the island's obstacles.`,[`Rescue BowWow from the Moblin hideout.`,`Let BowWow eat the swamp flowers blocking the dungeon.`,`Find the Power Bracelet and reach the Genie.`],`Return BowWow afterward.`,`Dodge fire, strike the moving bottle, then lift and throw it; attack the Genie once the bottle breaks.`),t(`key`,`Key Cavern`,`Acquire the Pegasus Boots.`,[`Trade the Yoshi Doll through to the bananas.`,`Give bananas to Kiki, recover five Golden Leaves for Richard and find the Slime Key.`,`Enter Key Cavern; combine running and jumping across wide gaps.`],`Long jumps use Boots and Feather together.`,`Dash into the wall to drop Slime Eye, then cut and dash through its narrowing connection.`),t(`angler`,`Angler's Tunnel`,`Learn to swim.`,[`Take Marin from the beach to awaken the Animal Village walrus.`,`Defeat the desert Lanmola for the Angler Key; open the mountain waterfall.`,`Enter the tunnel and obtain the Flippers.`],`Dive to explore deep water.`,`In the side-view battle, strike Angler Fish's glowing lure.`),t(`catfish`,`Catfish's Maw`,`Recover the Hookshot.`,[`Escort the following ghost to its seaside home, then its grave.`,`Dive into the underwater entrance near Martha's Bay.`,`Defeat Master Stalfos at its successive locations to reclaim the Hookshot.`],`Mark passages that need the new tool.`,`Pull Slime Eel's real head from a wall hole and strike its exposed neck.`),t(`face`,`Face Shrine`,`Lift heavier statues.`,[`Explore the Southern Face Shrine and obtain the Face Key.`,`Enter the main shrine and upgrade the Power Bracelet.`,`Use heavy statues and chess pieces to complete its puzzles.`],`Bombs are essential for the boss.`,`Place bombs on Facade's face while avoiding flying tiles and pits.`),t(`eagle`,`Eagle's Tower`,`Bring down the upper floor.`,[`Learn the Frog's Song of Soul from Mamu and revive Mabe's rooster.`,`Use the rooster in the mountains to recover the Bird Key.`,`Carry the tower's iron ball to destroy all four supporting pillars; take the Mirror Shield.`],`Plan the ball's path before dropping through holes.`,`Block Evil Eagle's gust with the shield and attack when it approaches.`),t(`turtle`,`Turtle Rock`,`Take the eighth instrument.`,[`Use the Mirror Shield through the flame passage.`,`Wake the turtle head with the Frog's Song and defeat it.`,`Inside, steer floor-making blocks and recover the Magic Rod.`],`The rod melts ice; consider the path before firing.`,`Strike Hot Head with the Magic Rod as it rises from lava.`),t(`egg`,`The Wind Fish's Egg`,`Follow your own maze clue.`,[`Finish the trading sequence; use the Lens to read Mabe's hidden library book.`,`With eight instruments, play the Ballad before the egg.`,`Follow the book's directions and defeat the Nightmare's forms.`],`Use the clue from your game instead of a memorized maze route.`,`Powder the slime, return magic, attack exposed sword forms, then shoot the final open eye while jumping its arms.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Nintendo · Switch control changes`,url:`https://zelda.nintendo.com/links-awakening/ca/gameplay/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Game Boy Color Face Shrine`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/links-awakening-walkthrough/face-shrine-game-boy-color/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · original boss guide`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/Zelda04/laboss.pdf`}]},{slug:`oracle-of-seasons`,title:`The Legend of Zelda: Oracle of Seasons`,year:2001,platform:`Game Boy Color`,era:`handheld`,intro:`Winter builds bridges. Summer grows ladders. Learn to read Holodrum as four overlapping landscapes rather than one fixed map.`,edition:`Original 2001 Game Boy Color quest. Animal-companion terrain can vary. A linked game adds events and an additional shared finale.`,scope:`Standalone route through eight Essences to Onox; linked-game continuation is identified separately.`,essentials:[`Change seasons while standing on a tree stump.`,`Collect each new seed type when its tree becomes accessible.`,`Read the Maku Tree's guidance between dungeons.`],chapters:[t(`root`,`Gnarled Root Dungeon`,`Recover the first Essence.`,[`Find the sword in Hero's Cave and visit the Maku Tree.`,`Use the Gnarled Key to open the northern tree dungeon.`,`Take the Seed Satchel and use Ember Seeds on unlit torches.`],`Refill seeds before leaving their tree.`,`Avoid Aquamentus's fireballs and strike its horn.`),t(`snake`,`Winter and Snake's Remains`,`Obtain the Power Bracelet.`,[`Follow the Subrosian portal route to the Temple of Seasons.`,`Receive the Rod's winter power; use snow to reach Holly and her Shovel.`,`Open Snake's Remains, collect the Bracelet and solve its pot switches.`],`Winter changes ledge access as well as water.`,`Feed Dodongo a bomb, then lift and throw it onto spikes.`),t(`moth`,`Summer and Poison Moth's Lair`,`Learn to jump.`,[`Open Spool Swamp's floodgates with their key.`,`Reach Subrosia; give Rosa her ribbon and follow her into the summer tower.`,`Grow the dungeon's entrance vines with summer and obtain Roc's Feather.`],`Your animal companion changes the swamp approach.`,`Jump over Mothula's attacks and strike when it lands.`),t(`dragon`,`Sunken City and Dancing Dragon`,`Acquire the Slingshot.`,[`Complete the Master Diver's test for the Flippers.`,`Explore Mount Cucco and unlock the Rod's spring power.`,`Recover the Dragon Key, enter the dungeon and find the Slingshot.`],`Spring flowers launch you to higher ground.`,`Shoot Gohma's open eye with Ember or Scent Seeds.`),t(`unicorn`,`Autumn and Unicorn's Cave`,`Master magnetic movement.`,[`Use the new mountain connections to obtain autumn power.`,`Change Eyeglass Lake's seasons to reach Unicorn's Cave.`,`Retrieve the Magnetic Gloves and move metal balls onto switches.`],`Change polarity to switch between pulling and pushing.`,`Drive the spiked metal ball into Digdogger and its smaller forms.`),t(`ruins`,`Tarm Ruins and Ancient Ruins`,`Recover the Magical Boomerang.`,[`Collect the four shaped jewels and fit them into Tarm Ruins' gate.`,`Use seasonal routes and the Lost Woods clue to reach the dungeon.`,`Steer the upgraded Boomerang around obstacles to hit switches.`],`Keep Feather ready for spikes and broken flooring.`,`Strike Manhandla's open flowers with the Boomerang; finish its exposed core with the sword.`),t(`crypt`,`The pirates and Explorer's Crypt`,`Find Roc's Cape.`,[`Follow the pirates' clues to the missing bell in Samasa Desert.`,`Have the Subrosian smiths restore it, then return it to the captain.`,`Sail west; use summer vines to reach the graveyard dungeon and collect the Cape.`],`Hold the jump input to extend the Cape's flight.`,`Cut Gleeok's heads, then jump its ground shockwaves and attack.`),t(`maze`,`Sword & Shield Maze`,`Finish the eight Essences.`,[`From Temple Remains, reach Subrosia's volcanoes and bomb the lava pit to trigger an eruption.`,`Return through the altered ruins; use summer vines and mountain passages to reach the dungeon portal.`,`Recover the Hyper Slingshot; carry ice crystals to cool lava and connect the dungeon halves.`],`Use spread shots when several torches need lighting.`,`Jump Medusa Head's attacks and strike its vulnerable eye.`),t(`onox`,`Onox's Castle`,`Rescue Din.`,[`Collect the Huge Maku Seed after all eight Essences.`,`Enter Onox's Castle, clearing its combat rooms.`,`Defeat Onox and the Dark Dragon, then save the ending's Secret to Labrynna.`],`That secret starts a linked Ages adventure; the shared Twinrova/Ganon finale belongs to linked play.`,`Spin-attack Onox; move Din's crystal with the Rod. In dragon form, jump onto a lowered hand and strike the forehead jewel.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Seasons route`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/oracle-of-seasons-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Unicorn's Cave`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/oracle-of-seasons-walkthrough/unicorns-cave/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Onox's Castle`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/oracle-of-seasons-walkthrough/onoxs-castle/`}]},{slug:`oracle-of-ages`,title:`The Legend of Zelda: Oracle of Ages`,year:2001,platform:`Game Boy Color`,era:`handheld`,intro:`The answer may be waiting centuries away. Follow the consequences of changed landscapes, planted seeds and unfinished promises through Labrynna.`,edition:`Original 2001 Game Boy Color quest. This is a standalone start; linked play changes some events and adds the shared finale.`,scope:`Main-story route through eight Essences and Veran, with the key past/present transitions.`,essentials:[`Note your era before following an overworld clue.`,`Keep a supply of Mystery Seeds for possession battles.`,`The Harp's successive tunes expand where you can travel.`],chapters:[t(`spirit`,`Spirit's Grave`,`Save the Maku Tree's future.`,[`Receive the sword from Impa after Nayru's possession.`,`Use the past route to rescue the young Maku Tree.`,`Enter Spirit's Grave and recover the Power Bracelet.`],`Lift pots and test movable blocks.`,`Destroy Pumpkin Head's body, lift its head, then attack the exposed spirit.`),t(`wing`,`Wing Dungeon`,`Obtain Roc's Feather.`,[`Retrieve the Harp of Ages at Nayru's house.`,`Travel into the past when the present dungeon entrance collapses.`,`Enter Wing Dungeon and solve its coloured-floor puzzles.`],`The past entrance replaces a blocked present route.`,`Throw bombs into Head Thwomp's open top; aim for the damaging red result.`),t(`moon`,`Crescent Island and Moonlit Grotto`,`Recover your equipment and Seed Shooter.`,[`After the shipwreck, reclaim stolen tools from the Tokay through trades and challenges.`,`Plant the Scent Seedling in the past and collect its seeds in the present.`,`Open Moonlit Grotto and use the Seed Shooter's ricochets.`],`A seed can reach a target you cannot face directly.`,`Look away from Shadow Hag, then bounce a seed behind you when she approaches.`),t(`skull`,`Skull Dungeon`,`Learn the Switch Hook.`,[`Follow the Maku Tree's new clue toward the western highlands.`,`Use the available time routes to enter Skull Dungeon.`,`Take the Switch Hook and exchange places with distant objects.`],`Check the landing tile before swapping.`,`Hook Eyesoar's central eye away from its escort, then strike it.`),t(`crown`,`Rolling Ridge and Crown Dungeon`,`Obtain the Cane of Somaria.`,[`Help the Goron Elder using a Bomb Flower.`,`Follow Rolling Ridge's Goron routes to Crown Dungeon.`,`Make blocks with the Cane to hold switches and redirect movement.`],`One created block can replace an object you cannot carry.`,`Guide Smog's scattered clouds together with blocks, then attack the reunited cloud.`),t(`mermaid`,`Mermaid's Cave`,`Complete one dungeon across two eras.`,[`Follow the Goron trading and minigame chain for the Mermaid Keys.`,`Explore both past and present versions of the cave.`,`Collect the Mermaid Suit and use underwater passages to finish the route.`],`Underwater movement differs from ordinary swimming.`,`Hit Octogon's face with seeds; dive after it when it submerges.`),t(`jabu`,`Nayru and Jabu-Jabu`,`Expand time travel and upgrade the Hook.`,[`Enter Ambi's Palace when she leaves; free Nayru with Mystery Seeds, Switch Hook and sword.`,`Use the new Tune of Ages to help King Zora and clear the sea's pollution.`,`Enter Jabu-Jabu, change water levels and find the Long Hook.`],`Remember which floors become accessible at each water level.`,`Swap with Plasmarine so its projectile strikes it with the opposite colour.`),t(`tomb`,`Ancient Tomb`,`Collect the last Essence.`,[`Help the pirates and obtain the route into the Sea of No Return.`,`Use the past-era access to enter Ancient Tomb.`,`Find the Power Glove and collect the four slates that open its deeper route.`],`Ramrock changes the required tool between phases.`,`Return fists, bomb cupped hands, ricochet seeds behind its guard, then use the Glove on its ball hands.`),t(`veran`,`The Black Tower`,`Free Labrynna.`,[`Receive the Huge Maku Seed in the present.`,`Return to the past, enter the Black Tower and follow its maze clues.`,`Defeat Veran's possession and transformed phases; preserve the ending's linking secret.`],`A linked second adventure unlocks Twinrova and Ganon beyond the standalone ending.`,`Separate Veran with Mystery Seeds and the Long Hook. Bomb the spider, strike the turtle's exposed head, and attack the flying forms when accessible.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Ages route`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/oracle-of-ages-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Mermaid's Cave`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/oracle-of-ages-walkthrough/mermaids-cave/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Black Tower`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/oracle-of-ages-walkthrough/the-black-tower/`}]},{slug:`four-swords`,title:`The Legend of Zelda: Four Swords`,year:2002,platform:`Game Boy Advance`,era:`handheld`,intro:`Four colours, shared obstacles and a competitive rupee total: cooperation opens the route even when everyone wants the biggest purse.`,edition:`Original 2002 GBA multiplayer adventure, requiring two to four players. The 2011 Anniversary Edition adds solo control of two Links and extra areas.`,scope:`A flexible first-clear route to Vaati. The three opening areas use selected layouts, so this guide follows their mechanics rather than inventing a fixed room order.`,essentials:[`Agree who carries each pedestal item.`,`Rupees fund revival, so protect the team's supply.`,`Bring every player to the exit before advancing.`],chapters:[t(`training`,`Learn the shared controls`,`Make the party work together.`,[`Draw the Four Sword and complete the introductory instructions.`,`Practise lifting another Link and throwing them across a gap.`,`Assign one player to a switch while another crosses the opened route.`],`Say who moves first before anyone throws a teammate.`),t(`trees`,`Sea of Trees`,`Earn the forest's first key.`,[`Choose Sea of Trees from the stage selection.`,`Search each selected floor for its switches, required item and exit.`,`Cut vegetation for rupees and assemble the party before the boss.`],`A coloured obstacle belongs to the matching Link.`,`Attack Big Manhandla's coloured buds with the corresponding Link, avoiding the other heads.`),t(`cave`,`Talus Cave`,`Complete the ice challenge.`,[`Enter Talus Cave and collect the local pedestal equipment.`,`Cross slippery ground deliberately; position partners before moving shared blocks.`,`Take Pegasus Shoes into the Dera Zol encounter.`],`Stop dashing before an unprotected edge.`,`Ram Dera Zol into the icy wall with the Shoes, then slash it while frozen.`),t(`mountain`,`Death Mountain`,`Claim the third opening key.`,[`Choose Death Mountain and follow its selected lava-floor routes.`,`Use the provided equipment to cross hazards and reach separated switches.`,`Gather the party and available recovery before Gouen.`],`Wait for a safe landing rather than rushing across lava.`,`Return Gouen's coloured projectile with the matching Link; strike the scattered flames to reveal its body and finish the smaller form.`),t(`keys`,`Open Vaati's Palace`,`Turn three victories into the final route.`,[`Finish all three opening areas in whichever order suits the party.`,`Check that each has awarded its Silver Key.`,`Select the newly available Vaati's Palace and review the party's item roles.`],`Golden and Hero's Keys belong to later replay challenges; they are not required for the first ending.`),t(`palace`,`Cross the palace`,`Reach the wind sorcerer together.`,[`Inspect each room's item pedestals before splitting up.`,`Use Roc's Cape where supplied to cross the palace's gaps.`,`Coordinate distant switches and regroup at each exit.`],`Changing your carried item can solve a room that looked blocked; the equipment is not a permanent dungeon reward.`),t(`vaati`,`Vaati and the rescue`,`Release Zelda and complete the first quest.`,[`Use the arena's bombs against Vaati's tornado.`,`Attack the eye when he becomes vulnerable.`,`During the later form, coordinate colour-matched returns and attacks until he falls.`],`Call out the projectile's current colour; a volley can change the required player.`,`Time a bomb to explode beside Vaati inside the tornado. In the colour phase, use the matching Link against projectiles and exposed coloured targets.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Four Swords editions`,url:`https://zeldadungeon.net/wiki/The_Legend_of_Zelda%3A_Four_Swords`},{label:`Zelda Wiki · Vaati's Palace`,url:`https://zeldawiki.wiki/wiki/Vaati%27s_Palace`},{label:`Zelda Wiki · Gouen`,url:`https://zeldawiki.wiki/wiki/Gouen`}]},{slug:`four-swords-adventures`,title:`The Legend of Zelda: Four Swords Adventures`,year:2004,platform:`Nintendo GameCube`,era:`classic`,intro:`Hyrule becomes a stage for four heroes moving as one. Formations, shared switches and parallel worlds carry this rescue through eight regions.`,edition:`2004 GameCube Hyrulean Adventure campaign. Play solo with four Links or cooperatively; this is not the separate GBA Four Swords.`,scope:`Main campaign through its eight regions, Vaati and Ganon; not a room-by-room treasure guide.`,essentials:[`Collect 2,000 Force Gems per stage to break its final barriers.`,`Items and hearts do not remain as permanent stage-to-stage upgrades.`,`Choose formations for simultaneous switches and attacks.`],chapters:[t(`wind`,`Whereabouts of the Wind`,`Rescue the first maiden.`,[`Cross Lake Hylia using team lifts and switches.`,`Explore the Cave of No Return with its supplied tools.`,`Clear Hyrule Castle and destroy its powered-down barriers.`],`Revisit missed gem rooms if your sword lacks power.`,`Return Phantom Ganon's energy attacks, then strike while he is stunned.`),t(`east`,`Eastern Hyrule`,`Follow the coastal investigation.`,[`Clear the Coast and collect Moon Pearls for dark-world access.`,`Follow the Village of the Blue Maiden's conversations and exchanges.`,`Use both worlds to complete the Eastern Temple.`],`A blocked path can have a usable counterpart across a Moon Gate.`),t(`mountain`,`Death Mountain`,`Climb to the Tower of Flames.`,[`Complete the foothills using formation switches.`,`Follow the Mountain Path and obtain its Hammer.`,`Clear the Tower of Flames, using supplied tools on distant switches.`],`Retrieve a new item when the stage changes.`,`Break Helmaroc King's helmet with the Hammer, then attack its exposed head.`),t(`fields`,`Near the Fields`,`Infiltrate Hyrule Castle.`,[`Cut the Field's grass to uncover four switches and use team lifts on logs.`,`Take Dampé's Bracelet through the Swamp.`,`Avoid castle searchlights and carry the Lamp to Jalhalla.`],`Cross formation can activate four nearby targets.`,`Light all four castle torches without entering Jalhalla's beam, slash him, then attack the small enemy inside.`),t(`dark`,`The Dark World`,`Reach the Temple of Darkness.`,[`Use Moon Pearls and the Lamp through the Lost Woods.`,`Investigate Kakariko Village's houses and underground routes.`,`Complete the Temple's linked-world switches and defeat Phantom Ganon.`],`Keep track of which world contains the open passage.`,`Return the real energy volley; do not chase every phantom image.`),t(`desert`,`The Desert of Doubt`,`Uncover the desert's route.`,[`Speak to the Gerudo elder, then the guard to enter.`,`Read the desert clue and travel against the wind through its maze.`,`Complete the Desert Temple and Pyramid.`],`Watch the current wind direction at each maze screen.`,`Attack Big Moldorm's tail with the Link matching its colour, including after it divides.`),t(`frozen`,`Frozen Hyrule`,`Climb the Tower of Winds.`,[`Cross Frozen Hyrule and enter the Ice Temple.`,`Move statues onto switches and use four-Link formations where required.`,`Recover the knight's jewel and ascend the Tower to rescue Zelda.`],`Allow extra stopping distance on ice.`),t(`heavens`,`Realm of the Heavens`,`Confront Vaati.`,[`Cross the Realm of the Heavens into the Dark Cloud.`,`Recover the Dark Mirror and finish the Shadow Link encounters.`,`Enter the Palace of Winds and defeat Vaati.`],`Regroup before using a cannon.`,`Bomb the tornado; later launch above Vaati, down-thrust through his opening, and attack beneath the arena.`),t(`ganon`,`The escape and Ganon`,`Seal the final threat.`,[`Escape the tower alongside Zelda.`,`Dodge Ganon's trident and attack after openings; clear the dark-world enemies when sent there.`,`Protect Zelda as she charges light, then complete the final shot.`],`Use wide formation for sword coverage without standing in the trident's path.`,`Return Ganon's projectiles while Zelda prepares her orb. Fire an arrow through the light orb into Ganon.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Zelda Dungeon · campaign stages`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Near the Fields`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/near-the-fields/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Realm of the Heavens`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/realm-of-the-heavens/`}]},{slug:`the-minish-cap`,title:`The Legend of Zelda: The Minish Cap`,year:2004,platform:`Game Boy Advance`,era:`handheld`,intro:`A cracked wall becomes a doorway and a puddle becomes a lake. Ezlo's gift changes the scale of Hyrule as you restore a broken blade.`,edition:`Original GBA adventure, first released in Japan and Europe in 2004 and North America in 2005.`,scope:`Main-story elements, essential overworld chains and the complete Vaati encounter; optional figurines and most Kinstones are excluded.`,essentials:[`Shrink only at usable portals.`,`Activate Wind Crests as you find them.`,`Use the map to distinguish human and Minish routes.`],chapters:[t(`deepwood`,`The festival and Deepwood Shrine`,`Recover the Earth Element.`,[`After the festival, rescue Ezlo in Minish Woods.`,`Eat the Jabber Nut in the village to understand the Minish.`,`Enter Deepwood Shrine and obtain the Gust Jar.`],`Use suction to move lily pads and clear webs.`,`Suck away Big Green Chuchu's base, dodge its collapse, then slash it.`),t(`flames`,`Mount Crenel and Cave of Flames`,`Recover the Fire Element.`,[`Take a bottle, grow the mountain beans with water and mineral water, and purchase the Grip Ring.`,`Find Melari and leave the broken sword for repair.`,`Enter the Cave and collect the Cane of Pacci.`],`Pacci flips minecarts and charges holes for jumping.`,`Flip Gleerok's shell, climb its neck and strike the exposed crystal.`),t(`wilds`,`The sword and Castor Wilds`,`Reach the Wind Ruins.`,[`Collect Melari's White Sword and infuse two elements at the Sanctuary.`,`Wake Rem with Syrup's Wake-Up Mushroom to receive Pegasus Boots.`,`Dash across the swamp, obtain the Bow and complete the required golden Kinstone fusions.`],`Use sword copies on paired switches.`),t(`fortress`,`Fortress of Winds`,`Find the next lead.`,[`Enter through the Wind Ruins.`,`Take the Mole Mitts and dig through soft barriers.`,`Defeat Mazaal and collect the Ocarina of Wind.`],`The Wind Element is not here; the Ocarina opens fast travel.`,`Shoot the hands' eyes, slash them, then shrink into Mazaal's head and destroy its vulnerable pillar.`),t(`droplets`,`Books and Temple of Droplets`,`Recover the Water Element.`,[`Speak to the Lake Hylia Minish, then return the library's three overdue books.`,`Reach Librari for the Flippers and shrink at the lake to enter the temple.`,`Find the Flame Lantern and melt the dungeon's ice.`],`Retrieve the Power Bracelets during the book quest.`,`Return Big Octorok's rocks; when frozen, ignite its tail with the Lantern.`),t(`clouds`,`Royal Crypt and Cloud Tops`,`Find the Wind Tribe.`,[`Infuse the Water Element, then follow the Royal Valley graveyard route.`,`Complete the Royal Crypt for King Gustaf's golden Kinstone.`,`Fuse at Veil Falls and finish the Cloud Tops' five golden fusions.`],`Explore above and below each cloud layer.`),t(`palace`,`Palace of Winds`,`Claim the Wind Element.`,[`Enter from the Wind Tribe's tower.`,`Obtain Roc's Cape and climb through cloud platforms.`,`Complete the interior switches and reach the Gyorg Pair.`],`The Big Key opens more than one major door.`,`Match copies to the red Gyorg's eyes; on the blue one, strike its eye and jump its sweeping tail.`),t(`castle`,`Dark Hyrule Castle`,`Restore the Four Sword and reach Zelda.`,[`Infuse the final element at the Sanctuary.`,`Use the Four Sword to free petrified people and solve four-copy switches.`,`Climb the castle, obtain the Big Key and defeat the three Darknuts before the final bell.`],`Prepare healing before the timed final ascent.`),t(`vaati`,`Vaati's three forms`,`Break Zelda's curse.`,[`Destroy surrounding eyes, clearing their covering with the Gust Jar, then strike Vaati's central eye.`,`Reveal the next form's vulnerable eye pattern with arrows and match it using copies.`,`After the escape sequence, defeat Vaati's Wrath.`],`Do not mistake the first victory for the ending.`,`Flip each buried arm with Pacci, shrink inside and destroy its distinct eye. Use the Lantern in darkness; finally return four projectiles together with four Links.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Zelda's Palace · Minish Cap route`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/theminishcap/walkthrough.php`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Palace of Winds`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-minish-cap-walkthrough/palace-of-winds/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Dark Hyrule Castle`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-minish-cap-walkthrough/dark-hyrule-castle/`}]},{slug:`a-link-between-worlds`,title:`The Legend of Zelda: A Link Between Worlds`,year:2013,platform:`Nintendo 3DS`,era:`handheld`,intro:`Slip around Hyrule's walls, cross into Lorule and rent the tool that opens your next route.`,edition:`2013 Nintendo 3DS, normal mode.`,scope:`One main-story order. Lorule permits alternatives; Thieves' Hideout unlocks the Sand Rod for Desert Palace.`,essentials:[`Rent the required tool before each dungeon.`,`Rented equipment returns to Ravio after defeat.`,`Watch energy while merged; activate weather vanes.`],chapters:[t(`eastern`,`Eastern Palace`,`Unlock wall merging.`,[`Deliver the sword to the Sanctuary and follow Yuga's trail.`,`Borrow Ravio's Bow and activate Eastern Palace's switches.`,`Defeat Yuga and escape using the bracelet's new power.`],`Merged movement reaches ledges around corners.`,`Stun Yuga with arrows, then use the sword.`),t(`gales`,`House of Gales`,`Earn another pendant.`,[`Recover the Smooth Gem for Queen Oren to obtain Flippers.`,`Rent the Tornado Rod and enter Lake Hylia's dungeon.`,`Use wind devices and the Rod to reach its upper rooms.`],`The Rod lifts vertically; it is not a directional jump.`,`Use Margomill's moving tiers to reach and strike its eye.`),t(`hera`,`Tower of Hera`,`Complete the pendants.`,[`Get Rosso's Power Glove and rent the Hammer.`,`Climb Death Mountain to the tower.`,`Use springy Hammer platforms and wall merging to ascend.`],`A fall may return you to a lower floor.`,`Strike Moldorm's tail, staying away from edges.`),t(`lorule`,`Master Sword and Hyrule Castle`,`Enter Lorule.`,[`Follow the Lost Woods ghosts' instructions to the Master Sword.`,`Break the castle barrier and climb to Yuga.`,`Defeat him, follow the opened passage and meet Hilda.`],`Read each ghost challenge anew.`,`Identify the real Yuga among his wall images and attack when he emerges.`),t(`thieves`,`Thieves' Hideout`,`Free Osfala.`,[`Enter the thieves' town hideout.`,`Free the imprisoned thief and coordinate switches during her escort.`,`Defeat Stalblind; return to Ravio for the available Sand Rod.`],`Keep enemies away from your companion.`,`Merge into Stalblind's shield, then emerge behind him to attack.`),t(`desert`,`Desert Palace`,`Rescue Irene.`,[`Rent the Sand Rod and use world cracks to reach Hyrule's desert.`,`Raise sand columns and collect the Titan's Mitt.`,`Follow the palace route into Lorule for Zaganaga.`],`Sand columns collapse; plan the next jump.`,`Build a route toward Zaganaga and strike between its attacks.`),t(`dark`,`Dark Palace`,`Rescue Gulley.`,[`Rent Bombs and sneak past the palace guards using wall merging.`,`Blast boarded windows to direct light onto sensors.`,`Extinguish torches where darkness reveals hidden paths.`],`Keep the Lantern equipped for the boss.`,`Bomb Gemasaur King's helmet, strike its exposed spot and relight the torches.`),t(`swamp`,`Swamp Palace`,`Rescue Oren.`,[`Pay for the large Bomb Flower and lead it to the entrance boulder.`,`Drain the water and enter with the Hookshot.`,`Adjust water levels to reach the Big Key.`],`Ordinary bombs cannot remove that boulder.`,`Pull Arrghus's small eyes with the Hookshot, destroy them and attack its body.`),t(`skull`,`Skull Woods`,`Rescue Seres.`,[`Drop through forest holes to connect dungeon sections.`,`Use wall merging around gaps and moving platforms.`,`Carry the required eyeballs to their sockets.`],`Watch the shadow of falling hands.`,`Merge when Knucklemaster charges; attack after it hits the wall.`),t(`turtle`,`Turtle Rock`,`Rescue Impa.`,[`Reunite the lake's baby turtles with their mother.`,`Ride to the entrance with the Ice Rod.`,`Freeze lava routes and seesaw platforms.`],`Ice platforms are temporary.`,`Drop ice onto Grinexx through the floor openings, then strike its head when it surfaces.`),t(`ice`,`Ice Ruins`,`Rescue Rosso.`,[`Cross the mountain's world crack with the Fire Rod.`,`Melt the entrance and activate the tongue-operated lift.`,`Follow descending routes, melting ice and moving floor sections.`],`The central lift reconnects explored levels.`,`Melt Dharkstare's ice coat, slash it and avoid its triangular freezing zones.`),t(`finale`,`Lorule Castle`,`Restore both kingdoms.`,[`With seven sages rescued, clear the castle's four trials.`,`Fight Yuga Ganon and return his energy volleys.`,`Use Zelda's Bow of Light during the wall-painting phases.`],`The Bow of Light fires while you are merged.`,`Shoot Yuga from behind; for the final variation, fire around the wall in the opposite direction so the arrow reaches his back.`)],sources:[e,{label:`Zelda's Palace · flexible dungeon route`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/alinkbetweenworlds/walkthrough.php`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Swamp Palace`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/a-link-between-worlds-walkthrough/swamp-palace/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon · Lorule Castle`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/a-link-between-worlds-walkthrough/lorule-castle/`}]}],r=(e,t,n,r,i,a)=>({id:e,title:t,objective:n,steps:r,tip:i,...a?{boss:a}:{}}),i=[{slug:`tri-force-heroes`,title:`Tri Force Heroes`,year:2015,platform:`Nintendo 3DS`,era:`handheld`,intro:`Three heroes share one health bar. Think in heights, positions, and complementary tools.`,edition:`3DS: solo with two Doppels or three local players; no two-player campaign. Official online play ended in April 2024.`,scope:`Eight-region campaign; excludes challenges, costume completion, and Den of Trials.`,essentials:[`A totem's top hero uses items; its bottom hero moves.`,`Switch solo heroes deliberately.`,`Match costumes to stage hazards.`],chapters:[r(`woodlands`,`Woodlands`,`Learn to work at three heights.`,[`Visit Madame Couture, equip an outfit, and enter the castle's adventure lobby.`,`Clear Deku Forest, Buzz Blob Cave, and Moblin Base; raise the Bow hero to hit elevated targets.`,`Enter the Forest Temple and shoot arrows through lit torches to ignite the others.`],`Rearrange the totem when a different item must be on top.`,`Bomb Margoma's opening, throw a hero onto its body, and strike its eye; use taller totems as it grows.`),r(`riverside`,`Riverside`,`Combine water pillars with the Gripshot.`,[`Complete Secret Fortress and Abyss of Agony using the Water Rod to raise temporary stepping stones.`,`Cross Cove of Transition by moving heroes to separate switches before reuniting them.`,`Enter the Water Temple; Gripshot teammates and targets across gaps.`],`Allow water pillars to settle before moving a full totem.`,`Pull Arrghus's small eyes with the Gripshot and slash; later put the Gripshot hero atop a full totem to stun its main eye.`),r(`volcano`,`Volcano`,`Cross moving platforms and minecart tracks.`,[`Use the Gust Jar to send heroes across gaps and the Boomerang to retrieve the remaining teammate.`,`Time switches from minecarts and return the Hinox riders' bombs.`,`Reach the Fire Temple and coordinate the three timed crystal switches.`],`Separate heroes before handling bombs near a crowded cart.`,`Attack Moldorm's tail; as it rises, stack two and then three heroes with the Bow on top.`),r(`ice`,`Ice Cavern`,`Control slippery terrain.`,[`Use Fire Gloves in Frozen Plateau and Snowball Ravine to melt obstacles and light torches.`,`Clear Silver Shrine, then bring every hero across the Ice Temple's moving platforms.`,`Use hammers on launch pegs, timing the landing before activating them.`],`Cozy Parka helps with slippery ground.`,`Hammer Blizzagia's head until its mask breaks, then damage the exposed gem while avoiding its tail.`),r(`fortress`,`Fortress`,`Reach the Lady's lair.`,[`Operate lifts with a hero left beside their switch.`,`In Bomb Storage, blow bombs back at the Hinox Brothers.`,`Enter the Lady's Lair and solve its stacked platform puzzles.`],`Bring everyone to the exit.`,`The Lady's Pets revisit earlier bosses: bomb Margoma's opening, reach Moldorm's tail, then clear Arrghus's elemental eyes and stun its jewel.`),r(`dunes`,`The Dunes`,`Retrieve another part of the Lady's outfit.`,[`Cross Infinity Dunes with Water Rod pillars and hammer-operated tilting platforms.`,`Clear Stone Corridors and Gibdo Mausoleum; burn Gibdo wrappings before attacking.`,`Reach the Desert Temple and position heroes on different sides of the arena.`],`Leave one hero as a counterweight when balancing a platform.`,`Strike Stalchampion from behind, hammer its exposed heart, then use a tall Boomerang totem against its final head.`),r(`ruins`,`The Ruins`,`Read colors in the dark.`,[`Clear Illusory Mansion and relight Palace Noir's torches to reveal its ghostly threats.`,`Navigate Lone Labyrinth using the paths belonging to each hero's color.`,`Reach Grim Temple, light its rooms, and free any hero caught by a ReDead.`],`Color-matched platforms require the appropriate hero, even when the destination looks close.`,`Have each hero hit Prismantus's matching orb; throw a hero onto it to strike the eye once all three go dark.`),r(`sky`,`Sky Realm and Lady Maud`,`Break Princess Styla's curse.`,[`Finish Floating Garden, Deception Castle, and Dragon Citadel before the Sky Temple gauntlet.`,`Reach Maud with health restored; she removes your items, so use totems and swords.`,`Collect the final outfit material and return to Hytopia to complete the rescue.`],`Stay spread out when a colored lightning marker singles out one hero.`,`Throw heroes over Maud's barrier and attack behind her; return her energy ball, then climb matching-color parasols to reach her head.`)],sources:[{label:`Nintendo — online-service discontinuation`,url:`https://en-americas-support.nintendo.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/63227/p/603/c/950`},{label:`Zelda's Palace — eight-region walkthrough`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/walkthrough.php`},{label:`Prima — boss strategies`,url:`https://primagames.com/tips/legend-zelda-triforce-heroes-boss-guide`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Sky Realm`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/tri-force-heroes-walkthrough/sky-realm/`}]},{slug:`breath-of-the-wild`,title:`Breath of the Wild`,year:2017,platform:`Nintendo Wii U / Nintendo Switch`,era:`modern`,intro:`Build confidence on the plateau, help Hyrule's four peoples, then approach the castle prepared.`,edition:`Original base-game campaign. This route does not require DLC, glitches, or amiibo rewards; Master Mode changes combat pressure.`,scope:`A suggested four-Divine-Beast story route. These objectives can be reordered, and the game allows an earlier castle attempt. This is not a shrine or Korok completion guide.`,essentials:[`Cook ingredients together for healing and a useful effect; mixed effects can cancel.`,`Upgrade armor at Great Fairy fountains.`,`Cold, desert heat, and volcanic fire require different protection.`],chapters:[r(`plateau`,`The Great Plateau`,`Earn the Paraglider.`,[`Take the Sheikah Slate, activate the tower, and complete the Magnesis and Remote Bomb shrines.`,`Prepare cold protection before climbing to the Stasis and Cryonis shrines.`,`Trade four Spirit Orbs at the Temple of Time statue and meet the old man above.`],`A cooked spicy meal provides temporary cold resistance; watch its timer.`),r(`villages`,`Kakariko and Hateno`,`Recover Link's direction and memories.`,[`Travel past Dueling Peaks to Kakariko and speak with Impa.`,`Visit Purah at Hateno's Ancient Tech Lab; carry the blue flame to its furnace.`,`Photograph a subject with the restored Camera, return to Impa, and begin the photographed-memory search.`],`Shrines double as travel points even before every puzzle is finished.`),r(`ruta`,`Zora's Domain and Vah Ruta`,`Help Sidon calm the reservoir.`,[`Follow the road to Zora's Domain and receive the Zora Armor.`,`Collect twenty Shock Arrows around Ploymus Mountain; sneaking past the Lynel is enough.`,`Ride with Sidon, break incoming ice, enter Ruta, and use its trunk positions to reach the terminals.`],`Cryonis destroys the incoming ice blocks without spending arrows.`,`Avoid Waterblight's spear in phase one; break its ice attacks and shoot its eye when platforms shrink.`),r(`medoh`,`Rito Village and Vah Medoh`,`Reclaim the sky.`,[`Equip sufficient cold protection and meet Teba at the Flight Range.`,`Use aerial slow-motion aiming to pass his test and destroy Medoh's cannons.`,`Take the dungeon map, tilt the beast, and redirect wind to reach all terminals.`],`Release the bow between shots to save stamina while airborne.`,`Use updrafts for clear shots at Windblight's eye, then attack when it falls.`),r(`rudania`,`Goron City and Vah Rudania`,`Climb Death Mountain safely.`,[`Obtain fireproof protection before approaching Goron City.`,`Rescue Yunobo and escort him up the mountain, avoiding sentry searchlights.`,`Use the cannons to enter Rudania; rotate its body and transport blue flame to open passages.`],`Ordinary heat-resistant meals do not stop volcanic ignition.`,`Damage Fireblight at close range; throw a Remote Bomb into its vacuum attack to break the fiery shield.`),r(`naboris`,`Gerudo Town and Vah Naboris`,`Return the Thunder Helm.`,[`Acquire the Gerudo disguise at Kara Kara Bazaar and meet Riju.`,`Infiltrate the Yiga hideout, use bananas to distract guards, and defeat Master Kohga.`,`Ride within Riju's protective circle to attack Naboris; rotate its cylinders and connect electrical circuits.`],`Rain and electricity make equipped metal especially dangerous.`,`Block Thunderblight's rushes; during the metal-pillar phase, lift a pillar beside it with Magnesis to redirect lightning.`),r(`preparation`,`Memories and the forest sword`,`Choose your preparations before the finale.`,[`Use the Camera album and Pikango's location hints to recover memories.`,`Follow the Lost Woods' wind clues to Korok Forest; obtain thirteen permanent hearts if you want to draw the Master Sword.`,`Upgrade armor, collect strong weapons and shields, and cook healing meals.`],`The Master Sword and memories enrich this route but are not prerequisites for entering the castle.`),r(`ganon`,`Hyrule Castle`,`End the Calamity.`,[`Enter by a route suited to your equipment, including the docks or surrounding cliffs.`,`Reach the Sanctum; any undefeated Blights must be fought before Calamity Ganon.`,`After Calamity Ganon, take the Bow of Light for the mounted finale.`],`Freed Divine Beasts weaken Calamity Ganon before your duel.`,`Use precise dodges, parries, or Urbosa's Fury to breach the guarded phase. Shoot Dark Beast Ganon's marked weak points, then use an updraft for the final eye.`)],sources:[{label:`Nintendo — Explorer's Guide`,url:`https://media.nintendo.com/zelda/breath-of-the-wild/assets/ExplorersGuide.pdf`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — campaign walkthrough`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/breath-of-the-wild-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Hyrule Castle`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/breath-of-the-wild-walkthrough/hyrule-castle/`},{label:`Zelda Universe — Destroy Ganon`,url:`https://zeldauniverse.net/guides/breath-of-the-wild/walkthrough/chapter-15-destroy-ganon/`}]},{slug:`tears-of-the-kingdom`,title:`Tears of the Kingdom`,year:2023,platform:`Nintendo Switch`,era:`modern`,intro:`Connect sky, surface, and Depths with improvised machines and five allies.`,edition:`Switch campaign using standard abilities, without glitches or version-dependent shortcuts.`,scope:`Suggested main-story route. Exploration order is flexible; shrines and caves are not exhaustively covered.`,essentials:[`Fuse weapons to strengthen them.`,`Bring Brightblooms for darkness and Sundelion meals for gloom-damaged hearts.`,`Activate travel points.`],chapters:[r(`sky-island`,`Great Sky Island`,`Open the Temple of Time.`,[`Complete the three shrines teaching Ultrahand, Fuse, and Ascend.`,`Return to the Temple of Time for Recall, then finish the fourth shrine.`,`Exchange four blessings for a heart, open the door, and descend to Hyrule.`],`Cook spicy food before entering the island's snowy area.`),r(`landing`,`Lookout Landing`,`Obtain the Paraglider.`,[`Meet Purah, then Hoz by Hyrule Castle's First Gatehouse.`,`Report back; activate Lookout Landing's tower.`,`Accept Regional Phenomena; consider Robbie's Depths expedition for the Camera.`],`The shelter provides a free bed and cooking pot.`),r(`wind`,`Tulin and the Wind Temple`,`Reach the storm above Hebra.`,[`Visit Rito Village, find Tulin, and recover his stolen bow.`,`Use his gusts and the rising chain of sky islands to reach the storm's center.`,`Open five turbine locks using Tulin's wind.`],`Bring two levels of cold resistance for the highest areas.`,`Break Colgera's icy undersides by diving through exposed plates or shooting from below; dodge the tornadoes.`),r(`fire`,`Yunobo and the Fire Temple`,`Trace the marbled rock roast.`,[`Break Yunobo's mask at YunoboCo and accompany him up Death Mountain.`,`Defeat the crater threat, descend the chasm, and follow the statues toward the temple.`,`Route the minecarts and launch Yunobo into five gongs.`],`Use flame protection inside burning caves and the temple.`,`Roll Yunobo through Marbled Gohma's legs, climb to its eye, and use wall ramps when it moves overhead.`),r(`water`,`Sidon and the Water Temple`,`Remove the sludge.`,[`Help Yona restore the Zora Armor; investigate Toto's slate.`,`Find Dorephan; shoot a King's Scale through the floating fish island's stone droplet.`,`Drain the Ancient Zora Waterworks, climb Wellspring Island, and open four faucets with Sidon.`],`Splash Fruit also clears sludge.`,`Wash away Mucktorok's shark form, then attack the exposed creature.`),r(`lightning`,`Riju and the Lightning Temple`,`End the sand shroud.`,[`Find Riju in the ruins and help defend Kara Kara Bazaar and Gerudo Town.`,`Use the mural's pillar clues to reveal the Lightning Temple.`,`Align mirrors and charge four batteries with Riju's lightning.`],`Elemental attacks make Gibdos vulnerable to ordinary weapons.`,`Strike Queen Gibdo with lightning, then attack; destroy glowing nests when their protective covering opens.`),r(`castle`,`A false princess`,`Resolve the castle sightings.`,[`Report all four regional successes to Purah.`,`Follow Zelda's appearances through the floating castle, defeating each ambush.`,`Confront Phantom Ganon and return to Lookout Landing for the fifth-sage investigation.`],`Keep space between yourself and grouped enemies rather than trading hits inside gloom.`),r(`spirit`,`The fifth sage`,`Build Mineru's body.`,[`Investigate Kakariko's Ring Ruins; follow Tauro to Dracozu and complete the Charged Armor ritual.`,`Reach Dragonhead Island with ten hearts; carry Mineru's mask along its beam into the Depths.`,`Bring four depot limbs to the Construct Factory; ride Mineru to the Spirit Temple.`],`Clearing Thunderhead's storm makes navigation easier.`,`Block the Seized Construct, stagger it, and knock it into the electrified ropes.`),r(`sword`,`Recover the hero's sword`,`Prepare for the final descent.`,[`Follow the Master Sword quest; helping the Great Deku Tree provides the moving location marker.`,`Reach the Light Dragon and draw the sword with two complete permanent stamina wheels.`,`Gather strong fused weapons, shields, arrows, healing, and gloom-recovery meals.`],`Geoglyph memories reveal major story answers; their viewing order affects when you learn them.`),r(`ganondorf`,`Beneath Hyrule Castle`,`Defeat Ganondorf.`,[`Descend Hyrule Castle Chasm to the army battle.`,`Fight the Demon King after the sages handle their corresponding threats.`,`In the airborne finale, use the Light Dragon to reach the enemy's vulnerable growths.`],`Cook before descending; gloom removes usable hearts.`,`Dodge Ganondorf's counters after he evades your strike. Destroy the Demon Dragon's back growths, then strike its head's stone.`)],sources:[{label:`Zelda Dungeon — main walkthrough index`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/wiki/Walkthrough%3ATears_of_the_Kingdom`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Regional Phenomena`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/wiki/Regional_Phenomena`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Guidance from Ages Past`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/wiki/Guidance_from_Ages_Past`},{label:`Zelda Wiki — Destroy Ganondorf`,url:`https://zeldawiki.wiki/wiki/Destroy_Ganondorf`}]},{slug:`echoes-of-wisdom`,title:`Echoes of Wisdom`,year:2024,platform:`Nintendo Switch`,era:`modern`,intro:`Save Hyrule as Zelda, remembering useful things and moving the world with Tri.`,edition:`Switch campaign using echoes, Bind, and Swordfighter Form. Other solutions often work.`,scope:`Every story dungeon through the finale; not an all-collectibles guide.`,essentials:[`Learn useful echoes immediately.`,`Heal with beds; prepare smoothies.`,`Bind moves targets; Follow lets them carry Zelda.`],chapters:[r(`suthorn`,`Escape and Suthorn Ruins`,`Learn what Tri can do.`,[`Escape the castle with the Tri Rod, copying tables and beds to pass the guards.`,`Travel through Suthorn Forest, enter its rift, and rescue Tri's trapped friends.`,`Defeat Link's echo in Suthorn Ruins to obtain Swordfighter Form; use Bind on large obstacles.`],`Let combat echoes occupy enemies while you move to safety.`,`Pull Seismic Talus's glowing orb out with Bind, then attack it while exposed.`),r(`gerudo`,`Gerudo Desert`,`Earn access to the sanctum.`,[`Meet Dohna and help the Gerudo resolve the smaller desert rifts.`,`Enter the Cryptic Cavern and lower the sand blocking the sanctum route.`,`Learn the dungeon's statue echoes, use Holmill on diggable ground, and defeat Link's echo for the Bow.`],`Read the statue clues before placing copies.`,`Make Mogryph collide with a statue during a charge; after it falls, attack before it takes flight again.`),r(`jabul`,`Jabul Waters`,`Reunite the Zora communities.`,[`Help Dradd and Kushara reopen Jabu-Jabu's den.`,`Defeat its impostor; cross the rift into Jabul Ruins.`,`Activate five colored switches to raise the central water column.`],`Water Blocks provide climbing and swimming routes.`,`Avoid Vocavor's whirlpools, break its back growths, and attack while it collapses.`),r(`castle`,`Hyrule Castle's rift`,`Rescue the king.`,[`Return to Hyrule Castle Town after both regional quests.`,`Enter the castle rift, avoid the guards, and use echoes to operate its switches and torches.`,`Collect the boss key and confront the Ganon echo.`],`Save Swordfighter energy for a clear opening instead of leaving the form active.`,`Evade spear attacks and fire bats; return the energy ball with sword timing or let strong echoes attack during recoveries.`),r(`eldin`,`Eldin Volcano`,`Receive Din's Sanction.`,[`Help Darston and the Gorons along the volcano route.`,`Cross the lava safely using appropriate echoes and enter Eldin Temple.`,`Defeat Link's bomb-using echo, then clear cracked barriers and climb the temple.`],`Keep a flying echo available for lava crossings.`,`Use Bind to pull Volvagia's green necklace and create an opening; move away before the next eruption.`),r(`faron`,`Faron Wetlands`,`Receive Farore's Sanction.`,[`Investigate the Deku Scrubs' cotton-candy problem and escape their prison.`,`Enter the Faron rift and temple, learning electric echoes along the way.`,`Coordinate electrical switches and find the boss key.`],`Keep electric attacks away from water you are standing in.`,`Electrify Gohma's leg crystals to knock it down; then attack the exposed eye.`),r(`lanayru`,`Hebra and Lanayru Temple`,`Receive Nayru's Sanction.`,[`Climb Hebra Mountain with Condé's guidance and prepare cold resistance.`,`Enter Lanayru Temple and carry its temperature orbs with Bind.`,`Change rooms between frozen and thawed states, blocking air vents when an orb must keep its temperature.`],`A warmed room can hide a key underwater that was inaccessible beneath ice.`,`Use fire against Skorchill's icy helmet and ice against its fiery helmet; attack its body after the armor breaks.`),r(`forest`,`The Eternal Forest`,`Find Link.`,[`After all three sanctions, follow the lead into the Eternal Forest.`,`Learn the Ancient Orb echo; fill the six triangularly arranged pedestals.`,`Cross the Stilled Ancient Ruins, defeat Zelda's echo, and free Link.`],`Prepare before returning Link's weapons; Zelda then loses Swordfighter Form.`),r(`null`,`Null's Body`,`Fight alongside Link.`,[`Return the weapons to Link and enter Null's body together.`,`Use Bind and traversal echoes to help Link cross obstacles while he handles direct sword attacks.`,`Follow the separated and underwater passages, then reunite for the final battle.`],`Keep replacing combat echoes when they disappear; Zelda's role remains active throughout.`,`Pull Null's arms with Bind so Link can sever them, defeat summoned enemies, and join Tri in removing the final core.`)],sources:[{label:`Nintendo — ten practical tips`,url:`https://www.nintendo.com/en-gb/News/2024/October/10-tips-to-help-save-Hyrule-in-The-Legend-of-Zelda-Echoes-of-Wisdom-2668982.html`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — story walkthrough index`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/echoes-of-wisdom-walkthrough-guide/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Eternal Forest`,url:`https://zeldadungeon.net/wiki/Walkthrough%3AEternal_Forest_%28Echoes_of_Wisdom%29`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Null's Body`,url:`https://zeldadungeon.net/wiki/Walkthrough%3ANull%27s_Body_%28Echoes_of_Wisdom%29`}]},{slug:`ocarina-of-time`,title:`Ocarina of Time`,year:1998,platform:`Nintendo 64`,era:`3d`,intro:`A forest child, a vanished princess, and a kingdom separated by seven years. Follow the original adventure from Kokiri Forest to Ganon.`,edition:`Original Nintendo 64 quest. The linked detailed walkthrough also follows this version; Master Quest layouts and 3DS changes are outside its scope.`,scope:`Six orientation chapters, with our complete 14-chapter main-story walkthrough one click away. Optional collections are separate.`,essentials:[`A bottle gives you space for fairies, fish, or Blue Fire.`,`Keep the ocarina accessible: songs open routes as well as tell the story.`,`Dungeon maps show different floors; compare them before spending a Small Key.`],existingGuide:`/zelda-64`,chapters:[r(`forest-child`,`The child of the forest`,`Earn the Kokiri Emerald.`,[`Find the Kokiri Sword through the Training Center crawlspace; buy the Deku Shield.`,`Show both to Mido, meet the Deku Tree, and enter its trunk.`,`Collect the Slingshot, break the central web from above, and reach the basement.`],`Deku Sticks carry flame between torches and burn webs.`,`Stun Gohma's red eye with the Slingshot, then close in with the sword.`),r(`two-stones`,`Zelda and the remaining stones`,`Open the way to the Temple of Time.`,[`Meet Zelda at Hyrule Castle; learn Zelda's Lullaby from Impa.`,`Learn Saria's Song, cheer up Darunia, and clear Dodongo's Cavern for the Bomb Bag and Goron Ruby.`,`Find Ruto's letter, move King Zora, and offer a bottled fish to Jabu-Jabu. Carry Ruto and use the Boomerang to finish the dungeon.`],`The letter is underwater in Lake Hylia; the Silver Scale helps you reach it.`,`Bomb King Dodongo's open mouth. Against Barinade, sever its ceiling connections and clear the jellyfish with the Boomerang.`),r(`adult-link`,`Seven years later`,`Awaken the forest and fire sages.`,[`Retrieve the Ocarina of Time from the castle moat, play the Song of Time, and draw the Master Sword.`,`Race Dampé's ghost in Kakariko Graveyard for the Hookshot; return to the Sacred Forest Meadow.`,`Clear the Forest Temple for the Bow, then visit Goron City and rescue the Fire Temple prisoners to obtain the Megaton Hammer.`],`Completing the Forest Temple unlocks returning to childhood through the Master Sword.`,`Return Phantom Ganon's energy shots with sword swings. Hammer Volvagia when its real head emerges.`),r(`water-and-shadow`,`Water and shadow`,`Restore Lake Hylia and enter the royal tomb.`,[`Bring bottled Blue Fire from the Ice Cavern to King Zora; equip the Iron Boots and Zora Tunic.`,`Clear the Water Temple, tracking the three water levels and collecting the Longshot.`,`Learn the Song of Storms as an adult, drain Kakariko's well as a child for the Lens of Truth, then learn the Nocturne of Shadow and enter the Shadow Temple.`],`Watch the space under the central Water Temple platform when it rises.`,`Pull Morpha's nucleus with the Longshot. Use the Lens to see Bongo Bongo, stun both hands, then its eye.`),r(`spirit`,`Across the desert`,`Awaken the final sage.`,[`Rescue the four carpenters in Gerudo's Fortress to earn free passage.`,`Cross the Haunted Wasteland and follow the ghost with the Lens of Truth; learn the Requiem of Spirit.`,`Complete the child side of the Spirit Temple for Silver Gauntlets, then return as an adult for the Mirror Shield.`],`The Spirit Temple intentionally requires both ages; do not try to force the child crawlspace as an adult.`,`Reflect each Twinrova witch's beam at the other; after they merge, absorb three matching attacks before releasing the shield's charge.`),r(`finale`,`The last climb`,`Rescue Zelda and defeat Ganon.`,[`Return to the Temple of Time for the Light Arrows and cross the sages' bridge.`,`Dispel the six barriers in Ganon's Castle, obtaining the Golden Gauntlets along the way.`,`Climb the tower, defeat Ganondorf, and follow Zelda out before the collapse.`],`Refill magic, arrows, and bottles before entering the final tower.`,`Volley Ganondorf's spell, stun him with a Light Arrow, and attack. In the final arena, circle Ganon to strike his tail; reclaim the Master Sword and use it for the finish.`)],sources:[{label:`Zelda Dungeon — original quest walkthrough`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/ocarina-of-time-walkthrough/`},{label:`Thonky — Inside the Deku Tree`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/inside-deku-tree`},{label:`Zelda's Palace — Ocarina walkthrough`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/ocarinaoftime/soluce.php?p=1`}]},{slug:`majoras-mask`,title:`Majora's Mask`,year:2e3,platform:`Nintendo 64`,era:`3d`,intro:`Carry discoveries across time and give four troubled regions another dawn.`,edition:`N64 route. The 3DS remake changes saving, swimming, and bosses; these strategies follow the original.`,scope:`Four temples and the Moon; excludes mask and fairy completion.`,essentials:[`Bank rupees before resetting time.`,`Play the Song of Time backward to slow time.`,`Reset before temples when needed; songs and permanent equipment remain.`],chapters:[r(`first-cycle`,`The first three days`,`Recover the ocarina.`,[`Return Clock Town's Stray Fairy, catch the Bombers, and use their code to enter the observatory.`,`Collect the Moon's Tear and trade it for the Business Scrub's flower.`,`Reach the Clock Tower roof after midnight on the final night; hit Skull Kid and play the Song of Time.`],`After resetting, visit the Happy Mask Salesman to learn the Song of Healing.`),r(`woodfall`,`Southern Swamp and Woodfall`,`Free the first giant.`,[`Bring Koume a red potion, take the boat, and enter Deku Palace as a Deku.`,`Use a watered Magic Bean to reach the captive monkey and learn the Sonata of Awakening.`,`Raise Woodfall Temple, collect the Bow, and light its required torches.`],`Activate owl statues as you travel for later Song of Soaring warps.`,`Stun Odolwa with arrows when his guard opens, then attack with the sword.`),r(`snowhead`,`The mountain in winter`,`Restore spring.`,[`Use the Lens of Truth to follow Darmani; heal his spirit for the Goron Mask.`,`Learn the Goron Lullaby's beginning from the elder and complete it with his child.`,`Put Snowhead's guardian to sleep, enter the temple, and obtain Fire Arrows.`],`Manage the central pillar from the dungeon map rather than repeatedly circling one floor.`,`As Goron Link, chase Goht with spiked rolls; collect magic jars along the track.`),r(`ranch-and-coast`,`A horse and seven eggs`,`Open Great Bay Temple.`,[`Earn the Powder Keg license, clear the ranch boulder early in a cycle, and learn Epona's Song from Romani.`,`Jump the coastal barriers, heal Mikau for the Zora Mask, and raid the Pirates' Fortress for the Hookshot and four eggs.`,`Rescue the seahorse, find three more eggs at Pinnacle Rock, and deliver all seven to the laboratory.`],`The hatched eggs teach New Wave Bossa Nova; play it to Lulu as a Zora.`),r(`great-bay`,`Great Bay's machinery`,`Restore the ocean's current.`,[`Hookshot onto the awakened turtle to enter the temple.`,`Follow the colored pipes and obtain Ice Arrows.`,`Freeze water and enemies to reach valves; reverse the central current when the route requires it.`],`A bottle of magic recovery helps with prolonged Zora combat.`,`Stun Gyorg from the platform with an arrow, dive to attack with Zora's electric barrier, then retreat.`),r(`ikana`,`The voices of Ikana`,`Learn the Elegy of Emptiness.`,[`Win Garo's Mask at the Gorman race; obtain the Captain's Hat and learn the Song of Storms beneath the first-night grave.`,`Reach Ikana Canyon, restore the river with the Song of Storms, and heal Pamela's father for the Gibdo Mask.`,`Trade requested supplies beneath the well for the Mirror Shield; enter Ikana Castle and defeat its king.`],`Carry bottles and check each Gibdo's request before giving away supplies.`),r(`stone-tower`,`The inverted tower`,`Free the fourth giant.`,[`Use Elegy statues of different forms to hold Stone Tower's switches.`,`Enter its temple, defeat the Garo Master, and collect Light Arrows.`,`Strike the outside red emblem with a Light Arrow to invert the temple; find the Giant's Mask and boss key.`],`Refill magic before Twinmold; the Giant's Mask drains it.`,`Wear the Giant's Mask and strike Twinmold's vulnerable heads or tails with your sword.`),r(`moon`,`The final night`,`Stop the falling Moon.`,[`Return to the Clock Tower at midnight with all four boss remains.`,`Play the Oath to Order; on the Moon, approach the child under the tree when ready.`,`Complete the three-part battle and watch the new dawn.`],`The Moon's optional mask trials are not required to finish.`,`Attack Majora's Mask from behind, stun Incarnation with arrows, and punish Wrath after a stun while avoiding its whips.`)],sources:[{label:`Zelda Dungeon — first three days`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/majoras-mask-walkthrough/first-three-days/`},{label:`Zelda Universe — Ikana Canyon`,url:`https://zeldauniverse.net/guides/majoras-mask/walkthrough/ikana-canyon/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Stone Tower Temple`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/majoras-mask-walkthrough/stone-tower-temple/`},{label:`GameFAQs — Nintendo 64 walkthrough`,url:`https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/n64/197770-the-legend-of-zelda-majoras-mask/faqs/71155`}]},{slug:`the-wind-waker`,title:`The Wind Waker`,year:2002,platform:`Nintendo GameCube`,era:`3d`,intro:`Rescue Aryll, awaken two sages, and follow Hyrule's history beneath the waves.`,edition:`GameCube, first released in Japan in 2002. Original: eight Triforce charts. Wii U HD: three charts and five direct shards.`,scope:`Main story; excludes island and collection completion.`,essentials:[`Set wind before sailing or gliding.`,`Feed Fishmen to map islands.`,`Upgrade your wallet for chart fees.`],chapters:[r(`outset`,`Outset and the Forsaken Fortress`,`Attempt Aryll's rescue.`,[`Train with Orca, rescue Tetra, and take your family's shield.`,`Sail with the pirates and infiltrate the fortress.`,`Disable searchlights, recover your sword, and climb toward Aryll.`],`Barrels conceal Link only while still.`),r(`dragon-roost`,`The first pearl`,`Help the Rito on Dragon Roost.`,[`Buy the sail on Windfall and follow the King of Red Lions.`,`Receive the Wind Waker, learn the Wind's Requiem, and help Medli reach the cavern.`,`Collect the Grappling Hook and climb through Dragon Roost Cavern.`],`Swing the Grappling Hook before releasing toward a safe landing.`,`Grapple Valoo's hanging tail to break Gohma's armor, then pull its eye and slash.`),r(`forest`,`Forbidden Woods`,`Rescue Makar for Farore's Pearl.`,[`Reach Forest Haven and remove the ChuChus from the Deku Tree.`,`Obtain the Deku Leaf; align the wind and use the updraft to reach Forbidden Woods.`,`Collect the Boomerang and sever hanging vines to lower platforms.`],`Cut grass for magic before long flights.`,`Target Kalle Demos's ceiling vines with the Boomerang, then attack its exposed center.`),r(`gods`,`Three pearls and a sunken kingdom`,`Draw the Master Sword.`,[`Visit ruined Greatfish Isle, then obtain bombs from the pirates on Windfall.`,`Return to Outset and blast Jabun's sealed entrance for Nayru's Pearl.`,`Place the pearls on the three Triangle Islands; clear the Tower of the Gods using the Bow and Command Melody.`],`After the tower, solve Hyrule Castle's Triforce block puzzle.`,`Shoot Gohdan's hands and eyes, then throw a bomb into its open mouth.`),r(`fortress-return`,`Return to the fortress`,`Rescue Aryll and discover the sword's weakness.`,[`Sail back to the Forsaken Fortress and defeat Phantom Ganon.`,`Obtain the Skull Hammer and climb the flooded tower.`,`Defeat the Helmaroc King and follow the story back to Hyrule.`],`Smash barred switches with the Skull Hammer.`,`When the bird's beak sticks in the floor, hammer its mask; slash after the armor breaks.`),r(`earth`,`The Earth Sage`,`Restore the first half of the sword's power.`,[`Defeat Cyclos for the Ballad of Gales; warp inside Mother and Child Isles for elemental arrows.`,`Use Ice Arrows on Fire Mountain for Power Bracelets, then learn the Earth God's Lyric at Headstone Island.`,`Bring Medli to the Earth Temple; control her harp's reflections and obtain the Mirror Shield.`],`Keep Medli near doors that require both characters.`,`Shine light on Jalhalla, lift and throw him into spikes, then defeat the scattered Poes.`),r(`wind`,`The Wind Sage`,`Finish restoring the Master Sword.`,[`Use Fire Arrows at Ice Ring Isle for the Iron Boots.`,`Learn the Wind God's Aria at Gale Isle and find Makar behind Forest Haven's waterfall.`,`Bring Makar into the Wind Temple; obtain the Hookshot and grow trees for grapple points.`],`Iron Boots hold down spring mechanisms and resist strong wind.`,`Hookshot Molgera's tongue from outside the sand pit, then slash it.`),r(`triforce`,`Eight pieces of courage`,`Reopen the route to Hyrule.`,[`Follow the IN-credible Chart to Triforce-chart locations in the GameCube quest.`,`Have Tingle decipher each chart; sail to its marked position and salvage the shard.`,`Assemble all eight pieces and return to the Tower of the Gods.`],`HD replaces five of these chart-and-salvage chains with direct shard rewards.`),r(`ganon`,`Ganon's Tower`,`Bring the ocean journey to its conclusion.`,[`Clear the four dungeon rematches and navigate the Phantom Ganon maze.`,`Use Light Arrows against Puppet Ganon's glowing tail across its three forms.`,`Climb to Ganondorf and fight alongside Zelda.`],`Replenish arrows and magic before the Puppet Ganon arena.`,`Let Zelda's Light Arrows create openings; later reflect her shot with your shield and use the prompted parry.`)],sources:[{label:`Zelda Dungeon — chapter walkthrough`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-wind-waker-walkthrough/`},{label:`Piggyback — official guide sample`,url:`https://www.piggyback.com/en/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2020/04/ZLD_E_SamplePages.pdf`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Triforce quest`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-wind-waker-walkthrough/the-triforce/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — HD Triforce changes`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/the-wind-waker-hd-triforce-quest-changes-detailed/`}]},{slug:`twilight-princess`,title:`Twilight Princess`,year:2006,platform:`Nintendo GameCube / Wii`,era:`3d`,intro:`Follow Midna between light and twilight as swordsman and wolf.`,edition:`GameCube/Wii campaign; Wii is mirrored, so directions use landmarks. HD changes some collection requirements.`,scope:`Nine-dungeon main story; optional collections excluded.`,essentials:[`Use wolf senses to track scents.`,`Defeat the last two Shadow Beasts together.`,`Restock bottles and bombs in settlements.`],chapters:[r(`ordon`,`Ordon to the forest`,`Restore Faron's light.`,[`Complete Ordon's errands, obtain the sword and shield, and follow the kidnapped children.`,`Escape Hyrule Castle as a wolf with Midna.`,`Collect Faron's Tears of Light, regain human form, and enter the Forest Temple.`],`Track marked insects with wolf senses.`,`Rescue the monkeys, obtain the Gale Boomerang, and use it to carry Bombling explosions into Diababa's mouths.`),r(`gorons`,`Kakariko and the Gorons`,`Rescue the children and enter the mines.`,[`Restore Eldin's light and defend Kakariko.`,`Return to Bo for sumo training and the Iron Boots.`,`Challenge the Gorons, enter their mines, and collect the Hero's Bow and key shards.`],`Equip the boots on magnetic surfaces and when resisting a Goron's charge.`,`Shoot Fyrus's forehead, grab a chain while wearing Iron Boots, and pull him down.`),r(`lakebed`,`Beneath the lake`,`Recover the last Fused Shadow.`,[`Thaw Zora's Domain with Midna's warp; restore Lanayru's light.`,`Escort the carriage to Kakariko; follow Rutela for Zora Armor.`,`Buy Water Bombs, enter Lakebed, and redirect water with its staircase.`],`Collect the Clawshot for distant targets.`,`Clawshot Morpheel's tentacle eye; afterward swim above its back and grapple the eye.`),r(`master-sword`,`The Sacred Grove`,`Break the wolf curse.`,[`Carry the injured Midna to Zelda through the castle passage.`,`Return to Faron and follow the Skull Kid through the Sacred Grove.`,`Solve the guardian-statue puzzle and draw the Master Sword.`],`You can now change forms through Midna outside others' sight.`),r(`arbiter`,`The desert prison`,`Find the Mirror of Twilight.`,[`Meet Auru through Telma's group; take Fyer's cannon to Gerudo Desert.`,`Cross the Bulblin camp into Arbiter's Grounds.`,`Track four Poes and obtain the Spinner for wall rails.`],`Use wolf senses to reveal hidden threats.`,`Spin into Stallord's spine; during the tower phase, leap between rails and strike its head.`),r(`snowpeak`,`Snowpeak Ruins`,`Recover a mirror shard.`,[`Show Ashei's sketch to Ralis; use his earring to catch a Reekfish.`,`Follow its scent as a wolf to Yeto.`,`Collect the Ball and Chain; move cannonballs to blast the mansion's ice barriers.`],`Yeto's soup refills bottles.`,`Break Blizzeta's ice with the Ball and Chain; watch reflections to dodge falling ice.`),r(`time`,`Temple of Time`,`Return a statue to its place.`,[`Meet Rusl in Faron and revisit the Sacred Grove.`,`Open the time door and enter the temple behind the Master Sword pedestal.`,`Obtain the Dominion Rod; escort the large statue downstairs using switches and scales.`],`Smash obstructions with the controlled statue.`,`Shoot Armogohma's open eye, then command a nearby statue to crush it.`),r(`sky`,`The city above`,`Find the last shard.`,[`Follow Renado, Telma, and Hidden Village leads to restore Ilia's memory.`,`Take the Ancient Sky Book to Shad; recharge the rod, collect sky characters, and reveal the cannon.`,`Have Fyer repair it; enter the sky city and obtain Double Clawshots.`],`Chain targets without dropping.`,`Pull Argorok down with Iron Boots; climb the targets and reach its back's weak point.`),r(`twilight`,`The Palace of Twilight`,`Reunite the mirror and face Zant.`,[`Return to the Mirror Chamber with all shards.`,`Carry both Sol orbs to the palace entrance to empower the sword.`,`Cut through the dark barriers and climb to Zant.`],`Keep moving while carrying a Sol; its guardian hand follows.`,`Zant revisits earlier arenas: use their corresponding tools, then punish his exhausted spinning attacks.`),r(`castle`,`Hyrule Castle`,`End the occupation.`,[`Break the castle barrier and advance through the courtyards.`,`Climb the interior using keys, wolf senses, and the Clawshot.`,`Complete the throne-room battle, pursuit, and final duel.`],`Bring healing supplies before climbing the final staircase.`,`Return possessed Zelda's energy, wrestle Beast Ganon as a wolf, keep Zelda aligned on horseback, then dodge Ganondorf's sword and counter.`)],sources:[{label:`Zelda Dungeon — full campaign guide`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/twilight-princess-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Palace of Twilight`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/twilight-princess-walkthrough/palace-of-twilight/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Hyrule Castle`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/twilight-princess-walkthrough/hyrule-castle/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — In Search of the Sky`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/twilight-princess-walkthrough/in-search-of-the-sky/`}]},{slug:`phantom-hourglass`,title:`Phantom Hourglass`,year:2007,platform:`Nintendo DS`,era:`handheld`,intro:`Chart four seas while an hourglass buys minutes inside a cursed temple.`,edition:`DS campaign. Other supported platforms require equivalents for touch, microphone, and closing-the-system inputs.`,scope:`Main story with required Ocean King return visits; optional collections excluded.`,essentials:[`Mark clues on maps.`,`Safe zones pause the temple's hourglass.`,`New tools open return-visit shortcuts.`],chapters:[r(`mercay`,`Mercay and the first spirit`,`Rescue Linebeck and reach the Isle of Ember.`,[`Take Oshus's sword and free Linebeck in the Temple of the Ocean King.`,`Sail to Ember, rescue Astrid using the island's grave clues, and enter the Temple of Fire.`,`Obtain the Boomerang and reunite the three spirits forming Blaaz.`],`The upper screen reveals the correct order by the spirits' horns.`,`Draw the Boomerang through all three in that order, then strike the reunited Blaaz.`),r(`wind`,`The northwestern sea`,`Recover the Spirit of Wisdom.`,[`Take the Phantom Hourglass and retrieve the next sea chart from the Ocean King's temple.`,`Buy the cannon on Cannon Island; record the safe route through the fog from Molida's hidden hideaway.`,`Sail to the Isle of Gust, activate its windmills, and obtain bombs in the Temple of Wind.`],`Mark wind directions and safe paths before moving.`,`Throw bombs into Cyclok's small whirlwinds when they move beneath him, then slash after he falls.`),r(`courage`,`A mark on the sea`,`Find the third spirit.`,[`Revisit the Ocean King's temple; transfer the sacred crest to your sea chart by closing the DS.`,`Buy the Salvage Arm and recover the Sun Key at that mark.`,`Open Molida's sun door, enter the Temple of Courage, and obtain the Bow.`],`Trace the invisible floor route on your map.`,`The top screen shows invisible Crayk's viewpoint: fire toward that camera, break the exposed shell growths, then attack his tail.`),r(`ghost-ship`,`The Ghost Ship`,`Find Tetra.`,[`Follow the spirits' signals through the fog.`,`Escort the sisters through the decks, checking their advice against visible clues.`,`Defeat the Cubus Sisters, find Tetra, and visit Zauz for the Phantom Sword plan.`],`Some advice aboard is deliberately misleading.`,`Return the solid energy ball with sword swings; avoid the other projectiles.`),r(`goron`,`The first pure metal`,`Recover Crimsonine.`,[`Return to the Ocean King's temple for the southeastern sea chart.`,`Speak with every Goron on Goron Island, pass Biggoron's quiz, and follow Gongoron.`,`Alternate between Link and Gongoron in the temple; steer Bombchus through small passages.`],`Station one character safely before switching.`,`Knock Dongorongo over with Gongoron and send a Bombchu into its mouth; later feed it bombs when it inhales.`),r(`ice`,`The frozen island`,`Recover Azurine.`,[`Sail to the Isle of Frost and identify the disguised Yook among the Anouki.`,`Cross the snowfield and enter the Temple of Ice.`,`Obtain the Grappling Hook; stretch ropes between posts for crossings and rebounds.`],`Draw grapple paths carefully: the rope itself is part of the puzzle.`,`Reflect Gleeok's fire and ice shots toward the opposite-colored head, then grapple its tongues to posts.`),r(`ruins`,`The drowned kingdom`,`Recover Aquanine.`,[`Get the northeastern chart during another Ocean King visit; follow the Isle of the Dead's clues to the Isle of Ruins.`,`Obtain the Regal Necklace, visit the royal spirits, and lower the island's water.`,`Enter Mutoh's Temple, collect the Hammer, and use its launch platforms.`],`Draw or mark puzzle patterns before changing floors.`,`Launch upward to hammer Eox's marked body points; after its armor breaks, attack the remaining head's weak point.`),r(`bellum`,`The Phantom Sword`,`Free the Ocean King and Tetra.`,[`Bring all three metals to Zauz; take the forged blade to Oshus for completion.`,`Descend the Ocean King's temple again, now able to defeat Phantoms, and confront Bellum.`,`Pursue the possessed ship with Linebeck and complete the final sword battle.`],`Ciela's time-stopping power works only after collecting the required Phantom Sphere.`,`Grapple Bellum's slime and shoot its eyes; in the possessed-Linebeck duel, stop time when the upper screen shows its back eye open.`)],sources:[{label:`Zelda Dungeon — complete campaign index`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/phantom-hourglass-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Temple of Courage`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/phantom-hourglass-walkthrough/temple-of-courage/`},{label:`Thonky — Goron Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/goron-temple`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Mutoh's Temple`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/phantom-hourglass-walkthrough/mutohs-temple/`}]},{slug:`spirit-tracks`,title:`Spirit Tracks`,year:2009,platform:`Nintendo DS`,era:`handheld`,intro:`An engineer and a ghostly princess rebuild the railway together.`,edition:`DS campaign: microphone for flute and Whirlwind; touch screen for Phantom routes.`,scope:`Main story through the Dark Realm; passenger favors and stamps excluded.`,essentials:[`Revisit the tower between realms for maps.`,`Empower Link's sword before Phantom possession.`,`Leave trains room to brake or reverse.`],chapters:[r(`tower`,`The princess and the tower`,`Recover the Forest Rail Map.`,[`Travel from Aboda to the castle for the engineer ceremony.`,`Help Zelda escape and follow the broken tracks toward the tower.`,`Collect three Tears of Light, strike a Phantom from behind, and let Zelda possess it.`],`Send Zelda across hazards first; Link can ride her shield through some dangers.`),r(`forest`,`Restore the Forest Realm`,`Complete the first Lokomo duet.`,[`Follow the Lost Woods' tree directions to Gage's sanctuary.`,`Play the restoration duet and take the restored tracks to the Forest Temple.`,`Obtain the Whirlwind; blow keys, mist, and explosive objects where needed.`],`Aim before blowing into the microphone.`,`Clear Stagnox's rear cloud with the Whirlwind; later blow an explosive enemy into him.`),r(`snow`,`Snowbound tracks`,`Restore the second region.`,[`Return to the tower, use Zelda's Phantom help, and recover the Snow Rail Map.`,`Consult the Anouki and Ferrus to navigate the blizzard and reach Steem.`,`Play Steem's duet, enter the Snow Temple, and obtain the Boomerang.`],`Draw a Boomerang path through fire or ice before its destination.`,`Hit Fraaz with the opposite element; later use the fire and ice he leaves behind.`),r(`ocean`,`A railway beneath the sea`,`Open the Ocean Temple.`,[`Complete the next tower section, then arrange the broken bridge's repair.`,`Bring Carben back from Papuchia to his sanctuary and perform the duet.`,`Follow the underwater tracks; in the Ocean Temple, obtain the Whip and use its handles and switches.`],`Protect the train from sea attacks instead of holding maximum speed blindly.`,`Whip a thorn from Phytops's tendril and throw it at the eye to create a sword opening.`),r(`fire`,`Gorons and the Fire Temple`,`Restore the final realm's tracks.`,[`Get the Fire Rail Map at the tower and visit the blocked Goron Village.`,`Deliver Mega Ice from the snow region to cool the obstruction; reach Embrose and play his duet.`,`Collect the keys needed to enter the Fire Temple, obtain the Bow, and ride its minecarts.`],`Protect the ice shipment; enough must survive the journey.`,`Shoot Cragma's glowing body targets, then attack its eye from the minecart.`),r(`byrne`,`The tower summit`,`Reach Zelda's stolen body.`,[`Return to the tower and combine Link's items with Zelda's different Phantom abilities.`,`Open the upper route and confront Byrne.`,`After the story sequence, follow Anjean's new lead toward the Sand Realm.`],`Keep Zelda available to intercept Byrne's attacks.`,`Let Zelda catch Byrne's extended claw, then attack while he is held.`),r(`sand`,`The Bow of Light`,`Prepare for the Dark Realm.`,[`Reach Rael and complete his duet; pass the sand region's railway trials.`,`Enter the Sand Temple and obtain the Sand Wand.`,`Raise sand to move objects, redirect boulders, and reach the Bow of Light.`],`Sand columns collapse; prepare a whole crossing before climbing.`,`Raise sand to catch Skeldritch's boulders, launch them at its armor, then reach its exposed weak point.`),r(`compass`,`One last ascent`,`Find the Compass of Light.`,[`Return to the Tower of Spirits with the Bow of Light.`,`Use Torch, Warp, and Wrecker Phantoms where their specific abilities fit.`,`Recover the compass and board the train for the newly revealed Dark Realm tracks.`],`Mark which Phantom type each unfinished obstacle needs.`),r(`malladus`,`The Dark Realm`,`Defeat Malladus.`,[`Collect Tears of Light; ram armored trains while invincible.`,`Destroy the Demon Train's weapons; guide Zelda past Cole to restrain Malladus for a Light Arrow.`,`Protect Zelda, perform the duet, and lure Malladus into her aim.`],`The upper screen shows Zelda's shooting angle.`,`Expose Malladus's back to her arrows, slash its forehead gem when it falls, and complete the finishing thrust.`)],sources:[{label:`Nintendo — Spirit Tracks manual`,url:`https://www.nintendo.com/eu/media/downloads/games_8/emanuals/nintendo_ds_21/Manual_NintendoDS_TheLegendOfZeldaSpiritTracks_EN.pdf`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — chapter walkthrough`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/spirit-tracks-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Fire Realm`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/spirit-tracks-walkthrough/the-fire-realm/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Dark Realm`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/spirit-tracks-walkthrough/the-dark-realm/`}]},{slug:`skyward-sword`,title:`Skyward Sword`,year:2011,platform:`Nintendo Wii`,era:`3d`,intro:`Descend beneath the clouds to temper a sacred blade.`,edition:`Wii campaign. Switch HD retains its story and dungeons, adding button-only controls and conveniences.`,scope:`All story dungeons through the finale; excludes Hero Mode and collection completion.`,essentials:[`Choose sword directions deliberately.`,`Repair shields at the bazaar.`,`Use bird statues; replenish supplies in Skyloft.`],chapters:[r(`skyloft`,`The sky and the sealed woods`,`Find the route Zelda took.`,[`Rescue your Loftwing, win the Wing Ceremony, and follow Fi to the Goddess Sword.`,`Place the tablet, descend to Faron, and meet the old woman at the Sealed Temple.`,`Find the Kikwis, obtain the Slingshot, and reach Skyview Temple.`],`Dowsing narrows searches; it does not reveal a safe walking route.`),r(`skyview`,`Skyview Temple`,`Reach the spring.`,[`Dizzy eye sentries with circular sword movement.`,`Fly the Beetle through gaps to hit switches.`,`Raise the water, collect the boss key, and confront Ghirahim.`],`Save stamina for vine climbs.`,`Feint, slash around Ghirahim's guard, and match incoming daggers' orientation.`),r(`earth`,`Eldin and the Earth Temple`,`Follow the second tablet.`,[`Find the Mogmas, obtain Digging Mitts, and collect the scattered entrance-key pieces.`,`Roll bombs beneath low openings and obtain the Bomb Bag inside the temple.`,`Guide the large stone ball through lava to the upper route.`],`Bomb flowers refill the Bomb Bag.`,`Throw bombs into Scaldera's mouth while it inhales; slash the exposed eye.`),r(`lanayru`,`A desert that remembers`,`Reach the Temple of Time.`,[`Activate Timeshift Stones to restore local machinery.`,`Power the three nodes that open the Lanayru Mining Facility.`,`Obtain the Gust Bellows and clear sand hiding switches and mechanisms.`],`A Timeshift Stone changes only the area around it.`,`Cut Moldarach's claw eyes with correctly angled swings, then thrust into its central eye.`),r(`flame-one`,`The sacred flames`,`Begin tempering the sword.`,[`Stop the Imprisoned at the Sealed Grounds and learn the Ballad of the Goddess.`,`Repair Skyloft's windmill with Scrapper; align both windmills and enter Thunderhead's Isle of Songs.`,`Complete Faron's trial for the Water Dragon's Scale; bring Skyview's sacred water to the Water Dragon.`],`Tears pause Silent Realm guardians.`),r(`cistern`,`Ancient Cistern`,`Temper the sword with Farore's Flame.`,[`Enter behind the waterfall and explore both levels of the cistern.`,`Obtain the Whip to pull handles and take keys from enemies.`,`Raise the central statue and climb to Koloktos.`],`Inspect the statue's hand positions for the directional door clue.`,`Whip away Koloktos's arms, seize a dropped sword, and break its cage to attack the heart.`),r(`sandship`,`The buried sea`,`Find Nayru's Flame.`,[`Learn Nayru's Wisdom; complete Lanayru's trial for Clawshots.`,`Investigate the skipper's shipyard and pirate stronghold; locate the invisible Sandship.`,`Obtain the Bow; shoot the Timeshift Stone through openings to change eras.`],`Mechanisms depend on the active era.`,`Cut Tentalus's tentacles with Skyward Strikes, then shoot its eye and slash.`),r(`fire-sanctuary`,`Din's Flame`,`Complete the sword's transformation.`,[`Finish Eldin's Silent Realm for the Fireshield Earrings.`,`Help Scrapper carry the Water Dragon's basin to the summit.`,`Enter the Fire Sanctuary, obtain Mogma Mitts, and navigate underground passages.`],`Avoid lava routes without checking the available stepping stones.`,`Beat Ghirahim again by striking around his guards and countering his committed attacks.`),r(`hero-song`,`The Song of the Hero`,`Earn the final trial.`,[`Repel the Imprisoned and open the Gate of Time for Zelda's blessing.`,`Help Levias in Thunderhead; seek the three dragons' song parts.`,`Gather Tadtones, recover Eldin's confiscated equipment, and heal Lanayru with a Life Tree fruit grown in the past.`],`Return to Levias to complete the song.`),r(`finale`,`Sky Keep and the last descent`,`Finish the quest across time.`,[`Complete Skyloft's Silent Realm; use the Stone of Trials to open Sky Keep.`,`Rearrange the dungeon's rooms and collect all three Triforce pieces.`,`Follow Ghirahim into the past, defeat his army and final form, then face Demise.`],`Replenish potions before entering Demise's arena.`,`Counter Demise's sword openings; when lightning begins, charge your raised blade, stun him with a strike, and land the finishing blow after knocking him down.`)],sources:[{label:`Zelda Dungeon — main campaign`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/skyward-sword-walkthrough/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Thunderhead`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/skyward-sword-walkthrough/thunderhead/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Sky Keep`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/skyward-sword-walkthrough/sky-keep/`},{label:`Zelda Dungeon — Final Showdown`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/skyward-sword-walkthrough/final-showdown/`}]}].sort((e,t)=>e.year-t.year),a={"the-legend-of-zelda":{chapters:{eagle:{route:[`From the starting screen, collect the sword in the cave. Travel right once, north four screens and left once to find the bridge into the Eagle.`,`Clear enemy rooms before trying their block puzzles. The Bow is in a side-view treasure chamber: collect it before leaving, even though this dungeon's boss does not require it.`,`Keep track of locked doors and spend keys on unexplored branches. Defeat Aquamentus from beside the line of its fireballs, then collect both the Heart Container and Triforce fragment.`],references:[{title:`It's Dangerous To Go Alone! Take This.`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/its-dangerous-to-go-alone-take-this`},{title:`Dungeon 1: Eagle`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-1-eagle`}]},"moon-manji":{route:[`Explore the Moon in the eastern woods with bombs available. Dodongo swallows a bomb placed in front of its mouth; attacking its armoured body with the sword is ineffective.`,`In the Manji, approach Darknuts from behind or from their unshielded side. Retrieve the Raft from the basement before heading to the boss.`,`Manhandla becomes faster as it loses heads. A bomb placed where several heads overlap can shorten the fight; retreat and reposition instead of trading damage.`],references:[{title:`Dungeon 2: Moon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-2-moon`},{title:`Dungeon 3: Manji`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-3-manji`}]},snake:{route:[`Stand on the dock on the western shore to let the Raft carry you to the island dungeon. Bring a candle to reveal enemies and exits in dark rooms.`,`Find the Stepladder, then revisit passages interrupted by one tile of water. It works automatically at a suitable gap; it cannot carry you across a lake.`,`Gleeok's severed heads remain dangerous. Concentrate attacks on heads still attached to the body while moving away from the detached ones.`],references:[{title:`Dungeon 4: Snake`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-4-snake`}]},lizard:{route:[`At the Lost Hills, take the northern exit repeatedly to reach the dungeon. Refill bombs first: several connections are concealed inside ordinary-looking walls.`,`Use the underground passage network to reach the Recorder. Fight blue Darknuts patiently from their sides and avoid being surrounded.`,`Play the Recorder in Digdogger's room to change its form, then switch back to the sword. If you have twelve hearts, the Magical Sword is a useful detour before the later levels.`],references:[{title:`Dungeon 5: Lizard`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-5-lizard`},{title:`Get the Magical Sword`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/get-magical-sword`}]},dragon:{route:[`Enter the graveyard-region dungeon with arrows and some rupees. Each arrow consumes a rupee, so purchasing arrows alone is insufficient.`,`Watch where Wizzrobes appear, then attack between their volleys. Keep away from Like Likes, which can consume the larger shield.`,`Find the Magical Rod in its basement chamber. Against Gohma, line up directly in front of its eye and release an arrow when the eye opens.`],references:[{title:`Dungeon 6: Dragon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-6-dragon`}]},demon:{route:[`Purchase Food before travelling to the western pond that has no fairy. Play the Recorder on that screen to reveal the entrance.`,`The hungry Goriya blocks progression until you give it Food. Use bombs to investigate dead ends and collect the Red Candle on the way through.`,`Treat recurring bosses as resource checks: use the Recorder on Digdogger and attack Aquamentus from outside its fireball spread. Keep spare bombs for the hidden routes beyond them.`],references:[{title:`Dungeon 7: Demon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-7-demon`}]},lion:{route:[`Burn the suspicious bush in the southeastern woods to uncover the Lion. Carry healing and avoid entering the hardest rooms with an empty bomb supply.`,`Search the stair passages for the Magical Key and Book of Magic. The key handles locked dungeon doors without using your remaining small keys.`,`Do not stop exploring simply because you have found the route to Gleeok. Take the dungeon treasures, defeat its multiple heads and collect the eighth Triforce fragment.`],references:[{title:`Dungeon 8: Lion`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-8-lion`}]},"death-mountain":{route:[`Bomb the southern face of the western rock at Spectacle Rock. All eight fragments are required to pass the guardian inside.`,`Map stair passages as pairs of connected rooms; their exits can be far apart. Defeat every enemy before testing movable blocks, and check bombable walls when the visible route ends.`,`Collect the Red Ring and Silver Arrows before the final approach. The ring reduces incoming damage; the arrows are required for the finishing blow.`],references:[{title:`Dungeon 9: Death Mountain`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-9-death-mountain`}]},ganon:{route:[`Bring medicine and enough rupees to fire arrows. Watch the origin of Ganon's fireballs to estimate his invisible position and strike with the sword.`,`When repeated sword hits leave him red and vulnerable, fire a Silver Arrow immediately. Ordinary arrows cannot finish the battle.`,`Collect the Triforce he leaves behind, enter Zelda's room and cut away the flames. The ending unlocks the separate Second Quest.`],references:[{title:`Dungeon 9: Death Mountain`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/dungeon-9-death-mountain`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Collect the Heart Container after each of the first eight dungeon bosses. Explore the overworld for the five additional containers; when an old man offers medicine or a heart, choose the heart for permanent completion.`,`Use the Raft and Stepladder to revisit shoreline rewards. Check sword thresholds separately: five hearts for the White Sword and twelve for the Magical Sword.`,`Buy the Blue Ring when your budget allows, upgrade bomb capacity in Levels 5 and 7, and check the equipment list before entering Death Mountain. The Red Ring replaces the Blue Ring later.`],references:[{title:`List of Heart Containers`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/heart-containers`},{title:`List of Items`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/list-of-items`},{title:`Overworld Maps`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/map`}],title:`Heart Containers and permanent equipment`},{route:[`Start from the completed save or use the name ZELDA on a separate file. Treat this as a new journey: the First Quest's locations are not a reliable dungeon route.`,`Some dungeon walls can be walked through without a bomb. Check the dedicated level references when a room seems sealed, and plan heart upgrades around this quest's changed locations.`],references:[{title:`Second Quest Start`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/second-quest-start`},{title:`Second Quest Dungeon 1`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/quest2-dungeon-1`},{title:`Second Quest Dungeon 2`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/quest2-dungeon-2`},{title:`Second Quest Dungeon 3`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/quest2-dungeon-3`},{title:`Second Quest Dungeon 4`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/quest2-dungeon-4`},{title:`Second Quest Dungeon 5`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/quest2-dungeon-5`},{title:`Second Quest Dungeon 6`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/quest2-dungeon-6`},{title:`Second Quest Dungeon 7`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/quest2-dungeon-7`},{title:`Second Quest Dungeon 8`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/quest2-dungeon-8`},{title:`Second Quest Dungeon 9`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/legend-of-zelda/quest2-dungeon-9`}],title:`The Second Quest`}],editions:[`These routes use the First Quest. After the ending, the Second Quest rearranges dungeon entrances, rooms and treasures; use its separate references rather than repeating this itinerary.`]},"adventure-of-link":{chapters:{parapa:{route:[`Learn Shield in Rauru and gather experience on the road before entering Parapa Palace. Shield reduces damage but uses magic needed for other spells.`,`Explore the palace's side branches for the Candle before placing the crystal. The Candle illuminates the overworld caves used later.`,`Against Horsehead, jump and strike the head above the armour, then retreat as the mace swings. After winning, continue to the statue and place the crystal.`],references:[{title:`Rauru Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/rauru-town`},{title:`Parapa Desert`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/parapa-desert`},{title:`Parapa Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/parapa-palace`}]},"death-mountain":{route:[`Return the stolen trophy to Ruto to learn Jump. Find the mirror for the woman in Saria to gain access to Life, then use Bagu's permission to cross the river.`,`In Death Mountain, record cave entrances and exits rather than choosing every fork at random. Refill before the final stretch to the Hammer.`,`Use the Hammer to break overworld rocks and reach the nearby Magic Container. In Mido, obtain Fairy through the medicine quest and use Jump to reach the Downward Thrust teacher.`],references:[{title:`Ruto Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/ruto-town`},{title:`Saria Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/saria-town`},{title:`Death Mountain`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/death-mountain`},{title:`Mido Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/mido-town`}]},midoro:{route:[`Use the Hammer to reach the swamp palace. Carry enough magic for Shield and Life, and check the lower branches for the Handy Glove.`,`The glove allows sword strikes to break dungeon blocks. Return to blocked corridors with it instead of wasting time looking for a separate switch.`,`Helmethead's helmets detach and fire projectiles as the fight progresses. Jump to strike the vulnerable head, then move clear of the floating helmets.`],references:[{title:`Midoro Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/midoro-palace`}]},island:{route:[`Reach the island through the cave route from the coast. Look for the Raft inside the palace before continuing to the boss.`,`Use Downward Thrust on enemies that are dangerous to approach head-on. Save magic for Fairy where a passage or gap requires flight.`,`Rebonack first attacks on horseback. Use downward strikes to unseat him, then fight the exposed Iron Knuckle by alternating high and low attacks around its shield.`],references:[{title:`Island Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/island-palace`}]},maze:{route:[`In eastern Hyrule, help the woman in Nabooru for Fire. Reach Darunia, rescue the child from Maze Island and return for Reflect; learn Upward Thrust from the hidden teacher too.`,`Recover the Boots in Maze Palace. They let you traverse designated shallow-water paths on the overworld rather than every sea tile.`,`Carock cannot be defeated by ordinary sword attacks. Cast Reflect, face his projectiles and crouch with your shield toward them.`],references:[{title:`Nabooru Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/nabooru-town`},{title:`Darunia Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/darunia-town`},{title:`Maze Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/maze-palace`}]},ocean:{route:[`Use the Boots to find the route across the eastern sea. Search the palace for the Flute before placing the next crystal.`,`Do not chase every optional experience bag if your lives or magic are low. Preserve enough magic for defence and healing during the boss.`,`Gooma swings a heavy weapon while leaving his body exposed between attacks. Step in for a sword hit, then back away before the swing reaches you.`],references:[{title:`Ocean Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/ocean-palace`}]},hidden:{route:[`Play the Flute to remove the River Devil. In New Kasuto, obtain the final Magic Container and Spell, then use Spell in the empty part of town to reveal the Magic Key.`,`Play the Flute at the three-rock formation to reveal Hidden Palace. Retrieve the Cross and watch for invisible floor gaps; some deliberate falls lead to new routes.`,`Keep magic for Jump and Fairy during the descent. Against Barba, jump to strike the dragon's head as it emerges from lava, then return to safe ground.`],references:[{title:`New Kasuto`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/new-kasuto`},{title:`Hidden Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/hidden-palace`}]},"great-palace":{route:[`Confirm that all six crystals are placed and collect every Magic Container. Learn Thunder in Old Kasuto, then refill before the long road to the Great Palace.`,`The palace is a navigation challenge as well as a combat test. Mark elevator branches and avoid spending all your magic before the final rooms.`,`Cast Thunder to expose Thunderbird's weak point, then jump to strike its face. Dark Link follows immediately: block, change attack height and take controlled openings instead of jumping constantly.`],references:[{title:`Great Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/great-palace`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Collect all four extra Heart Containers and all four Magic Containers. Magic capacity is a progression requirement because the final spell depends on it.`,`Check the spell list and both sword techniques before the Great Palace. Attack, Magic and Life can each reach level 8; raising them makes the final route more forgiving.`,`Save one-use extra-life dolls for a difficult late-game attempt rather than collecting them automatically while passing through.`],references:[{title:`Heart Container Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/heart-containers`},{title:`New Kasuto`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/new-kasuto`},{title:`Mido Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/mido-town`},{title:`Darunia Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-ii-adventure-of-link/darunia-town`}],title:`Hearts, magic and techniques`}],editions:[`The route follows the western NES game. Experience rules, enemy behaviour and some layouts differ in the original Japanese Disk System release.`]},"links-awakening":{chapters:{tail:{route:[`Take the shield from Tarin and reclaim the sword at the beach. In the forest, bring the mushroom to the witch, then use her Magic Powder on the raccoon to open the route to the Tail Key.`,`Inside Tail Cave, collect Roc's Feather and use it to cross floor gaps. Match the symbols on the rotating enemies before collecting their key.`,`Moldorm's vulnerable point is its tail. Stay near the middle of the platform and circle behind it; falling sends you away from the arena.`],references:[{title:`Mysterious Forest`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/mysterious-forest`},{title:`Tail Cave`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/tail-cave`}]},bottle:{route:[`After the Moblin raid, rescue BowWow from the cave and bring him to Goponga Swamp. He eats the flowers blocking Bottle Grotto.`,`Light the entrance torches and retrieve the Power Bracelet. For the Pols Voice puzzle, defeat the rabbit-like enemy first, the bat second and the Stalfos last.`,`Block the Genie's fireballs, strike the bottle until it stops, then lift and throw it with the bracelet. Once it breaks, attack the exposed Genie.`],references:[{title:`Goponga Swamp`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/goponga-swamp`},{title:`Bottle Grotto`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/bottle-grotto`}]},key:{route:[`Complete Richard's request for five Golden Leaves in Kanalet Castle, then cross the field behind his villa to dig up the Slime Key.`,`Inside Key Cavern, collect the Pegasus Boots and combine running with Roc's Feather to clear longer gaps. Defeat all enemies in suspicious rooms before leaving.`,`Dash into Slime Eye to make it drop, then strike and run through the connection between its halves. Jump when the separated eyes land to avoid being stunned.`],references:[{title:`Ukuku Prairie`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/ukuku-prairie`},{title:`Key Cavern`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/key-cavern`}]},angler:{route:[`Bring Marin to wake the walrus blocking Yarna Desert. Defeat the Lanmola for the Angler Key, unlock the waterfall and enter from the mountain route above.`,`Learn the order of the glowing floor tiles in the clue room, then repeat it in the matching puzzle room. Obtain the Flippers to explore deep water.`,`The Angler Fish is fought underwater. Swim near its head, strike the glowing lure and move away from falling debris and smaller fish.`],references:[{title:`Yarna Desert`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/yarna-desert`},{title:`Angler's Tunnel`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/anglers-tunnel`}]},catfish:{route:[`Help the ghost return to its house and grave, then reach the entrance in Martha's Bay by diving through the underwater approach.`,`Track the recurring Master Stalfos encounters until you recover the Hookshot. Strike the skeleton to collapse it and use a bomb while it is down.`,`For Slime Eel, pull a genuine head out of a wall opening with the Hookshot. Attack its exposed body while staying clear of the rotating tail in the centre.`],references:[{title:`Martha's Bay`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/marthas-bay`},{title:`Catfish's Maw`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/catfishs-maw`}]},face:{route:[`Visit the southern shrine for the Face Key and the mural before opening Face Shrine. Bring bombs and prepare to lift the large elephant statues.`,`Acquire the stronger Power Bracelet and throw statues at sealed doors. For chess-piece puzzles, account for the landing movement rather than throwing blindly.`,`When Facade's face appears in the floor, place a bomb on it. Keep moving around temporary holes; avoid standing beside a hole as it opens.`],references:[{title:`Face Shrine`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/face-shrine`}]},eagle:{route:[`Learn the Frog's Song of Soul, revive the flying rooster and use it to reach the Bird Key. Follow the mountain caves to Eagle's Tower.`,`Carry the iron ball through the tower and throw it into all four pillars. Plan how to move the ball across barriers before leaving it behind; destroying the pillars lowers the upper floor.`,`Collect the Mirror Shield before climbing to Evil Eagle. Raise it against feathers and walk into the wind to stay on the platform, then strike the eagle's beak during its passes.`],references:[{title:`Tal Tal Mountains`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/tal-tal-mountains`},{title:`Eagle's Tower`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/eagles-tower`}]},turtle:{route:[`Use the Mirror Shield to pass the flamethrower cave. Play the Frog's Song of Soul outside Turtle Rock, defeat the awakened entrance guardian and enter.`,`Steer the moving platform to fill every gap in its floor puzzle. Collect the Magic Rod, then use it to melt ice while preserving blocks needed as stepping stones.`,`Shoot Hot Head with the Magic Rod as it emerges from lava. Continue firing at the exposed core once the outer shell breaks.`],references:[{title:`Turtle Rock`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/turtle-rock`}]},egg:{route:[`Finish the trading sequence to obtain the Magnifying Lens. Read the previously unreadable library book and record the maze directions from your own save.`,`Play the Ballad of the Wind Fish outside the Egg with all eight instruments. Follow your recorded directions inside; another player's sequence may not match.`,`Change tools for the Nightmare's forms: Magic Powder for the blob, reflected projectiles for the wizard, sword attacks for the familiar monsters and arrows or the boomerang for the final eye.`],references:[{title:`Wind Fish's Egg`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/wind-fishs-egg`},{title:`Trading Sequence`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/trading-sequence`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Advance the trading chain whenever you enter a new settlement. It eventually gives the Magnifying Lens needed to read the Egg's route and obtain the boomerang.`,`Revisit the beach, castle, prairie and mountain caves after gaining the shovel, bracelet, Flippers and Hookshot. Mark the individual seashell and heart locations in the reference for your edition.`,`In the original and DX versions, visit the Seashell Mansion at the five- and ten-shell milestones before collecting more; Switch uses a different reward ladder.`],references:[{title:`Trading Sequence`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/trading-sequence`},{title:`Game Boy Secret Seashells`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/secret-seashells`},{title:`Nintendo Switch Secret Seashells`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/nintendo-switch-secret-seashells`},{title:`Pieces of Heart`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/pieces-of-heart`}],title:`Trading, seashells and hearts`},{route:[`In DX and Switch, read the hidden library book for the Color Dungeon's graveyard clue. Complete its colour puzzles and choose a tunic reward.`,`DX photographs include events tied to temporary companions and story situations. Check the photograph list before advancing those scenes.`,`On Switch, return to Dampé as new dungeon chambers become available. Complete his challenges separately from the eight main instruments.`],references:[{title:`Color Dungeon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/color-dungeon`},{title:`Photographs`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/photographs`},{title:`Dampé's Chamber Dungeons`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-links-awakening/dampes-chamber-dungeons`}],title:`Edition-specific optional adventures`}],editions:[`Game Boy, DX and Switch have different collection totals. DX adds the Color Dungeon and photographs; Switch has Chamber Dungeons, bottles and fifty seashells. Use the edition selector before tracking completion.`]},"majoras-mask":{chapters:{"first-cycle":{route:[`Find the missing Stray Fairy and return it to the Great Fairy. Use Deku bubbles to pop the balloon, complete the Bombers' hide-and-seek game and note your own password.`,`Reach the observatory, look through the telescope and collect the Moon's Tear. Trade it to the Business Scrub to access the flower beneath the Clock Tower.`,`At midnight on the final night, reach Skull Kid and recover the ocarina with a bubble. Play the Song of Time, then learn the Song of Healing and return for the Great Fairy's Mask.`],references:[{title:`Beginning the Game`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/beginning-the-game`},{title:`Clock Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/clock-town`},{title:`How to Save the Game`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/how-to-save-the-game`}]},woodfall:{route:[`Bring medicine to Koume in the Woods of Mystery and use the boat tour to reach the Deku Palace. Follow the monkey's route and learn the Sonata of Awakening.`,`Open Woodfall Temple as Deku Link. Obtain the Bow, light distant torches with arrows through flames and use Deku flowers to cross the central room.`,`Against Odolwa on N64, create openings with the sword and other weapons while avoiding summoned enemies. On 3DS, use a Deku aerial attack to expose the eye, then strike it. Carry the rescued princess back in a bottle.`],references:[{title:`Southern Swamp`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/southern-swamp`},{title:`Woodfall Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/woodfall-temple`}]},snowhead:{route:[`Follow Darmani with the Lens of Truth and play the Song of Healing. Use hot spring water to thaw the Goron elder, then complete the lullaby with his child.`,`Play the Goron Lullaby at Snowhead. Obtain Fire Arrows and use them to thaw frozen switches; adjust the central pillar and remove its marked sections with Goron punches.`,`Roll after Goht and hit it with Goron spikes. In 3DS, attack its exposed eye when it falls. Before resetting time, use the restored spring for the Goron race and sword-upgrade chain.`],references:[{title:`Mountain Village`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/mountain-village`},{title:`Snowhead`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/snowhead`},{title:`Snowhead Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/snowhead-temple`},{title:`After Goht`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/after-goht`}]},"ranch-and-coast":{route:[`Use a Powder Keg to open Romani Ranch early in a cycle, learn Epona's Song and reach the coast. Heal Mikau to obtain the Zora Mask.`,`In the Pirate Fortress, obtain the Hookshot and collect four Zora eggs. Empty bottles at the Marine Research Laboratory between trips if you cannot carry all four.`,`Find the remaining three eggs at Pinnacle Rock, using the seahorse to navigate the murky water. Deliver all seven to the laboratory and learn the New Wave Bossa Nova.`],references:[{title:`Great Bay`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/great-bay-coast`},{title:`Pirate Fortress`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/pirate-fortress`}]},"great-bay":{route:[`Play the song for Lulu to awaken the turtle and Hookshot onto its trees. Inside the temple, follow coloured pipes to valves rather than swimming randomly through the central machinery.`,`Obtain Ice Arrows, use them for frozen stepping stones or enemy platforms, and reverse the central water flow to access the remaining branches. The 3DS version limits where ice platforms can form.`,`Against Gyorg, keep access to a safe platform and attack its weak point when exposed. In 3DS, the later underwater phase requires you to release underwater mines when the boss inhales.`],references:[{title:`Great Bay Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/great-bay-temple`}]},ikana:{route:[`Win the Garo's Mask from the Gorman brothers, then enter Ikana. Play the Song of Storms for Sharp to restore the river and allow the Music Box House sequence.`,`Reach Pamela's father without frightening her away and play the Song of Healing for the Gibdo Mask. Wear it underground and bring the supplies requested by the Gibdos.`,`Collect the Mirror Shield, use reflected light in Ikana Castle and expose the throne room to sunlight. Defeat the king and his guards, then learn the Elegy of Emptiness.`],references:[{title:`Ikana Valley`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/ikana-valley`},{title:`Ikana Canyon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/ikana-canyon`},{title:`Beneath the Well`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/beneath-the-well`},{title:`Ikana Castle`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/ikana-castle`}]},"stone-tower":{route:[`Use the Elegy with different forms to leave statues on the tower's switches. Inside, collect Light Arrows before trying to invert the dungeon.`,`Shoot the red emblem outside with a Light Arrow. Revisit the inverted rooms, remembering that ceilings become routes and treasure positions change in relation to you.`,`Collect all fifteen Stray Fairies across both orientations before returning them. Twinmold uses the Giant's Mask differently in N64 and 3DS; in 3DS, defeat the first worm before the giant phase becomes available.`],references:[{title:`Stone Tower`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/stone-tower`},{title:`Stone Tower Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/stone-tower-temple`}]},moon:{route:[`Carry the four boss remains to the Clock Tower at midnight on the final night. Play the Oath to Order to stop the Moon and enter it.`,`Complete the children's optional trials before approaching the child beneath the tree. Bringing all twenty non-transformation masks lets you earn the Fierce Deity's Mask.`,`Attack the back of Majora's Mask or reflect its beams when appropriate. Follow the moving Incarnation carefully, then use ranged stuns and sword openings against the whip-wielding final form.`],references:[{title:`The Moon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/the-moon`},{title:`Final Boss`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/final-boss-majora`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Separate permanent rewards from events reset by the Song of Time. Bank rupees and return dungeon Stray Fairies before rewinding; temporary fairies do not carry over.`,`Reserve a dedicated cycle for Anju and Kafei. Keep the Notebook's appointments in order and use separate cycles for mutually exclusive delivery rewards.`,`Combine regional heart and mask errands with the appropriate transformation, then use the Moon trials for the final hearts. Check the bottle list for your edition because the remake adds another bottle.`],references:[{title:`Masks Guide`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/masks-guide`},{title:`Pieces of Heart`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/pieces-of-heart`},{title:`Bombers Notebook`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/bombers-notebook`},{title:`Anju and Kafei Quest`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/anju-kafei-quest`},{title:`List of Bottles`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-majoras-mask/bottles`}],title:`A three-day completion plan`}],editions:[`The Nintendo 64 and 3DS versions differ in saving, some locations and boss mechanics. The routes below identify major differences; do not use an N64 boss tactic unchanged in the remake.`]},"oracle-of-ages":{chapters:{spirit:{route:[`After Veran possesses Nayru, take the sword and follow the Maku Tree's disappearance into the past. Rescue the young tree, then return to the present for the graveyard route.`,`In Spirit's Grave, light torches and investigate movable blocks. The Power Bracelet opens routes through pots that could not be lifted earlier.`,`Destroy Pumpkin Head's body, lift its pumpkin and throw it away. Strike the small spirit before it can recover its protection.`],references:[{title:`Beginning the Game`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/beginning-the-game`},{title:`Meet the Maku Tree`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/meet-the-maku-tree`},{title:`Yoll Graveyard`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/yoll-graveyard`},{title:`Spirit's Grave`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/spirits-grave`}]},wing:{route:[`Take the Harp of Ages from Nayru's house. When the present-day entrance collapses, use time travel to reach Wing Dungeon in the past.`,`Obtain Roc's Feather and use it for side-view passages and gaps. For coloured-floor puzzles, plan a route that reaches every required tile without trapping the moving marker.`,`Throw bombs into Head Thwomp's open top from the platform above. The resulting face determines its response; keep moving and repeat until the damaging red result defeats it.`],references:[{title:`Western Woods`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/western-woods`},{title:`Wing Dungeon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/wing-dungeon`}]},moon:{route:[`After the shipwreck, recover the stolen equipment through the Tokay exchanges. Plant the Scent Seedling in the past so its tree exists in the present.`,`In Moonlit Grotto, break the crystals controlling the central route and retrieve the Seed Shooter. Aim diagonally when a direct shot cannot reach a switch.`,`Shadow Hag retreats when watched. Turn away, then bounce a seed off a wall so it hits her as she approaches from behind.`],references:[{title:`Crescent Island`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/crescent-island`},{title:`Moonlit Grotto`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/moonlit-grotto`}]},skull:{route:[`Complete the Symmetry City restoration and use the Harp's expanded time travel to reach the highlands. Changes made in the past alter the route in the present.`,`Collect the Switch Hook and exchange positions with pots or diamond-shaped objects. Preserve a useful object on each side of a gap so you can return.`,`Plan the long floor-colouring puzzle before stepping off its starting tile. Against Eyesoar, hook the central eye out of its escort and strike it while stunned.`],references:[{title:`Symmetry City`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/symmetry-city`},{title:`Skull Dungeon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/skull-dungeon`}]},crown:{route:[`Bring a Bomb Flower to free the Goron Elder. Follow the ridge passages and pay attention to which entrances belong to each era.`,`The Cane of Somaria creates a block for pressure switches and path puzzles. Place it before crossing a route that depends on a switch staying pressed.`,`Smog's fragments follow obstacles. Add or remove a cane block to redirect them into one another, then strike the reassembled cloud and repeat for the next pattern.`],references:[{title:`Rescue the Goron Elder`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/rescue-goron-elder`},{title:`Crown Dungeon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/crown-dungeon`}]},mermaid:{route:[`Complete the Goron trading, dancing and minigame chain to obtain the keys for both eras. Mermaid's Cave is one progression spread across two versions of the dungeon.`,`Open the necessary route in the past, then revisit the present. Once you have the Mermaid Suit, dive into deep-water rooms and check underwater exits.`,`Use the Seed Shooter against the small mouth on Octogon's red side. When it dives, follow underwater and attack with the sword; return to the platform when it resurfaces.`],references:[{title:`Rolling Ridge`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/rolling-ridge`},{title:`Mermaid's Cave`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/mermaid-cave`}]},jabu:{route:[`Enter Ambi's Palace while she is away. Use Mystery Seeds on the possessed Nayru, pull Veran away with the Switch Hook and strike Veran rather than Nayru.`,`With the Tune of Ages, help King Zora and resolve the polluted sea. Enter Jabu-Jabu and use the water-level switches to expose different floors.`,`Upgrade to the Long Hook and revisit long gaps. Against Plasmarine, wait for its projectile, then swap positions so the boss changes colour and is struck by the opposite-coloured shot.`],references:[{title:`Ambi's Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/ambi-palace`},{title:`Jabu-Jabu's Belly`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/jabu-jabu-belly`}]},tomb:{route:[`Use the Zora Scale to reach the pirate route and obtain the information needed for the Sea of No Return. The tomb's entrance belongs to the past.`,`Find the Power Glove and collect four slates. Fit them into the central route to open the deeper chambers instead of hunting for an ordinary boss key alone.`,`Ramrock changes tools with each phase: return its fists, put bombs in its cupped hands, ricochet seeds behind its shields, then pull back a ball with the Power Glove and release it.`],references:[{title:`Sea of Storms`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/sea-of-storms`},{title:`Ancient Tomb`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/ancient-tomb`}]},veran:{route:[`Take the Huge Maku Seed after collecting all eight Essences. Enter the Black Tower in the past and follow the visual maze clues to its upper rooms.`,`Separate Veran from Ambi with Mystery Seeds and the Long Hook, then strike the exposed spirit. Defeat the flying phase while keeping clear of the mirror-moving shadows.`,`In the final transformations, bomb the spider to expose its face, evade the jumping armoured form and attack its exposed head, and strike the bee form when it approaches.`],references:[{title:`The Black Tower`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/black-tower`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Complete one Oracle first and start the other with its ending secret. Record each additional secret with the name of its recipient; return the reward password through Farore where required.`,`After the linked story's extra rescue events and final dungeon, continue to the Room of Rites. Reflect the witches' magic toward the opposite sister, then use the elemental seeds and sword openings against the combined form.`,`The final Ganon encounter follows the witches. Watch the teleport pattern, move away from the trident's range and use charged sword attacks when he reappears. The linked ending is distinct from defeating Veran alone.`],references:[{title:`Linked Game Differences`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/linked-game-differences`},{title:`Rescue Zelda`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/rescue-zelda`},{title:`Hero's Cave`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/hero-cave`},{title:`Room of Rites`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/room-of-rites`}],title:`Linked ending and secret exchanges`},{route:[`Search both eras for heart rewards and return with the shovel, swimming equipment and upgraded hook. Record which era a location belongs to.`,`Appraise rings at Vasu's shop and equip them deliberately; owning a ring does not activate its effect. Some rings depend on linked play or specific hardware and cannot all be obtained in one ordinary standalone file.`,`Plant Gasha Seeds in documented soft-soil spots and return after further adventuring. Keep random ring and heart rewards separate from fixed-location pickups when tracking what remains.`],references:[{title:`Oracle of Ages Heart Pieces Guide`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/heart-pieces`},{title:`Magic Rings in Oracle of Ages & Seasons`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/magic-rings`},{title:`Soft Soil Gasha Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/soft-soil-gasha`},{title:`Bipin and Blossom's Son`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-ages/bipin-blossom-son`}],title:`Hearts, rings and the trading journey`}],editions:[`An unlinked adventure and a linked adventure have different rewards and endings. Keep the ending secret and use it when starting the other Oracle game; a normal new file does not continue the linked story.`]},"oracle-of-seasons":{chapters:{root:{route:[`Recover the sword from Hero's Cave on a standalone file, then awaken the Maku Tree. Use the Gnarled Key to open the tree dungeon north of Horon Village.`,`Collect the Seed Satchel and use Ember Seeds to light torches. Push blocks after clearing enemies when a door remains closed.`,`Approach Aquamentus from outside the spread of its three fireballs. Strike its horn, collect the heart and Essence, then return to the Maku Tree's next clue.`],references:[{title:`Beginning the Game`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/beginning-the-game`},{title:`Meet the Maku Tree`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/meet-maku-tree`},{title:`Gnarled Root Dungeon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/gnarled-root-dungeon`}]},snake:{route:[`Follow the portal to Subrosia and obtain the Rod of Seasons' winter power. Stand on a tree stump to change the season; deep snow opens routes over otherwise impassable ledges.`,`Visit Holly for the Shovel and reach Snake's Remains. Retrieve the Power Bracelet and place pots on switches without throwing away the only usable pot.`,`Feed Dodongo a bomb, lift it while inflated and throw it onto the spikes. Sword strikes against its armoured body do not solve this fight.`],references:[{title:`Eastern Suburbs`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/eastern-suburbs`},{title:`Subrosia`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/subrosia`},{title:`Snake's Remains`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/snake-remains`}]},moth:{route:[`Find the Floodgate Key and open the swamp's water route. In Subrosia, give Rosa the ribbon and follow her to reach the summer tower.`,`Change the season to summer so vines grow to the dungeon entrance. Collect Roc's Feather and use it to cross pits and reach switches.`,`Against Mothula, jump over attacks while preserving a safe landing tile. Strike during its accessible passes and deal with smaller enemies before they crowd the platform.`],references:[{title:`Spool Swamp`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/spool-swamp`},{title:`Poison Moth's Lair`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/poison-moth-lair`}]},dragon:{route:[`Pass the Master Diver's test for the Flippers. Explore Mount Cucco and Subrosia to obtain spring power, then recover the Dragon Key.`,`Use the Slingshot to activate distant seed switches. Keep the appropriate seed selected: Ember Seeds can light torches, while other seeds serve different puzzles.`,`Avoid Gohma's claw and wait for its eye to open. Shoot Ember or Scent Seeds into the eye, then reposition before its next approach.`],references:[{title:`Sunken City`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/sunken-city`},{title:`Dancing Dragon Dungeon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/dancing-dragon-dungeon`}]},unicorn:{route:[`Obtain autumn power and change Eyeglass Lake's season to expose the route beneath the lake. Carry seeds and healing into Unicorn's Cave.`,`The Magnetic Gloves switch between attracting and repelling. Match the polarity to the anchor or metal ball, and use short adjustments to keep the ball on the intended path.`,`Drive the spiked metal ball into Digdogger. Continue using it against the smaller creatures after the boss splits, while keeping Link away from their movement.`],references:[{title:`Eyeglass Lake`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/eyeglass-lake`},{title:`Unicorn Cave`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/unicorn-cave`}]},ruins:{route:[`Collect the four shaped jewels and place them in the Tarm Ruins gate. Use seasonal changes to cross the ruins and follow the Lost Woods' instructions.`,`The Magical Boomerang can be steered after throwing. Curve it around walls to operate switches that cannot be hit in a straight line.`,`Hit Manhandla's open flowers with the boomerang. Once its protective form breaks, switch to the sword and chase the exposed core.`],references:[{title:`Tarm Ruins`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/tarm-ruins`},{title:`Ancient Ruins`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/ancient-ruins`}]},crypt:{route:[`Recover the pirates' missing bell in Samasa Desert and have the Subrosian smiths repair it. Return it to the captain to open the western route.`,`Reach the graveyard with the appropriate season. Inside Explorer's Crypt, light torches promptly where the ghosts threaten to return you to the entrance.`,`Roc's Cape extends jumps when held. Use it to cross longer gaps and evade Gleeok's shockwaves after cutting off its heads.`],references:[{title:`Graveyard`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/graveyard`},{title:`Explorer's Crypt`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/explorers-crypt`}]},maze:{route:[`Trigger the volcanic eruption through Subrosia, then return through the altered Temple Remains. Follow the new route and seasonal vines to the dungeon portal.`,`Collect the Hyper Slingshot and carry ice crystals through the minecart routes. Drop crystals into the correct shafts to cool lava on the lower floor.`,`Against Medusa Head, jump the beams and spinning orbs with Roc's Cape. Use a Pegasus Seed to stun it after the orb attack, then strike with the sword.`],references:[{title:`Temple Remains`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/temple-remains`},{title:`Sword and Shield Maze`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/sword-and-shield-maze`}]},onox:{route:[`Collect the Huge Maku Seed after the eighth Essence and enter Onox's Castle. Defeat the required enemies in each room before trying to advance.`,`Use charged sword attacks on Onox. When Din's crystal blocks your approach, move it with the Rod of Seasons rather than striking it.`,`For the dragon form, evade a hand slam, jump onto the lowered hand and strike the forehead jewel. Record the password displayed after the ending to start a linked Oracle of Ages adventure.`],references:[{title:`Onox's Castle`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/onox-castle`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Use the ending secret to start Ages as the continuation of Seasons, or import an Ages ending secret to begin a linked Seasons file. The order changes some encounters and secret recipients.`,`Complete each secret exchange in both games and return the resulting password to Farore where applicable. Keep ring transfer separate from the story-linking secret.`,`In linked play, return to Hero's Cave with late-game equipment for its expanded challenge. Defeating Onox does not complete the shared Oracle finale.`],references:[{title:`Linked Game Differences`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/linked-game-differences`},{title:`Magic Rings in Oracle of Ages & Seasons`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/magic-rings`}],title:`Linked play and permanent upgrades`},{route:[`Revisit locations in different seasons: frozen water, leaf-covered holes, mushrooms and summer vines can change access to a reward.`,`Track the fixed heart locations separately from rewards involving Gasha Nuts or Maple. A random reward may require more than one attempt and is not a missing map marker.`,`Record the animal companion attached to your file. Companion regions differ, so a route shown for another animal may not match your terrain.`],references:[{title:`Piece of Heart Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/pieces-of-heart`},{title:`Soft Soil Gasha Tree Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/soft-soil-gasha`},{title:`Bipin and Blossom's Son`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-oracle-of-seasons/bipin-blossom-son`}],title:`Hearts, Gasha trees and companions`}],editions:[`The first standalone route starts with Hero's Cave. In a linked file, the opening equipment and Hero's Cave challenge change, and the shared Oracle finale continues beyond Onox.`]},"the-minish-cap":{chapters:{deepwood:{route:[`Rescue Ezlo, shrink at the stump and enter the Minish village. Eat the Jabber Nut before trying to understand the villagers, then find the shrine entrance at Minish size.`,`Use mushroom handles as launchers and rotate the barrel to connect its exits. The Gust Jar clears webs and dust, and propels a lily pad across water.`,`Against Big Green Chuchu, suck away the base until it loses balance. Move away from the falling body, then attack its exposed head.`],references:[{title:`Journey to the Minish Woods`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/minish-woods`},{title:`Dungeon 1: Deepwood Shrine`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/deepwood-shrine`}]},flames:{route:[`Use ordinary water for the first bean and the mountain's mineral water for the special climbing bean. Buy the Grip Ring, reach Melari and leave the broken blade for repair.`,`Ride the minecarts and collect the Cane of Pacci. It flips overturned carts and charges holes that launch Link onto higher ledges.`,`Flip Gleerok's shell with the cane, climb its neck and strike the crystal. Return to safe ground before the lava rises and the neck becomes dangerous.`],references:[{title:`Mt. Crenel`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/mt-crenel`},{title:`Dungeon 2: Cave of Flames`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/cave-of-flames`}]},wilds:{route:[`Collect the repaired White Sword and infuse the two elements at the sanctuary. Charge the sword on marked tiles to create copies for paired switches.`,`Wake Rem with the Wake-Up Mushroom to obtain the Pegasus Boots. Dash across the swamp without stopping on unsafe ground.`,`Collect the Bow and golden Kinstones in Castor Wilds. Complete the required statue fusions to open the route into the Wind Ruins.`],references:[{title:`To Infuse the Picori Blade`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/infuse-picori-blade`},{title:`Castor Wilds`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/castor-wilds`}]},fortress:{route:[`Search the ruin's separate entrances and use sword copies on linked switches. Collect the Mole Mitts to dig through soft walls and uncover concealed passages.`,`Against Mazaal, shoot a hand's eye and strike the stunned hand. Disable both hands, shrink and enter the head.`,`Inside, dig to the vulnerable pillar and destroy it, then repeat the cycle. Take the Ocarina of Wind afterwards: the Wind Element is elsewhere.`],references:[{title:`The Fortress of Winds`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/fortress-of-winds`}]},droplets:{route:[`Return the three overdue library books. The book quest includes the Power Bracelets and eventually lets you reach Librari for the Flippers.`,`Enter the lake's Minish portal and navigate the frozen temple. Change the light reaching the ice, then use the Flame Lantern to open previously frozen routes.`,`Return Big Octorok's rocks with the sword. When it freezes itself, circle behind and light its tail; clear darkness with the lantern when needed.`],references:[{title:`The Water Element`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/water-element`},{title:`Dungeon 4: Temple of Droplets`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/temple-of-droplets`}]},clouds:{route:[`After infusing the Water Element, follow the Royal Valley route and complete the Royal Crypt. Use sword copies for switches that a single Link cannot hold.`,`Take King Gustaf's golden Kinstone to Veil Falls and fuse it at the source of the flow. Follow the climb into the clouds.`,`Explore both cloud layers, defeat the golden enemies and complete all five golden fusions. The cleared whirlwind leads to the Wind Tribe's tower.`],references:[{title:`To Find a Ghost`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/find-a-ghost`},{title:`The Royal Crypt`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/royal-crypt`},{title:`The Source of the Flow`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/source-of-the-flow`}]},palace:{route:[`Collect Roc's Cape and use extended jumps to cross cloud platforms. Watch a moving platform's whole cycle before launching across a long gap.`,`Alternate outdoor climbs with interior switch rooms. Create the required number of sword copies on the marked tiles before stepping onto multi-switch arrangements.`,`On the larger Gyorg, match copies to the exposed eyes and strike together. Jump to the smaller Gyorg when needed, strike its eye and jump the sweeping tail.`],references:[{title:`Dungeon 5: Palace of Winds`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/palace-of-winds`}]},castle:{route:[`Infuse the last element to restore the Four Sword. Use its power on petrified people and four-copy switches inside Dark Hyrule Castle.`,`Work through the castle's branches for keys and reconnect the central ascent. Refill hearts and arrange healing before taking the final stairs.`,`Defeat the three Darknuts before the final bell. Use controlled counters and rear attacks; spending too long circling without attacking can fail the timed sequence.`],references:[{title:`Completing the Sword`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/completing-the-sword`},{title:`Final Dungeon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/dark-hyrule-castle`}]},vaati:{route:[`Destroy the eyes around Vaati and remove their dark covering with the Gust Jar when needed. Strike the central eye only after the protection is gone.`,`In the next form, use arrows to reveal the vulnerable eyes, then create sword copies in the matching arrangement and attack together.`,`For Vaati's Wrath, flip an arm with Pacci, shrink and enter it. Destroy the different eye inside, using the lantern in darkness; finally return the four projectiles together with four Links.`],references:[{title:`Final Boss`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/vaati-final-boss`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Revisit towns after each major item and fuse available Kinstones. Follow the map animation to the opened reward instead of counting a fusion as a collected chest.`,`Save Carlov's shells for figures still missing from the collection. Some figures appear only after the ending; finish the collection to access its associated heart reward.`,`Use the Mitts, Flippers and Cape to revisit previously inaccessible caves and ledges. Track heart pieces separately from the full containers received through special rewards.`],references:[{title:`Kinstone Fusion Guide`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/kinstone-fusion`},{title:`Carlov's Figurines`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/carlov-figurines`},{title:`Pieces of Heart`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/pieces-of-heart`}],title:`Kinstones, figurines and hearts`},{route:[`Visit sword teachers as new equipment becomes available. Learn the eight Tiger Scroll techniques and check the additional training improvements separately.`,`Complete the mysterious-wall fusions to gather the Gorons and open their cave reward. Return after the ending for the final shield-related exchange.`,`Help the sick Wind Tribe resident with the Gust Jar during the early visit made possible by a fusion. Delaying until the normal late-game visit can lose the Light Arrows reward.`],references:[{title:`Tiger Scrolls`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/swiftblade-tiger-scrolls`},{title:`Goron Sidequest`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/goron-sidequest`},{title:`Gear Upgrades`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-minish-cap/gear-upgrades`}],title:`Training, bottles and missable help`}],editions:[`The main route follows the Game Boy Advance adventure. Complete time-sensitive character events before advancing too far, especially the sick Wind Tribe resident connected to the Light Arrows.`]},"a-link-between-worlds":{chapters:{eastern:{route:[`Follow the sword delivery to the Sanctuary, then return home after Yuga's attack. Borrow Ravio's Bow and activate the paired switches outside Eastern Palace.`,`Watch the rolling boulders before crossing their lanes. Shoot distant switches and ride the moving platforms to reach Yuga.`,`Stun Yuga with arrows and close in with the sword. After gaining the bracelet's wall-merging power, use it to escape the dungeon along ledges you could not previously cross.`],references:[{title:`Sanctuary`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/sanctuary`},{title:`Eastern Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/eastern-palace`}]},gales:{route:[`Recover Queen Oren's Smooth Gem to obtain the Flippers, then rent the Tornado Rod. Swim to the House of Gales and use the rod at its wind-operated entrance.`,`Use upward gusts and the Tornado Rod to reach moving platforms. Merge into walls around obstacles and keep enough energy to complete each crossing.`,`Use the rod to rise above Margomill's rotating layers and strike the eye. Remove intervening layers before trying to reach the weak point again.`],references:[{title:`House of Gales`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/house-of-gales`}]},hera:{route:[`Obtain the Power Glove from Rosso and rent the Hammer. Climb Death Mountain and flatten the entrance pegs.`,`Hit spring platforms with the Hammer, stand on them and wait for the launch. Use wall merging to move between ledges without falling to a lower floor.`,`Moldorm's tail is vulnerable; its head is not. Fight near the centre and circle behind it rather than following it toward the edge.`],references:[{title:`Tower of Hera`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/tower-of-hera`}]},lorule:{route:[`In the Lost Woods, follow the ghosts' changing instructions rather than assuming the same rule applies to every round. Draw the Master Sword with all three pendants.`,`Break the castle barrier and climb to Yuga. Identify the real target among the copies and attack when he leaves the wall.`,`Follow the newly opened passage to Lorule. Activate weather vanes and inspect world cracks: entering a crack from a different position can provide access to a different region.`],references:[{title:`Lost Woods`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/lost-woods`},{title:`Inside Hyrule Castle`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/inside-hyrule-castle`},{title:`Explore Lorule`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/explore-lorule`}]},thieves:{route:[`Enter the hideout in Thieves' Town and free the imprisoned thief. Leave her in safety when scouting a dangerous room.`,`Coordinate pressure switches, moving floors and barred passages. Merge into walls to reach controls while the thief waits, then return for her before proceeding.`,`When Stalblind presents his shield, merge into it and emerge behind him. After rescuing Osfala, return to Ravio to obtain the Sand Rod for Desert Palace.`],references:[{title:`Thieves' Hideout`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/thieves-hideout`}]},desert:{route:[`Use Lorule's cracks to reach Hyrule's desert. Raise sand pillars with the Sand Rod and merge along their sides to cross gaps.`,`Collect the Titan's Mitt and remove the large rocks blocking later routes. Keep track of which exits lead back outside rather than deeper into the palace.`,`The boss lies across the route into Lorule. Raise a path toward Zaganaga with sand pillars, avoid the summoned enemies and slash the flower when within reach.`],references:[{title:`Desert Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/desert-palace`}]},dark:{route:[`Sneak around the guards outside the palace, merging into walls to avoid their sightlines. Rent Bombs before entering.`,`Break boarded windows to send light onto sensors. In other rooms, extinguish torches to reveal paths that are only visible in darkness.`,`Bomb the Gemasaur King's mask to expose its weak point. Relight the room when darkness hides it, then strike while avoiding its charges.`],references:[{title:`Dark Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/dark-palace`}]},swamp:{route:[`Rent the Hookshot and bring the large Bomb Flower to the cracked boulder near the entrance. Its explosion opens the route and changes the surrounding water.`,`Pull switches and adjust water levels to reach different ledges. Use the Hookshot on targets across gaps before raising water that changes access.`,`Pull Arrghus's smaller eyes away one at a time and destroy them. Once the shield is gone, evade the main body's jumps and attack when it lands.`],references:[{title:`Swamp Palace`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/swamp-palace`}]},skull:{route:[`Use the forest's holes as separate dungeon entrances. Mark which upper opening leads to each lower room rather than repeatedly dropping into the same branch.`,`Carry the eyeballs to their sockets, using wall merging and moving platforms to reconnect paths. A carried eye cannot follow every route that Link can traverse alone.`,`When Knucklemaster charges, merge into the wall and let it crash. Emerge to attack during the recovery, then move before its next attempt.`],references:[{title:`Skull Woods`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/skull-woods`}]},turtle:{route:[`Help the three baby turtles and reunite them with their mother to reach the lake entrance. Bring the Ice Rod.`,`Freeze lava and moving seesaw platforms to create stable crossings. Merge along accessible walls when a frozen platform alone does not reach the exit.`,`Drop ice through the floor openings onto Grinexx below. When it surfaces, move away from its attacks and strike the exposed head.`],references:[{title:`Turtle Rock`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/turtle-rock`}]},ice:{route:[`Reach the mountain's Lorule crack with the Fire Rod available. Melt the entrance and pull the central statue's tongue to operate the lift.`,`Treat the dungeon as a controlled descent: inspect where a hole lands before dropping, melt obstructing ice and pull tongue switches to move floors into place.`,`Use repeated Fire Rod attacks to melt Dharkstare's shell. Slash the exposed creature and leave the marked triangular areas before they freeze.`],references:[{title:`Ice Ruins`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/ice-ruins`}]},finale:{route:[`After rescuing all seven sages, complete Lorule Castle's four trials. Use the tools and wall-merging techniques tested in the earlier dungeons.`,`Against Yuga Ganon, evade the trident attacks and return the energy volleys with the sword. Keep room to move rather than standing at the arena edge.`,`Use Zelda's Bow of Light during the wall phases. Shoot from behind; in the final variation, fire along the wall in the opposite direction so the arrow travels around to Yuga's back.`],references:[{title:`Lorule Castle`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/lorule-castle`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Visit Mother Maiamai to begin the search. Listen for the cries, use wall merging to dislodge wall-bound Maiamais and revisit rocks and deep water with upgraded equipment.`,`Buy an item from Ravio before asking Mother Maiamai to improve it. Rentals cannot receive those permanent upgrades.`,`Collect the four Master Ore pieces and take the pairs to the appropriate blacksmiths. Search the bottle locations separately; an empty bottle is a permanent reward even if its contents change.`],references:[{title:`Maiamai Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/maiamai-locations`},{title:`Master Ore Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/master-ore-locations`},{title:`Bottle Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/bottle-locations`}],title:`Maiamais and equipment improvements`},{route:[`Work region by region across both worlds, checking the corresponding crack exits. The same geographic area can contain different rewards in Hyrule and Lorule.`,`Return to minigames and optional combat challenges after upgrading equipment. Choose your edition's completion counters, then use the individual heart reference to resolve the remaining gaps.`],references:[{title:`Heart Piece Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/heart-piece-locations`},{title:`Explore Hyrule`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/explore-hyrule`},{title:`Explore Lorule`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-between-worlds/explore-lorule`}],title:`Hearts and the final sweep`}],editions:[`Lorule permits several dungeon orders. This itinerary places Thieves' Hideout before Desert Palace because rescuing Osfala makes the Sand Rod available from Ravio.`]},"the-wind-waker":{chapters:{outset:{route:[`Learn swordplay from Orca, rescue Tetra in the forest and board the pirate ship. In the fortress, disable the searchlights before crossing exposed walkways.`,`Use barrels and careful timing to pass guards while unarmed. Recover the sword near the upper approach to Aryll.`,`After arriving on Windfall, obtain a sail and free Tingle. Return to the King of Red Lions and sail east toward Dragon Roost.`],references:[{title:`The Game Begins`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/the-game-begins`},{title:`Forsaken Fortress`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/forsaken-fortress`},{title:`Windfall`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/windfall`}]},"dragon-roost":{route:[`Learn the Wind's Requiem, speak with the Rito and help Medli reach the upper ledge. Use water to restore the bomb flowers and open the cavern route.`,`Inside, cool lava with water pots and use bombs for blocked passages. Rescue Medli to obtain the Grappling Hook, then swing across the large gaps.`,`Hook Valoo's tail above Gohma to bring the ceiling down onto its shell. Once the shell breaks, pull or approach the exposed eye and strike.`],references:[{title:`Dragon Roost Island`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/dragon-roost-island`},{title:`Dragon Roost Cavern`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/dragon-roost-cavern`}]},forest:{route:[`Clear the creatures from the Great Deku Tree and climb using Baba Buds. Obtain the Deku Leaf, set the wind and glide toward the Forbidden Woods.`,`Use the leaf to operate wind devices and move suspended platforms. Cut vines with the Boomerang, marking several targets before releasing it.`,`Cut Kalle Demos's supporting vines with the Boomerang. Run into the fallen flower to attack its core, then leave before it closes.`],references:[{title:`Forest Haven`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/forest-haven`},{title:`Forbidden Woods`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/forbidden-woods`}]},gods:{route:[`Follow the Greatfish Island lead back to Windfall and obtain bombs from the pirates. Return to Outset and blast the whirlpool barrier to meet Jabun.`,`Place the three pearls on their matching Triangle Islands. In the Tower of the Gods, use the changing water level to navigate the lower rooms.`,`Guide the statues with the Command Melody and obtain the Bow. Shoot Gohdan's hands and eyes, then throw a bomb into its mouth; descend afterwards and draw the Master Sword.`],references:[{title:`Greatfish Island`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/greatfish-island`},{title:`Finding Jabun`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/finding-jabun`},{title:`Placing the Pearls`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/placing-the-pearls`},{title:`Tower of the Gods`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/tower-of-the-gods`},{title:`Mysterious Underwater Place`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/mysterious-underwater-place`}]},"fortress-return":{route:[`Return to the fortress armed with the Master Sword and bombs. Defeat Phantom Ganon by returning his energy ball, then collect the Skull Hammer.`,`Use the hammer on pegs blocking the rescue route. Climb the flooding tower and keep moving until you reach the rooftop arena.`,`When the Helmaroc King drives its beak into the floor, hit it with the hammer. After breaking its mask, use the sword on the exposed head.`],references:[{title:`Forsaken Fortress, Part 2`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/forsaken-fortress-2`},{title:`Ballad of Gales`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/ballad-of-gales`}]},earth:{route:[`Learn the Ballad of Gales and obtain Fire and Ice Arrows. Freeze Fire Mountain, collect the Power Bracelets and open the Earth Temple's stone entrance.`,`Learn the Earth God's Lyric and play it with Medli. Inside, use the Command Melody to aim her reflected light while Link operates switches and carries mirrors.`,`Acquire the Mirror Shield and combine beams to remove light-sensitive barriers. Illuminate Jalhalla, lift and throw him into a pillar, then defeat the scattered Poes.`],references:[{title:`Around the World for Upgrades and More`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/around-world-upgrades`},{title:`Fire Mountain`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/fire-mountain`},{title:`The Earth Sage`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/earth-sage`},{title:`Earth Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/earth-temple`}]},wind:{route:[`Use a Fire Arrow to thaw Ice Ring Isle's entrance and retrieve the Iron Boots. Learn the Wind God's Aria and find Makar behind the waterfall at Forest Haven.`,`Guide Makar to planting spots with the Command Melody. Use the Iron Boots on spring mechanisms and the Hookshot to reconnect routes when the companions are separated.`,`Hook Molgera's exposed tongue and strike it with the sword. Keep moving on firm sand and clear smaller worms when they interfere with your aim.`],references:[{title:`Ice Ring`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/ice-ring`},{title:`The Wind Sage`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/wind-sage`},{title:`Wind Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/wind-temple`}]},triforce:{route:[`Obtain the IN-credible Chart and work through the eight Triforce locations. Prepare the required equipment and rupees before setting off on a sea-wide collection trip.`,`On GameCube, take each Triforce Chart to Tingle for deciphering before salvaging its shard. In HD, collect five shards directly and decipher only the remaining three charts.`,`Use the correct chart and sea square to align the boat over the salvage light. Return to the Tower of the Gods once all eight shards are assembled.`],references:[{title:`The Triforce Charts and Shards`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/triforce-charts-shards`},{title:`World Tour`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/world-tour`}]},ganon:{route:[`Return to Hyrule and cross the restored route to Ganon's Tower. Complete the remembered boss rooms and follow the tower's visual clues through its maze.`,`Use Light Arrows for Phantom Ganon and cut Puppet Ganon's strings before shooting the tail jewel. Watch the tail's position during its later forms.`,`In the final duel, create openings with Zelda's arrows. When the battle changes, reflect her arrow with the shield to stun Ganondorf, then follow the sword opening.`],references:[{title:`Once Again, Mysterious Underwater Place`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/mysterious-underwater-again`},{title:`Ganon's Tower`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/ganons-tower`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Feed the Fishman in each sea square to build the chart. Combine nearby islands, Great Fairies, Big Octos and salvage sites in one sailing route.`,`Separate finding a Treasure Chart from salvaging its reward. Mark both stages before counting the associated heart or rupees as collected.`,`Collect bottles and capacity upgrades before longer optional challenges. Use the edition selector because HD changes some charts and rewards.`],references:[{title:`Treasure Charts`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/treasure-charts`},{title:`Pieces of Heart`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/heart-pieces`},{title:`Empty Bottles`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/empty-bottles`},{title:`Upgrades`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/upgrades`},{title:`Big Octo Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/big-octos`}],title:`Sea charts, hearts and upgrades`},{route:[`Unlock the Nintendo Gallery and take usable photographs before losing access to a subject. Review the figurine checklist before boss encounters and one-time character scenes.`,`Prepare a sailing route before collecting Forest Water for the wilted trees. The time allowance differs between the original game and HD.`,`Complete Zunari's trading chain and the island side quests as separate objectives. Owning a decorative trade item does not mean every trade or display reward is finished.`],references:[{title:`How to Unlock the Nintendo Gallery`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/unlock-nintendo-gallery`},{title:`Nintendo Gallery Figurine Checklist`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/nintendo-gallery-figurine-checklist`},{title:`The Wilting Deku Trees`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/wilting-deku-trees`},{title:`Zunari's Trading Quest`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-wind-waker/zunari-trading-quest`}],title:`The Nintendo Gallery and island errands`}],editions:[`GameCube uses eight deciphered Triforce Charts; Wii U HD replaces five of those chart rewards with shards directly. HD also changes sailing convenience and several collection requirements.`]},"twilight-princess":{chapters:{ordon:{route:[`Complete Ordon's fishing and village errands, then recover the sword and shield as a wolf. Use senses to follow scents and detect spirits after escaping the castle with Midna.`,`Collect Faron's Tears of Light to regain human form. In the Forest Temple, free the monkeys and use their swinging chain to reach new branches.`,`The Gale Boomerang carries bombs to distant targets. Bomb Diababa's side mouths, then target the bomb carried by Ook and the central mouth in one throw. Attack the eye when the head falls.`],references:[{title:`Ordon Village`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/ordon-village`},{title:`Twilight Realm`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/twilight-realm`},{title:`Faron Woods Twilight Realm`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/faron-woods-twilight-realm`},{title:`Forest Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/forest-temple`}]},gorons:{route:[`Restore Eldin's light and return to Ordon for Bo's sumo lesson and the Iron Boots. Wear the boots when stopping charging Gorons.`,`In the mines, the boots attach to magnetic surfaces and hold down heavy switches. Release them only after checking where Link will land.`,`Collect the Bow and the three elders' key shards. Shoot Fyrus's forehead, put on the Iron Boots, grab one of the chains dragging behind him and pull until he falls.`],references:[{title:`Kakariko Village Twilight Realm`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/kakariko-village-twilight-realm`},{title:`Death Mountain`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/death-mountain`},{title:`Goron Mines`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/goron-mines`}]},lakebed:{route:[`Warp the hot rock from Death Mountain to thaw Zora's Domain. Restore Lanayru's light, complete the carriage escort and obtain the Zora Armor from Rutela's grave.`,`Buy Water Bombs and enter Lakebed Temple. Turn the central staircase to direct water into unfilled rooms, keeping track of which side has already been supplied.`,`Obtain the Clawshot. Pull Morpheel's tentacle eye toward you, then in the swimming phase rise above its back and grapple the exposed eye.`],references:[{title:`Lake Hylia Twilight Realm`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/lake-hylia-twilight-realm`},{title:`Lakebed Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/lakebed-temple`}]},"master-sword":{route:[`Carry Midna to Zelda, then return to Faron in wolf form. Follow Skull Kid's lantern and music through the Sacred Grove, attacking when he becomes reachable.`,`At the guardian puzzle, the statues mirror your movements according to their rules. Work back from the two destination squares and reset if you trap a statue.`,`Draw the Master Sword to remove the forced transformation. Use voluntary wolf transformation to follow scents and reach digging routes during later exploration.`],references:[{title:`Sacred Grove`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/sacred-grove`}]},arbiter:{route:[`Speak with Auru and show his memo to Fyer for the desert cannon trip. Cross the Bulblin camp and enter Arbiter's Grounds.`,`Use wolf senses to track the four Poes and return their flames. Shift back to human form for the mechanical rooms and collect the Spinner.`,`Ride the Spinner along the rails and strike Stallord's spine through the sand. In the tower phase, jump between rails to evade fireballs and launch into the floating head.`],references:[{title:`Gerudo Desert`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/gerudo-desert`},{title:`Arbiter's Grounds`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/arbiters-grounds`}]},snowpeak:{route:[`Show Ashei's sketch to Ralis and fish for a Reekfish with the Coral Earring. Memorize its scent as a wolf and follow the mountain trail to Yeto.`,`Search the mansion's side rooms while Yeta directs you. Use cannonballs with cannons to break large ice barriers and obtain the Ball and Chain.`,`Break Blizzeta's outer ice with the Ball and Chain. Watch the floor reflection to anticipate falling ice, remove obstacles and strike her exposed form.`],references:[{title:`Snowpeak Mountain`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/snowpeak-mountain`},{title:`Snowpeak Ruins`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/snowpeak-ruins`}]},time:{route:[`Return to the Sacred Grove through Rusl's route and open the door leading to the temple. Notice the missing statue at the entrance before ascending.`,`Collect the Dominion Rod and escort the large statue back down. Use its weight on switches and scales, and its hammer to break barriers.`,`Shoot Armogohma's open eye with the Bow. Command a nearby statue to crush it, then finish the smaller creature left after the large body is destroyed.`],references:[{title:`Temple of Time`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/temple-of-time`}]},sky:{route:[`Complete the Hidden Village and Ilia's memory sequence to restore the Dominion Rod. Follow Shad's Ancient Sky Book search, gather the sky characters and have Fyer repair the cannon.`,`Inside the City in the Sky, use the boots against strong wind and the Clawshot on valid targets. The second Clawshot lets you move between targets without landing.`,`Pull Argorok down with the boots until its armour breaks. Climb the flying targets, move behind the dragon as it breathes fire and grapple the weak point on its back.`],references:[{title:`City in the Sky`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/city-in-the-sky`}]},twilight:{route:[`Return all Mirror Shards and enter the Palace of Twilight. Recover the two Sol orbs from the side wings and carry each back to the entrance.`,`Stay ahead of the pursuing hand while moving a Sol. Place it in floor sockets when needed to raise stairs, then retrieve it before continuing.`,`With the empowered sword, cut through the dark barriers. Zant's battle revisits earlier arenas: reuse the matching tools, then punish his exhausted spinning attacks in the final arena.`],references:[{title:`Palace of Twilight`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/palace-of-twilight`}]},castle:{route:[`Clear the courtyard routes for the keys and enter the castle. Use wolf senses to identify the safe route through the deceptive floor section.`,`Return possessed Zelda's energy shots with the sword. Against Beast Ganon, stop the charge as a wolf and attack after throwing him down.`,`Keep Ganondorf aligned for Zelda's arrows during the mounted chase. In the final sword duel, evade committed attacks and counter during the recovery.`],references:[{title:`Hyrule Castle`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/hyrule-castle`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Return to earlier regions with bombs, Clawshots, the Spinner and the Dominion Rod. Many heart rewards sit behind equipment gates rather than on the main dungeon route.`,`Search for Poes at night and use wolf senses to finish them. Group your searches by region, then compare the remaining total with the individual-location references in the completion section.`,`Restore travel connections such as the Bridge of Eldin and complete the Golden Bug, Hidden Skill and optional combat objectives separately. HD stamps and amiibo content belong to their own edition counters.`],references:[{title:`Ordon Village`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/ordon-village`},{title:`Sacred Grove`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/sacred-grove`},{title:`How to Repair the Bridge of Eldin`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-twilight-princess/restoring-the-bridge-of-eldin`}],title:`Hearts, Poes and regional returns`}],editions:[`Wii and Wii U HD Hero Mode mirror the world relative to GameCube and standard HD. Follow landmarks and room functions rather than reversing only a few left/right directions. HD also changes Tears of Light and adds edition-specific collectibles.`]},"skyward-sword":{chapters:{skyloft:{route:[`Find the missing Loftwing, practise flight and complete the Wing Ceremony. Follow Fi at night to the Goddess Sword and place the tablet.`,`Descend to the Sealed Grounds and enter Faron Woods. Search for the missing Kikwis, then use the Slingshot to lower the hanging vine.`,`Cross the Deep Woods using the rope and vine routes. Strike the crystal above Skyview Temple's entrance to open the door.`],references:[{title:`Starting the Game`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/starting-the-game`},{title:`The Wing Ceremony`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/wing-ceremony`},{title:`Sealed Grounds`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/sealed-grounds`},{title:`Faron Woods`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/faron-woods`},{title:`Deep Woods`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/deep-woods`}]},skyview:{route:[`Make the eye sentries follow a circular sword movement until they become dizzy. Adjust your position when several eyes must watch the blade together.`,`Obtain the Beetle and fly it through small openings to strike switches. Raise the water to reach the upper passages and rotate the carved key to fit the boss door.`,`Against Ghirahim's hand guard, hold the sword to one side, then slash from another direction. Match your cuts to the orientation of his incoming daggers.`],references:[{title:`Skyview Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/skyview-temple`}]},earth:{route:[`Help the Mogmas and obtain Digging Mitts. Search the marked Eldin areas for all entrance-key pieces, using bombs to clear blocked routes.`,`Inside the temple, collect the Bomb Bag and roll the large stone ball over lava. Use bombs on cracked walls to extend the ball's route.`,`Run uphill to avoid Scaldera's rolling body. When it inhales, throw a bomb into its mouth and slash the exposed eye after the explosion.`],references:[{title:`Eldin Volcano`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/eldin-volcano`},{title:`Earth Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/earth-temple`}]},lanayru:{route:[`Activate Timeshift Stones to restore machinery within their radius. Use the map to follow safe ground beneath the quicksand and power the three opening nodes.`,`Collect the Gust Bellows in the Mining Facility. Clear sand from platforms and switches, and use air to move the wind-powered mechanisms.`,`Cut Moldarach's claw eyes from an unguarded angle. Once the claws are gone, thrust into the central eye; use the bellows to uncover the boss when it burrows.`],references:[{title:`Lanayru Desert`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/lanayru-desert`},{title:`Lanayru Mining Facility`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/lanayru-mining-facility`}]},"flame-one":{route:[`Repel the Imprisoned and learn the Ballad of the Goddess. Restore the fallen windmill part with Scrapper and align Skyloft's windmills toward the Light Tower.`,`Enter Thunderhead and reach the Isle of Songs. In Faron's Silent Realm, collect the tears while managing the guardians' waking timer and avoiding the alerting water.`,`Use the Water Dragon's Scale to reach Lake Floria. Return to Skyview for sacred water and deliver it to the Water Dragon to open the waterfall.`],references:[{title:`Sealed Grounds, Part 2`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/sealed-grounds-2`},{title:`Activate the Light Tower`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/activate-light-tower`},{title:`Farore's Silent Realm`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/farore-silent-realm`},{title:`Help the Water Dragon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/help-water-dragon`}]},cistern:{route:[`Read the statue's directional clue and reproduce the sequence at the locked door. Explore the upper temple and its darker lower level as connected parts of one route.`,`Obtain the Whip to pull handles and steal keys from enemies. Raise the central statue, then return through the opened passages to the boss.`,`Pull Koloktos's arms away with the Whip. Take one of its dropped swords, break the leg and chest protection, then attack the heart inside.`],references:[{title:`Ancient Cistern`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/ancient-cistern`}]},sandship:{route:[`Complete Nayru's Silent Realm for the Clawshots. Help the skipper through his home, the shipyard and the pirate stronghold, then locate the invisible ship at sea.`,`Obtain the Bow and shoot the mast's Timeshift Stone through openings to switch the ship between eras. Free the crew and reach the engine-related passages.`,`Use Skyward Strikes to sever Tentalus's tentacles, then shoot its eye and slash while it is down. In the upper phase, cut the attacking hair and repeat the eye opening.`],references:[{title:`Nayru's Silent Realm`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/nayru-silent-realm`},{title:`Lanayru Sand Sea`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/lanayru-sand-sea`},{title:`Sandship`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/sandship`}]},"fire-sanctuary":{route:[`Complete Din's Silent Realm for the Fireshield Earrings. Help Scrapper bring the Water Dragon's basin to the summit to extinguish the entrance flames.`,`Use water-filled plants to cool lava temporarily. Obtain the Mogma Mitts and tunnel underground to operate switches and chase burrowing enemies.`,`Against Ghirahim, look for a sword angle his hands are not guarding. Avoid his landing attacks, then punish the recovery instead of striking into a closed guard.`],references:[{title:`Din's Silent Realm`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/din-silent-realm`},{title:`Volcano Summit`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/volcano-summit`},{title:`Fire Sanctuary`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/fire-sanctuary`}]},"hero-song":{route:[`Open the Gate of Time and receive Zelda's blessing. Help Levias in Thunderhead, then seek the three dragons' portions of the Song of the Hero.`,`In Faron, collect the Tadtones in their groups while watching your air. In Eldin, recover the confiscated equipment through the stealth route before approaching the dragon.`,`For Lanayru, carry the Life Tree seedling to the past at the Sealed Temple, then collect the grown fruit in the present. On the original Wii release, complete Faron and Eldin before Lanayru to avoid the documented Song of the Hero progression issue.`],references:[{title:`Gate of Time`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/gate-of-time`},{title:`Water Dragon's Song`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/water-dragon-song`},{title:`Fire Dragon's Song`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/fire-dragon-song`},{title:`Thunder Dragon's Song`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/thunder-dragon-song`},{title:`Nintendo: Song of the Hero progression issue (Wii)`,url:`https://en-americas-support.nintendo.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/2939/p/604`}]},finale:{route:[`Complete Skyloft's Silent Realm and use the Stone of Trials to open Sky Keep. Rearrange its rooms to connect the three Triforce objectives.`,`Follow Ghirahim into the past and fight through the army. In the final Ghirahim duel, force him toward the edge, finish the platform phases and break his large sword with matching cuts.`,`Against Demise, counter the sword attacks without overextending. When lightning begins, raise the blade to charge it, stun him and land the finishing blow while he is down.`],references:[{title:`Goddess's Silent Realm`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/goddess-silent-realm`},{title:`Sky Keep`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/sky-keep`},{title:`Monster Horde`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/monster-horde`},{title:`???`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/ghirahim-final-battle`},{title:`Final Boss`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/demise`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Complete Skyloft's character errands and search for loose Gratitude Crystals at night. Return to Batreaux at each reward threshold.`,`A struck Goddess Cube unlocks a chest elsewhere in the sky. Track the cube and the chest as two steps so an activated cube is not mistaken for a collected reward.`,`Revisit surface regions with swimming, Clawshots and improved digging. Finish bottles, heart pieces and equipment upgrades before optional endurance challenges.`],references:[{title:`Pieces of Heart`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/pieces-of-heart`},{title:`Gratitude Crystal Locations and Rewards`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/gratitude-crystal-locations`},{title:`Goddess Cube Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/goddess-cube-locations`},{title:`Empty Bottle Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-skyward-sword/empty-bottle-locations`}],title:`Hearts, Gratitude Crystals and sky rewards`}],editions:[`Wii and Switch HD differ in controls, quality-of-life features and some fixes. Test directional sword input before difficult fights; enemy guards require deliberate attack angles in either version.`]},"phantom-hourglass":{chapters:{mercay:{route:[`Take Oshus's sword, practise the required attacks and enter the Temple of the Ocean King to rescue Linebeck. Avoid lingering outside safe zones before you have the hourglass.`,`On the Isle of Ember, read the graves and mark the correct locations to release Astrid. Climb toward the temple and extinguish the entrance candles with the microphone.`,`Obtain the Boomerang and draw paths through several targets. During Blaaz's battle, read the horns on the upper-screen images and connect the three forms in that order.`],references:[{title:`Washed Ashore`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/washed-ashore`},{title:`Isle of Ember`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/isle-of-ember`},{title:`Temple of Fire`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-of-fire`}]},wind:{route:[`Take the Phantom Hourglass and return for the next sea chart. Use safe zones to stop the timer and wait for Phantom patrols before crossing.`,`Buy the cannon and follow the route recorded in Molida's hidden hideaway to cross the fog. Activate the Isle of Gust's windmills using the island clues.`,`Collect bombs in the Wind Temple. Throw a bomb into a small cyclone when it passes beneath Cyclok, then strike the fallen boss.`],references:[{title:`Temple of the Ocean King, Second Visit`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-of-the-ocean-king-2`},{title:`Cannon Island`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/cannon-island`},{title:`To the Northwestern Sea`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/to-the-northwestern-sea`},{title:`Isle of Gust`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/isle-of-gust`},{title:`Temple of Wind`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-of-wind`}]},courage:{route:[`Return to the Ocean King's temple and transfer the sacred mark by closing and reopening the DS while the two relevant screens are displayed. Use the equivalent lid control only if your platform provides one.`,`Buy the Salvage Arm and retrieve the Sun Key at the marked sea location. Return to Molida, open the sun door and enter the Temple of Courage.`,`Obtain the Bow and use the dungeon's clues to follow the invisible route. Against Crayk, aim toward the viewpoint shown on the upper screen, then attack the exposed shell growths and tail.`],references:[{title:`Temple of the Ocean King, Third Visit`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-of-the-ocean-king-3`},{title:`Salvage the Sun`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/salvage-the-sun`},{title:`Temple of Courage`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-of-courage`}]},"ghost-ship":{route:[`Follow the spirits' signal through the fog until you reach the ship. Explore the decks and escort the sisters while watching the patrolling enemies.`,`Verify the sisters' claims against the actual room clues. Plan the route around spikes and barrels before moving an escorted character.`,`Return the Cubus Sisters' solid energy ball with the sword while avoiding the misleading projectiles. After finding Tetra, visit Zauz to learn which metals the Phantom Sword needs.`],references:[{title:`Ghost Ship`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/ghost-ship`}]},goron:{route:[`Return to the central temple for the southeastern chart, then speak with all the Gorons on Goron Island. Answer Biggoron's questions using what the residents told you.`,`Alternate between Link and Gongoron to hold switches and open paths. Draw Bombchu routes through small holes to reach switches on the opposite side.`,`Use Gongoron to knock Dongorongo over and send a Bombchu into its mouth. In the later phase, place bombs where it inhales, then attack the exposed body.`],references:[{title:`Temple of the Ocean King, Fourth Visit`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-of-the-ocean-king-4`},{title:`Goron Island`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/goron-island`},{title:`Goron Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/goron-temple`}]},ice:{route:[`Compare the Anouki statements to identify the disguised Yook. Clear the snowfield route and enter the Temple of Ice.`,`The Grappling Hook can connect posts into a rope. Use ropes as bridges or springboards, and pull remote switches when a direct path is blocked.`,`Redirect Gleeok's fire and ice shots toward the opposite-coloured head with diagonal ropes. Later, attach a tongue to a post to pull the head down for sword attacks.`],references:[{title:`Isle of Frost`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/isle-of-frost`},{title:`Temple of Ice`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-of-ice`}]},ruins:{route:[`Read the Isle of the Dead's clues and obtain the Regal Necklace. On the Isle of Ruins, visit the royal spirits and lower the water to expose the temple approach.`,`Collect the Hammer in Mutoh's Temple. Use it on launch platforms and floor-switch patterns; work out how adjacent tiles change before repeatedly striking them.`,`Launch Link to Eox's marked weak points and hammer them. After the body breaks, land on the remaining head and attack its exposed jewel.`],references:[{title:`Isle of the Dead`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/isle-of-the-dead`},{title:`Isle of Ruins`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/isle-of-ruins`},{title:`Mutoh's Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/mutohs-temple`}]},bellum:{route:[`Bring the three pure metals to Zauz and take the forged blade to Oshus. Return to the Temple of the Ocean King; the completed sword can now defeat Phantoms from behind.`,`Pull away Bellum's slime and shoot the eyes around the arena. Use Ciela's time-stop power when the required opening appears.`,`After the ship battle, fight the possessed Linebeck. Watch the upper screen for the open eye on his back, stop time and move behind him to strike.`],references:[{title:`Temple of the Ocean King, Sixth Visit`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-of-the-ocean-king-6`},{title:`Final Boss`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/bellum`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Revisit early temple floors with bombs, arrows and later tools to create shortcuts. An earlier safe route can become unnecessary once a new item opens a direct passage.`,`Use the best checkpoint time available, carry healing and mark important symbols on the map. More Sand of Hours gives flexibility but does not replace safe-zone planning.`,`For completion, revisit islands for Spirit Gems, hearts, Treasure Maps and ship parts. Use the objective references below for individual locations; randomized ship-part rewards may need repeated activities.`],references:[{title:`Temple of the Ocean King Speed Run`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-ocean-king-speed-run`},{title:`Temple of the Ocean King, Fifth Visit`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-phantom-hourglass/temple-of-the-ocean-king-5`}],title:`Efficient returns and remaining treasures`}],editions:[`This route follows the Nintendo DS adventure. Microphone and lid-closing puzzles need the corresponding hardware or supported emulator controls; tapping the map alone does not replace those actions.`]},"spirit-tracks":{chapters:{tower:{route:[`Complete the engineer journey and help Zelda leave the castle without being seen. Guide her between safe positions while Link distracts guards.`,`In the Tower of Spirits, collect three Tears of Light to empower the sword. Strike a Phantom from behind so Zelda can possess it.`,`Use Zelda's armour to cross hazards or distract other Phantoms while Link handles switches. Collect the Forest Rail Map before leaving.`],references:[{title:`Starting the Game`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/starting-the-game`},{title:`Escape the Castle`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/escape-the-castle`},{title:`Hidden Castle Path`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/hidden-castle-path`},{title:`Tower of Spirits`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/tower-of-spirits`}]},forest:{route:[`Follow the trees' directions through the Lost Woods, including the final exception given by the clue. Reach Gage and practise the flute sequence before the duet.`,`Inside the Forest Temple, use the Whirlwind to move keys, clear poisonous mist and send stunned explosive enemies toward obstacles.`,`Blow away the cloud protecting Stagnox's rear and strike it. During the flying phase, blow an explosive enemy into the boss to bring it down.`],references:[{title:`Forest Sanctuary`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/gage-forest-sanctuary`},{title:`Forest Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/forest-temple`},{title:`Stagnox`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/stagnox`}]},snow:{route:[`Complete the next tower section and obtain the Snow Rail Map. Use the Anouki and Ferrus clues to find a route through the blizzard.`,`After Steem's duet, enter the Snow Temple and collect the Boomerang. Draw a path through fire or ice before the intended target to carry that element.`,`Hit Fraaz with the opposite element. When the original torches are destroyed, use the fire and ice left by his attacks as your new elemental sources.`],references:[{title:`Getting the Snow Rail Map`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/snow-rail-map`},{title:`Snow Sanctuary`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/snow-sanctuary`},{title:`Snow Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/snow-temple`},{title:`Fraaz`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/fraaz`}]},ocean:{route:[`Recover the Ocean Rail Map, arrange the broken bridge's repair and bring Carben back from Papuchia. His duet restores the tracks toward the underwater route.`,`In the Ocean Temple, obtain the Whip and use it on poles, handles and switches. Read the sword-handle clues before pulling a random sequence.`,`Pull a thorn from Phytops's tendril and throw it at the protected eye. Clear the covering, stun the eye and attack with the sword.`],references:[{title:`Getting the Ocean Rail Map`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/ocean-rail-map`},{title:`Ocean Sanctuary`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/ocean-sanctuary`},{title:`Ocean Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/ocean-temple`},{title:`Phytops`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/phytops`}]},fire:{route:[`Deliver Mega Ice from the snow region to unblock the Goron settlement. Plan the train route to reduce melting and avoid unnecessary damage.`,`Complete Embrose's duet and collect the temple-entry keys. Inside the Fire Temple, use the Bow and minecarts to activate distant targets.`,`Shoot Cragma's glowing body points to change the arena's routes. Ride the minecart upward and shoot the eye, then strike when the boss collapses.`],references:[{title:`Getting the Fire Rail Map`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/fire-rail-map`},{title:`Fire Sanctuary`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/fire-sanctuary`},{title:`Fire Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/fire-temple`},{title:`Cragma`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/cragma`}]},byrne:{route:[`Return to the Tower of Spirits and use the different Phantom forms for their specific obstacles. A protected or heavy route may require Zelda to lead.`,`During Byrne's battle, place Zelda where she can catch his extended claw. Move Link into position to attack while she holds him.`,`After the tower sequence, follow Anjean's new lead. The apparent restoration of the tower does not end the story.`],references:[{title:`Help Anjean`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/help-anjean`},{title:`Byrne Boss Fight Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/byrne-boss-fight`}]},sand:{route:[`Reach Rael, complete the duet and pass the railway trials. Enter the Sand Temple and retrieve the Sand Wand.`,`Raise sand beneath Link and heavy objects to reach ledges or move barriers. Temporary sand platforms collapse, so prepare the next move before creating them.`,`Catch Skeldritch's rolling boulders with raised sand and launch them into its armour. Reach the exposed weak point and collect the Bow of Light after the battle.`],references:[{title:`Sand Sanctuary`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/sand-sanctuary`},{title:`Sand Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/sand-temple`},{title:`Skeldritch`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/skeldritch`}]},compass:{route:[`Return to the Tower of Spirits with the Bow of Light. Charge shots when operating the light-sensitive targets.`,`Use Torch Phantoms to illuminate dark routes, Warp Phantoms to reach the appropriate targets and Wrecker Phantoms to break heavy obstacles.`,`Coordinate Zelda's position with Link's switches across the final rooms. Take the Compass of Light and follow the newly revealed tracks toward the Dark Realm.`],references:[{title:`Compass of Light`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/compass-of-light`}]},malladus:{route:[`Collect Tears of Light to make the train temporarily invincible and ram the armoured trains. Destroy the Demon Train's weapons while switching tracks to avoid attacks.`,`Guide Zelda past Cole so she can restrain Malladus, then shoot the Bow of Light. Protect her during the next phase and complete the flute duet.`,`Turn Malladus so Zelda can shoot his back. Strike the forehead jewel when he falls and complete the final combined attack.`],references:[{title:`Dark Realm`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/dark-realm`},{title:`Malladus Final Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/malladus-final-boss`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Take Niko's Stamp Book and stamp each station when you reach it. Return to him at the reward milestones rather than waiting until the final station.`,`Revisit settlements for passenger and freight requests. Deliver their cargo safely to obtain Force Gems that restore optional track sections.`,`Use the completed rail map to check isolated branches, rabbits and side destinations. The main story's restored tracks do not include every optional railway.`],references:[{title:`Stamp Stations List`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/stamp-stations-list`},{title:`Complete Rail Map`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-spirit-tracks/complete-rail-map`}],title:`Stamps and the complete railway`}],editions:[`The campaign uses the DS touchscreen and microphone, including Spirit Flute duets. Passenger and freight errands unlock optional tracks; they are distinct from restoring the four main realm maps.`]},"breath-of-the-wild":{chapters:{plateau:{route:[`Activate the Great Plateau Tower and complete the four shrine trials. Magnesis moves metal, bombs clear obstacles, Stasis stores impact on frozen objects and Cryonis makes pillars in water.`,`Prepare cold protection before climbing to the snowy shrines. Cook warming food or obtain suitable clothing, and watch the protection timer rather than relying on a single meal.`,`Exchange the four Spirit Orbs at the Goddess Statue, then meet the old man above the Temple of Time. Leave the plateau only after obtaining the Paraglider.`],references:[{title:`Raise the Towers`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/raise-the-towers`},{title:`Magnesis Trial`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/magnesis-trial`},{title:`Bomb Trial`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/bomb-trial`},{title:`Stasis Trial`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/stasis-trial`},{title:`Cryonis Trial`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/cryonis-trial`},{title:`Get the Paraglider`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/get-the-paraglider`}]},villages:{route:[`Travel through the Dueling Peaks toward Kakariko and speak with Impa. Register a horse or activate shrines along the road to make return trips easier.`,`At Hateno's laboratory, bring the blue flame from the village furnace, using lanterns along the route as relighting points. Unlock the Camera and take the requested photograph.`,`Return to Impa and begin the memory search. Gather ancient materials for rune upgrades and visit Great Fairies when you can afford to improve armour.`],references:[{title:`Seek Out Impa`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/seek-out-impa`},{title:`Locked Mementos`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/locked-mementos`}]},ruta:{route:[`Follow the road to Zora's Domain and accept Sidon's plan. Collect Shock Arrows around the Lynel's territory; defeating the Lynel is not required.`,`Ride on Sidon's back, break incoming ice with Cryonis and shoot Ruta's glowing targets after swimming up the waterfalls. Inside, obtain the map and change the position of the elephant's trunk to operate the waterwheels.`,`Activate all five terminals before the main control. Against Waterblight, attack its eye and evade the spear; in the flooded phase, break or return its ice blocks and use arrows to create an opening.`],references:[{title:`Reach Zora's Domain`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/reach-zoras-domain`},{title:`Divine Beast Vah Ruta`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/divine-beast-vah-ruta`},{title:`Waterblight Ganon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/waterblight-ganon`}]},medoh:{route:[`Reach Rito Village, speak with the elder and meet Teba at the Flight Range. Bring cold protection and practise aerial archery before the assault.`,`Destroy Medoh's cannons with Bomb Arrows while gliding between firing windows. Inside, tilt the beast and use airflow, sliding mechanisms and bombs to reach the terminals.`,`Use updrafts to gain height against Windblight and shoot its eye in slow motion. Avoid the tornadoes and reposition when the floating devices alter its attacks.`],references:[{title:`Reach Rito Village`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/reach-rito-village`},{title:`Divine Beast Vah Medoh`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/divine-beast-vah-medoh`},{title:`Windblight Ganon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/windblight-ganon`}]},rudania:{route:[`Obtain flame protection before entering the burning mountain region. Heat resistance for the desert does not protect against this environment.`,`Free Yunobo, escort him past the scouts and use the cannons. Inside Rudania, light blue-flame torches to open routes, then rotate the beast to reach the remaining terminals.`,`When Fireblight draws in air behind its flame barrier, throw a remote bomb into the suction and detonate it. Attack after the barrier breaks, avoiding the large sword swings.`],references:[{title:`Reach Goron City`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/reach-goron-city`},{title:`Divine Beast Vah Rudania`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/divine-beast-vah-rudania`},{title:`Fireblight Ganon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/fireblight-ganon`}]},naboris:{route:[`Enter Gerudo Town in the required disguise, recover the Thunder Helm from the Yiga hideout and return to Riju. During the approach, stay inside her protective field.`,`Obtain Naboris's map and rotate its three body sections to connect the electrical circuit. Follow the powered lifts and outer routes to the terminals.`,`Block or evade Thunderblight's rushes and break its guard. During the metal-pillar phase, use Magnesis to lift a pillar near the boss so its own lightning strikes it.`],references:[{title:`Reach Gerudo Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/reach-gerudo-town`},{title:`Divine Beast Vah Naboris`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/divine-beast-vah-naboris`},{title:`Thunderblight Ganon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/thunderblight-ganon`}]},preparation:{route:[`Follow the Lost Woods' wind clues to Korok Forest. Drawing the Master Sword requires thirteen permanent hearts; temporary yellow hearts do not count.`,`Use the album and Pikango's clues to visit the memory locations, then report to Impa for the final memory lead. Memories are optional for reaching Ganon.`,`Upgrade armour, prepare healing and gather shields, arrows and spare weapons. Choose which remaining shrines and side quests you want to finish before entering the castle.`],references:[{title:`The Hero's Sword`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/the-heros-sword`},{title:`Memory Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/memory-locations`},{title:`Great Fairy Fountain Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/great-fairy-fountains`}]},ganon:{route:[`Choose a castle approach suited to your equipment: water, cliffs and interior corridors offer different routes. Visit side rooms for supplies before entering the Sanctum.`,`Any uncleared Divine Beast bosses must be fought before Calamity Ganon. Use dodges, parries and the champions' powers to create openings when his protection is active.`,`During Dark Beast Ganon, use the Bow of Light on the glowing targets. Ride around the beast, then use the updraft and aerial aim for the final eye.`],references:[{title:`Hyrule Castle`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/hyrule-castle`},{title:`Calamity Ganon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/calamity-ganon`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Use the interactive map below to work one tower region at a time. Track shrine discovery separately from completing its trial and collecting its Spirit Orb.`,`Korok Seeds expand inventory through Hestu, but collecting every seed is a separate completion goal. Revisit suspicious rock patterns, tree arrangements and timed challenges with the relevant equipment.`,`The percentage shown after the ending measures map completion, not every quest, armour upgrade or Compendium entry. Finish the separate objective counters instead of treating that percentage as a universal checklist.`],references:[{title:`List of Shrines`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/shrine`},{title:`List of Shrine Quests`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/list-of-shrine-quests`},{title:`List of Side Quests`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/side-quests`}],title:`Shrines, Koroks and the map percentage`},{route:[`For Trial of the Sword, prepare before returning the Master Sword to its pedestal. Inside, collect food and equipment carefully because Link begins without his normal inventory.`,`The Champions' Ballad starts after all four Divine Beasts are freed. Complete its plateau trial, regional monument clues and added shrines before the final dungeon.`,`Track DLC shrines, equipment and quest rewards separately from the base game's objectives. Master Mode changes enemy pressure and resource planning; it does not share the ordinary mode's progression.`],references:[{title:`DLC Pack 1: The Master Trials`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/dlc-pack-1-the-master-trials`},{title:`Trial of the Sword`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/trial-of-the-sword`},{title:`Master Mode`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-breath-of-the-wild/master-mode`}],title:`Expansion Pass route`}],editions:[`The four Divine Beasts can be tackled in different orders. The base adventure and the Expansion Pass have separate shrine and quest totals; Master Mode is a separate save.`]},"tears-of-the-kingdom":JSON.parse(`{"chapters":{"sky-island":{"route":["Complete the first three shrines to learn Ultrahand, Fuse and Ascend. Use those abilities to build crossings, combine weapons and climb through solid ceilings.","Return to the Temple of Time for Recall, then reach the fourth shrine. Reversing the waterwheels opens the route that was previously inaccessible.","Exchange four Lights of Blessing for a Heart Container and open the large door. Follow the final sky-island path before diving into the water below."],"references":[{"title":"Great Sky Island","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/great-sky-island"},{"title":"The Closed Door","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/the-closed-door"},{"title":"Enter the Temple","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/enter-the-temple"},{"title":"Nachoyah Shrine","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/nachoyah-shrine"}]},"landing":{"route":["Meet Purah at Lookout Landing and report to Hoz near the castle's First Gatehouse. Return to unlock the tower and receive the Paraglider.","Use towers and nearby shrines to establish travel points. Accept the Regional Phenomena investigation and gather clothing and food for the first destination.","Follow Robbie's Depths expedition for the Camera. Bring Brightbloom Seeds and mark a route between Lightroots so the first underground trip remains manageable."],"references":[{"title":"Lookout Landing","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/lookout-landing"},{"title":"Crisis at Hyrule Castle","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/crisis-at-hyrule-castle"}]},"wind":{"route":["Help Tulin recover his bow, then follow the rising island chain. Use his gust only when it carries you toward a reachable platform or bounce sail.","Inside the Wind Temple, open all five turbine locks. Explore the ship's sides and lower passages; some mechanisms need an Ultrahand repair before Tulin can power them.","Break Colgera's icy weak points by diving through exposed plates or shooting from below. Keep enough distance to read its reappearance and avoid the tornadoes."],"references":[{"title":"Tulin of Rito Village","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/tulin-of-rito-village"},{"title":"Rising Island Chain","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/rising-island-chain"},{"title":"Wind Temple","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/wind-temple"},{"title":"Wind Temple Boss Strategy","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/colgera"}]},"fire":{"route":["Break Yunobo's mask and follow him up Death Mountain. Use the supplied flying vehicle and Yunobo's charge against the crater's rock heads.","Descend into the chasm and follow the statue route toward the Fire Temple. Switch minecart rails and use ramps to launch Yunobo into each of the five gongs.","Break Marbled Gohma's legs with Yunobo to expose the eye. In the ceiling phase, send Yunobo up the curved walls, then climb onto the fallen boss and attack."],"references":[{"title":"Yunobo of Goron City","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/yunobo-of-goron-city"},{"title":"Death Mountain Boss Strategy","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/moragia"},{"title":"Eldin Canyon Depths","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/eldin-canyon-depths"},{"title":"Fire Temple","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/fire-temple"},{"title":"Fire Temple Boss Strategy","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/marbled-gohma"}]},"water":{"route":["Restore the Zora Armor and investigate Toto's broken slate. Find King Dorephan, then shoot a King's Scale through the droplet-shaped formation seen from the floating fish island.","Clear the blocked pipes in the Ancient Zora Waterworks and climb the waterfall to Wellspring Island. In the Water Temple, operate four faucets using Sidon's water ability.","Wash away Mucktorok's sludge shark with water attacks. Chase and strike the exposed creature; clear sludge patches when they prevent you from moving safely."],"references":[{"title":"Sidon of the Zora","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/sidon-of-the-zora"},{"title":"Clues to the Sky","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/clues-to-the-sky"},{"title":"Ancient Zora Waterworks","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/ancient-zora-waterworks"},{"title":"Wellspring Island","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/wellspring-island"},{"title":"Water Temple","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/water-temple"},{"title":"Water Temple Boss Strategy","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/mucktorok"}]},"lightning":{"route":["Help Riju defend Kara Kara Bazaar and Gerudo Town. Follow the mural's pillar alignment clue to reveal the temple, then survive Queen Gibdo's first attack.","Inside the temple, follow light beams and rotate or move mirrors to expose the four battery rooms. Stand near Riju and fire an arrow at each target to charge it with lightning.","Use lightning or another effective element to weaken Queen Gibdo before attacking. Destroy the nests when their cores are exposed and use the resulting light to manage the smaller Gibdos."],"references":[{"title":"Riju of Gerudo Town","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/riju-of-gerudo-town"},{"title":"Lightning Temple","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/lightning-temple"},{"title":"Lightning Temple Boss Strategy","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/queen-gibdo-temple"}]},"castle":{"route":["After the four regional quests, report to Purah. Follow the princess sightings through the floating castle in the order shown by the investigation.","Refill between ambushes and keep a route back to a safe ledge. The sightings move between different floors, so read the vertical position on the map.","Fight the Phantom Ganon group in the Sanctum with the sages' help. Avoid gloom-covered ground and return to Lookout Landing afterwards for the next lead."],"references":[{"title":"Hyrule Castle","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/hyrule-castle"},{"title":"Sanctum Boss Strategy","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/phantom-ganon"}]},"spirit":{"route":["Investigate the Ring Ruins and follow Tauro to Dracozu. Complete the Charged Armor ritual, then cross Thunderhead Isles to Dragonhead Island.","Open the door with ten hearts and carry Mineru's mask along its indicated route. Deliver all four depot limbs to the Construct Factory and assemble the body.","Ride Mineru to the Spirit Temple. Block the Seized Construct's attacks, stagger it with consecutive hits and push it into the electrified boundary."],"references":[{"title":"Secret of the...","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/secret-of-the-ring-ruins"},{"title":"Thunderhead Isles","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/thunderhead-isles"},{"title":"Guidance from Ages Past","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/guidance-from-ages-past"},{"title":"Construct Factory","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/construct-factory"},{"title":"Spirit Temple","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/seized-construct"}]},"sword":{"route":["Investigate the geoglyphs and the Great Deku Tree's problem for the sword's whereabouts. The tree can provide a moving quest marker for the Light Dragon.","Reach the dragon from a high launch point and land near its head. Drawing the sword requires two complete permanent stamina wheels, not temporary yellow stamina.","Before the final descent, prepare strong fused weapons, arrows, healing and meals that restore gloom-damaged hearts. Temporary maximum-heart loss needs the appropriate recovery."],"references":[{"title":"Trail of the Master Sword","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/trail-of-the-master-sword"},{"title":"Recovering the Hero's Sword","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/recovering-the-heros-sword"},{"title":"List of Geoglyph Locations","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/list-of-geoglyph-locations"}]},"ganondorf":{"route":["Descend below Hyrule Castle through the underground route and face the monster army. Keep supplies for the Demon King rather than spending everything on earlier enemies.","Ganondorf can dodge your attacks. Read his follow-up and counter that opening instead of repeating the same strike immediately.","In the airborne finale, use the Light Dragon to regain height. Destroy the vulnerable growths on the Demon Dragon's back, then attack the stone on its head."],"references":[{"title":"Hyrule Castle Chasm","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/hyrule-castle-chasm"},{"title":"Final Boss Strategy","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/destroy-ganondorf"}]}},"collections":[{"route":["Work by region and by layer. Surface shrines correspond horizontally with Depths Lightroots, while sky shrines require their own island routes.","Check caves for Bubbulfrogs and record each cave entrance separately when auditing map completion. Wells have their own quest total and should not be mixed into the cave count.","Use the interactive map and objective counters for shrines, Lightroots and Koroks. The post-ending map percentage does not certify every quest, armour upgrade or Compendium photograph."],"references":[{"title":"List of Shrines","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/list-of-shrines"},{"title":"List of Caves","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/list-of-caves"},{"title":"List of Wells","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/list-of-wells"},{"title":"List of Named Locations","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/list-of-named-locations"},{"title":"List of Quests","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/list-of-quests"}],"title":"Surface, sky and Depths completion"},{"route":["Support Addison's signs with stable Ultrahand constructions, then speak to him before dismantling the support. Record the reward only after the sign is successfully secured.","Complete regional side adventures and the Great Fairy musician chain to unlock armour improvements. Save rare upgrade materials instead of selling every monster part.","Treat Coliseum rewards, stable rewards, fabrics and armour collections as separate goals. Use their location lists to plan targeted returns rather than wandering through cleared regions."],"references":[{"title":"Hudson Sign Locations","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/hudson-sign-locations"},{"title":"List of Coliseums","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/list-of-coliseums"},{"title":"List of Armor","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/list-of-armor"},{"title":"Pony Points Rewards","url":"https://www.thonky.com/zelda-tears-of-the-kingdom/pony-points-rewards"}],"title":"Side adventures and equipment"}],"editions":["The regional quests allow different orders. This route prioritizes a clear story progression and keeps optional map completion separate from the final battle."]}`),"echoes-of-wisdom":{chapters:{suthorn:{route:[`Copy tables, boxes and beds while escaping the castle. Build short, stable stairways to pass the guards and reach the Suthorn region.`,`Rescue Tri's friends in the rift, then enter Suthorn Ruins. Use Bind to move heavy obstacles and attack the Link impostor from an unguarded direction to obtain Swordfighter Form.`,`Against Seismic Talus, pull the glowing orb out with Bind and attack it. Repeat as the orb changes position, moving away from the boss's slams.`],references:[{title:`Hyrule Castle Town`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/hyrule-castle-town`},{title:`Stilled Suthorn Forest`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/stilled-suthorn-forest`},{title:`Suthorn Ruins`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/suthorn-ruins`},{title:`Seismic Talus Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/seismic-talus-boss-strategy`}]},gerudo:{route:[`Help Dohna and resolve the smaller desert rifts. In Cryptic Cavern, operate the mechanism that drains the sand blocking the sanctum route.`,`Learn the required statue echoes and use the dungeon's clues to choose them. Holmill can dig through suitable ground, opening routes that climbing echoes cannot.`,`Obtain the Bow from the Link impostor. During Mogryph's charge, place a statue in its path to make it collide, then attack while it is stunned.`],references:[{title:`A Rift in the Gerudo Desert`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/a-rift-in-the-gerudo-desert`},{title:`Cryptic Cavern`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/cryptic-cavern`},{title:`Gerudo Sanctum`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/gerudo-sanctum`},{title:`Mogryph Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/mogryph-boss-strategy`}]},jabul:{route:[`Help both Zora communities and reunite Dradd and Kushara. Defeat the Jabu-Jabu impostor, then cross the rift into the ruins.`,`Activate the five coloured switches to raise the central water column. Explore the side branches and use aquatic echoes for underwater enemies and obstacles.`,`Break Vocavor's back growths while avoiding its whirlpools. Attack the exposed weak point after it collapses and return to breathing space when necessary.`],references:[{title:`The Jabul Waters Rift`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/the-jabul-waters-rift`},{title:`Impostor Jabu-Jabu Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/impostor-jabu-jabu-boss-strategy`},{title:`Jabul Ruins`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/jabul-ruins`},{title:`Vocavor Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/vocavor-boss-strategy`}]},castle:{route:[`Return to Hyrule Castle Town after completing the Gerudo and Jabul regions. Enter the rift and move around the guards' sightlines.`,`Use echoes on switches and torches to open the castle's branches. Bind can reposition obstacles while a summoned creature handles nearby enemies.`,`Against the Ganon echo, evade the spear and fire bats. Return the energy ball with timed sword swings or use safe recovery windows for strong echoes to attack.`],references:[{title:`Still Missing`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/still-missing`},{title:`Hyrule Castle`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/hyrule-castle`},{title:`Ganon Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/ganon-boss-strategy`}]},eldin:{route:[`Help Darston resolve the Gorons' problems, then follow the volcano route. Use heat-resistant traversal echoes and avoid placing flammable objects over lava.`,`Defeat the bomb-using Link impostor and obtain the new weapon. Clear cracked barriers and combine moving lava platforms with climbing echoes.`,`Pull Volvagia's green necklace with Bind to stun it. Attack during the opening, then move to a safe platform before the dragon erupts elsewhere.`],references:[{title:`The Rift on Eldin Volcano`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/the-rift-on-eldin-volcano`},{title:`Rock-Roast Quarry`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/rock-roast-quarry`},{title:`Eldin Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/eldin-temple`},{title:`Volvagia Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/volvagia-boss-strategy`}]},faron:{route:[`Investigate the cotton-candy problem and escape the Deku Scrub prison. Follow the restored route into the Faron rift.`,`The temple has several entrances. Find the hidden ladder in the grass and use electric echoes to activate groups of crystals before their charge fades.`,`Electrify Gohma's leg crystals to bring it down. Attack the exposed eye, then prepare another electrical opening while avoiding its webs and summoned enemies.`],references:[{title:`A Rift in the Faron Wetlands`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/a-rift-in-the-faron-wetlands`},{title:`Stilled Faron Wetlands`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/stilled-faron-wetlands`},{title:`Faron Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/faron-temple`},{title:`Gohma Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/gohma-boss-strategy`}]},lanayru:{route:[`Climb Hebra with Condé's guidance and prepare cold protection. Use fire echoes to clear ice and stable objects to block damaging wind.`,`Carry the temple's temperature orbs with Bind and place them on the correct pedestals. Block air vents before transporting an orb that must remain hot or cold.`,`Use fire against Skorchill's icy helmet and ice against the fiery one. Attack the body once the helmet breaks, then adapt when its protection changes.`],references:[{title:`Rift on Holy Mount Lanayru`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/rift-on-holy-mount-lanayru`},{title:`Lanayru Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/lanayru-temple`},{title:`Skorchill Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/skorchill-boss-strategy`}]},forest:{route:[`After receiving all three goddess sanctions, enter the Eternal Forest and find the Ancient Orb. Learn its echo before searching for the other pedestals.`,`Use the triangular arrangement as a map clue and place an orb on each of the six pedestals. Follow the opened route into the stilled ruins.`,`Defeat the Zelda impostor by managing its summoned enemies and creating openings for your own attacks. Rescue the hero Link and prepare for the final cooperative section.`],references:[{title:`The Prime Energy and...`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/the-prime-energy-and-null`},{title:`Stilled Ancient Ruins`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/stilled-ancient-ruins`}]},null:{route:[`Return Link's weapons and enter Null's body together. Zelda's role shifts to movement, echoes and Bind while Link performs the direct sword attacks.`,`Create routes for Link and use Bind to pull obstacles or appendages into reach. When separated, use aquatic echoes and careful traversal to reach the reunion.`,`Pull Null's arms outward so Link can cut them. Clear summoned enemies, repeat through the changing arena and help Tri remove the exposed final core.`],references:[{title:`Final Boss Strategy`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/null-boss-strategy`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Learn an echo when you first defeat or discover its source; seeing a creature is not enough. Use the echo list to identify missing regional species and objects.`,`Revisit cliffs, caves and rifts after Tri gains capacity. Combine heart hunting with regional side quests and stamp stands to reduce repeated travel.`,`After the ending, use the available completion information to locate missing echoes. Continue tracking Might Crystals, hearts and stamps as separate objectives.`],references:[{title:`List of Echoes`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/echoes-and-locations`},{title:`List of Pieces of Heart`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/list-of-pieces-of-heart`},{title:`List of Quests`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/list-of-quests`},{title:`Stamp Stand Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/stamp-stand-locations`}],title:`Echoes, hearts and regional errands`},{route:[`Collect Fairy Bottles and expand accessory capacity through the Great Fairy. Equip bonuses that suit the route rather than leaving every slot on combat effects.`,`Record smoothie recipes as you discover them and prepare the resistance needed for each region. A useful recipe can solve an environmental obstacle without a new outfit.`,`Return to the Slumber Dojo with a broader echo collection for its timed challenges. Complete Dampé's automaton requests and the optional minigame rewards separately from the main ending.`],references:[{title:`List of Equipment`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/list-of-equipment`},{title:`List of Drinks`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/list-of-drinks`},{title:`Fairy Bottle Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/fairy-bottle-locations`},{title:`Slumber Dojo Training Guides`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-echoes-of-wisdom/slumber-dojo-training-guides`}],title:`Equipment, smoothies and challenges`}],editions:[`Many puzzles accept more than one echo combination. These routes give reliable mechanisms and progression requirements while leaving room for different solutions.`]},"four-swords":{chapters:{training:{route:[`Practise carrying and throwing a partner before beginning a scored stage. Agree who stays on a switch and who crosses first.`,`Inspect the available item pedestals when entering a new puzzle. Give each player a clear role instead of having everyone exchange equipment at once.`,`Before leaving a room, recover separated partners and check accessible rewards. A coordinated exit is safer than racing ahead alone.`],references:[{title:`Item Guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/item-guide/`},{title:`Stage guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/stage-guide/`}]},trees:{route:[`Explore the forest's branches and check the ground before charging through cut vegetation. Keep a route back to the party while collecting scattered rupees.`,`Use the supplied tools to move between isolated platforms and operate paired mechanisms together.`,`Strike Big Manhandla's buds with the matching coloured Link. When levers appear, pull them together to expose the next targets.`],references:[{title:`Stage guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/stage-guide/`},{title:`Boss Guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/boss-guide/`}]},cave:{route:[`Approach icy corners slowly and counter the slide before reaching an edge. Do not throw a teammate onto a platform that the receiving player has not checked.`,`Keep the Pegasus Shoes for the boss encounter and line up each charge before running.`,`Ram Dera Zol into the icy wall, then slash it while frozen. In the later phase, coordinate the colour information visible to the players.`],references:[{title:`Stage guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/stage-guide/`},{title:`Item Guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/item-guide/`},{title:`Boss Guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/boss-guide/`}]},mountain:{route:[`Wait for lava hazards to finish their cycle before crossing. Leave enough room between players so one mistake does not send the whole party into danger.`,`Assign the distant-switch task to a player whose tool can safely reach it, then regroup before the boss.`,`Return Gouen's projectile with the Link matching its current colour. After the boss disperses into flames, find and strike its vulnerable body.`],references:[{title:`Stage guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/stage-guide/`},{title:`Boss Guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/boss-guide/`}]},keys:{route:[`Finish Sea of Trees, Talus Cave and Death Mountain to earn the initial key set. Review the stage-selection screen before choosing Vaati's Palace.`,`For higher key tiers, replay the regions with the required rupee goals. Efficient collection matters more than winning a race against teammates.`,`Check every participating player's access before starting the palace route. Different key sets open different challenges.`],references:[{title:`Stage guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/stage-guide/`}]},palace:{route:[`Read each room as a cooperative puzzle: identify the exit, the switches holding it open and the tools needed to connect them.`,`Use the Cape for its intended gaps and control movement around fans. Avoid committing every player to a collapsing floor at once.`,`Recover health and choose the arena's equipment before beginning Vaati. Save the party's coordination for the colour-dependent phases.`],references:[{title:`Item Guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/item-guide/`},{title:`Stage guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/stage-guide/`}]},vaati:{route:[`Send bombs into Vaati's tornado and detonate them near him. Repeat until he drops within sword range.`,`In the later battle, pass the changing-colour projectile between the matching Links to create a stun.`,`Read the colours shown by the exposed arm targets and coordinate attacks on the corresponding sides. Do not assume every projectile follows the same colour rule.`],references:[{title:`Boss Guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/boss-guide/`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Replay the three regions for the higher key sets and the expanded palace challenges. Keep the rupee goal visible while planning which optional branches to explore.`,`In Anniversary Edition, finish the Realm of Memories for its sword reward and the Hero's Trial for its advanced technique. These areas are not part of the original GBA campaign.`],references:[{title:`Stage guide`,url:`https://www.linkshideaway.com/four-swords/stage-guide/`}],title:`Higher keys and Anniversary bonuses`}],editions:[`The original Four Swords requires multiplayer; Anniversary Edition adds solo control and bonus areas. Stages select different room layouts, so the route focuses on tools, cooperation and boss rules rather than inventing a fixed room sequence.`]},"four-swords-adventures":{chapters:{wind:{route:[`Lake Hylia: use Wide formation to push broad blocks and Box formation for square switches. Gather Force Gems from the side caves before reaching the barrier.`,`Cave of No Return: inspect the supplied items and use the appropriate formation for grouped targets. Keep track of cave exits that return to a different outdoor position.`,`Hyrule Castle: restore the sword's power with enough Force Gems, then clear the eye barriers. Return Phantom Ganon's energy volley and strike during the resulting stun.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 1 – Whereabouts of the Wind`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/whereabouts-of-the-wind/`}]},east:{route:[`The Coast: carry Moon Pearls to the matching portals and compare the two versions of a blocked route. A dangerous passage can be safer on the other side.`,`Village of the Blue Maiden: follow the residents' conversations and exchanges. Revisit the relevant houses after obtaining each requested item.`,`Eastern Temple: use Moon Gates to bypass hazards, the Bow for red-eye targets and the Lamp for torches. Exchange tools when needed rather than expecting one item to solve the entire stage.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 2 – Eastern Hyrule`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/eastern-hyrule/`}]},mountain:{route:[`Death Mountain Foothills: arrange the Links to cover grouped switches, then inspect the opened paths for the stage's equipment.`,`The Mountain Path: collect the Hammer and use it on the obstacles designed for it. Separate the Links when a narrow route or distant control requires individual movement.`,`Tower of Flames: climb through its indoor and outdoor passages. Against the Helmaroc King, break the helmet with the Hammer before attacking the exposed head.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 3 – Death Mountain`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/death-mountain/`}]},fields:{route:[`The Field: cut grass to reveal the four switches and use the group to lift large logs. Recheck side areas once the main path opens.`,`The Swamp: take Dampé's Power Bracelet and use it to move heavy obstacles. Carry the necessary object through the route before switching away from the tool that handles it.`,`Infiltration of Hyrule Castle: avoid the searchlights and bring the Lamp to Jalhalla. Light the four torches, attack during the opening and finish the smaller enemy revealed inside.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 4 – Near the Fields`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/near-the-fields/`}]},dark:{route:[`Lost Woods: compare signs and paths between worlds and use the Lamp for dark passages. Mark portal positions to avoid repeating the same loop.`,`Kakariko Village: search houses, back entrances, bushes and underground rooms for all ten thieves, then carry them to the pen.`,`Temple of Darkness: coordinate switches across the connected worlds. Return Phantom Ganon's real energy volley instead of chasing every image.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 5 – The Dark World`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/the-dark-world/`}]},desert:{route:[`Desert of Doubt: speak with the Gerudo elder and guard, then read the wind clue before entering the maze. Follow the instructed direction relative to the wind.`,`Desert Temple: inspect the branches for tools and keys before returning to its central obstacles. Keep enough Force Gems to empower the final barrier-breaking attack.`,`The Pyramid: use the Link whose colour matches Big Moldorm's tail. Continue matching colours after the boss divides.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 6 – The Desert of Doubt`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/the-desert-of-doubt/`}]},frozen:{route:[`Frozen Hyrule: bomb the concealed cave entrances and pull their levers to open the climb. Control movement carefully during the ice-covered fights.`,`The Ice Temple: leave a statue on a switch that must stay pressed, and use Cross formation for the grouped floor switches. Inspect loose pots before assuming a room has no mechanism.`,`Tower of Winds: climb the side-view rooms and coordinate separate platforms. Defeat the tower's guardian and complete Zelda's rescue before moving to the sky region.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 7 – Frozen Hyrule`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/frozen-hyrule/`}]},heavens:{route:[`Realm of the Heavens: study platform movement before committing the formation to a jump or narrow crossing. Recover isolated Links before moving to the next screen.`,`The Dark Cloud: complete the Shadow Link encounters and recover the Dark Mirror. Match the required colours when enemies stop responding to another Link.`,`Palace of Winds: use bombs on Vaati's tornado. In the later phase, launch above him, pass through the opening with a downward attack and strike from beneath the arena.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 8 – Realm of the Heavens`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/realm-of-the-heavens/`}]},ganon:{route:[`Escape with Zelda after defeating Vaati; the adventure still has a final confrontation. Keep the group together through the collapsing route.`,`Avoid Ganon's trident and clear the enemies when transported to the Dark World. Return to attack during his recovery windows.`,`Protect Zelda while she prepares the light orb. Return the incoming projectiles, then shoot an arrow through her orb toward Ganon.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 8 – Realm of the Heavens`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/realm-of-the-heavens/`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Aim to collect at least 2,000 Force Gems in each stage so the Four Sword can break its ending barriers. If short, explore the unopened side routes instead of repeatedly striking the barrier.`,`Collect Heart Containers and protective upgrades for the current stage, remembering that these do not form a permanent twenty-heart inventory across the campaign.`,`Treat Tingle's Tower activities and other multiplayer modes separately from the twenty-four story stages. Their availability depends on the mode and player setup.`],references:[{title:`Chapter 1 – Whereabouts of the Wind`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/whereabouts-of-the-wind/`},{title:`Chapter 8 – Realm of the Heavens`,url:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/four-swords-adventures-walkthrough/realm-of-the-heavens/`}],title:`Stage completion and optional rewards`}],editions:[`Hyrulean Adventure contains eight regions of three stages. Hearts, items and temporary upgrades are stage-specific; the archive's completion counters distinguish stage progress from a permanent inventory.`]},"tri-force-heroes":{chapters:{woodlands:{route:[`Deku Forest and Buzz Blob Cave: learn to throw teammates onto higher ledges and shoot raised targets from a totem. Keep the required item user at the top.`,`Moblin Base: separate the heroes for switches and rebuild the totem after each crossing. Bring all three to the Triforce gateway.`,`Forest Temple: shoot arrows through flames to light the torches. Bomb Margoma's opening, throw a hero onto the body and strike the eye; increase the totem's height as required.`],references:[{title:`Deku Forest`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=2`},{title:`Buzz Blob Cave`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=3`},{title:`Moblin Base`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=4`},{title:`Forest Temple`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=5`}]},riverside:{route:[`Secret Fortress and Abyss of Agony: use Water Rod pillars as temporary stepping stones. Raise the correct hero before throwing them across the next gap.`,`Cove of Transition: leave heroes on separate switches, open the route and reunite them in the correct order. Avoid stranding the only hero who can reach the remaining player.`,`Water Temple: use the Gripshot to cross targets and retrieve teammates. Pull Arrghus's smaller eyes away, then use a tall Gripshot totem to reach its central eye.`],references:[{title:`Secret Fortress`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=6`},{title:`Abyss of Agony`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=7`},{title:`Cove of Transition`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=8`},{title:`Water Temple`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=9`}]},volcano:{route:[`Blazing Trail: use the Gust Jar to send teammates across gaps and the Boomerang to recover a hero left behind. Confirm a safe landing before throwing.`,`Hinox Mine and Den of Flames: time attacks and switches from the moving carts. Return enemy bombs while keeping them away from the other heroes.`,`Fire Temple: coordinate the timed switches before the boss. Attack Moldorm's tail, then increase the Bow user's height as its weak point rises.`],references:[{title:`Blazing Trail`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=10`},{title:`Hinox Mine`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=11`},{title:`Den of Flames`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=12`},{title:`Fire Temple`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=13`}]},ice:{route:[`Frozen Plateau and Snowball Ravine: use Fire Gloves to melt barriers and light torches. Let rolling snowballs block the icy vents before crossing.`,`Silver Shrine and Ice Temple: use the Hammer on spring platforms and move the heroes in stages. A switch operator may need to join a moving platform last.`,`Hammer Blizzagia's head until the shell breaks, then use sword attacks on the exposed jewel. Avoid following its body so closely that the turn catches every hero.`],references:[{title:`Frozen Plateau`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=14`},{title:`Snowball Ravine`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=15`},{title:`Silver Shrine`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=16`},{title:`Ice Temple`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=17`}]},fortress:{route:[`Sealed Gateway: leave one hero at the necessary control while the others take the lift. Reunite only after the route stays open.`,`Bomb Storage and Training Ground: redirect bombs toward their targets and use the correct totem height for switches. Spread out when explosives are active.`,`The Lady's Lair: prepare for returning boss mechanics. Bomb Margoma, reach Moldorm's raised tail and remove Arrghus's protective eyes before striking its jewel.`],references:[{title:`Sealed Gateway`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=18`},{title:`Bomb Storage`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=19`},{title:`Training Ground`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=20`},{title:`The Lady's Lair`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=21`}]},dunes:{route:[`Infinity Dunes: use Water Rod columns and hammer-operated platforms to cross the sand. Leave a hero as a counterweight when the platform requires balance.`,`Stone Corridors and Gibdo Mausoleum: solve the room before moving every hero away from the entrance. Burn Gibdo wrappings to make the enemies vulnerable.`,`Desert Temple: strike Stalchampion from behind, use the Hammer on the exposed heart and build a tall Boomerang totem for the final head phase.`],references:[{title:`Infinity Dunes`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=22`},{title:`Stone Corridors`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=23`},{title:`Gibdo Mausoleum`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=24`},{title:`Desert Temple`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=25`}]},ruins:{route:[`Illusory Mansion and Palace Noir: keep torches lit where darkness hides enemies or routes. Position a second hero safely before advancing with the active one.`,`Lone Labyrinth: match each hero to the coloured paths. A full totem is not always the correct way through a colour-specific obstacle.`,`Grim Temple: free trapped teammates promptly. Strike Prismantus's orbs with the matching heroes, then throw a hero onto the exposed body to attack the eye.`],references:[{title:`Illusory Mansion`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=26`},{title:`Palace Noir`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=27`},{title:`Lone Labyrinth`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=28`},{title:`Grim Temple`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=29`}]},sky:{route:[`Floating Garden, Deception Castle and Dragon Citadel: combine throws, totem height and the available tools. Check where every hero will finish a platform sequence before starting it.`,`Sky Temple: prepare for a gauntlet and recover health when available. Maud removes your items, so the final fight depends on swords, positioning and totems.`,`Throw heroes across Maud's barrier, return her energy ball and climb the colour-matched parasols. Collect the final outfit material and return to Hytopia to finish Styla's rescue.`],references:[{title:`Floating Garden`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=30`},{title:`Deception Castle`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=31`},{title:`Dragon Citadel`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=32`},{title:`Sky Temple`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=33`},{title:`Last steps in the Kingdom of Hytopia`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=34`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Complete each normal stage before tackling its challenge variants. Choose an outfit that addresses the specific restriction, such as terrain, item range or survival.`,`Check the material rewards before replaying a stage for an outfit. Normal clears, challenge clears and crafted outfits are separate collection goals.`,`Enter the Den of Trials after its update content is available. Clear each enemy wave before advancing, conserve recovery resources and treat the trial as an endurance challenge separate from Maud's campaign.`],references:[{title:`Tips and Tricks`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/tips.php`},{title:`Bonus area: Den of Trials`,url:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/triforceheroes/soluce.php?p=35`}],title:`Challenges, outfits and the Den of Trials`}],editions:[`Play solo with two Doppels or with three local players; the campaign has no two-player mode. Official Nintendo 3DS online play has ended. The challenge variants and Den of Trials are separate from the thirty-two normal stages.`]},"ocarina-of-time":{chapters:{"forest-child":{route:[`Find the Kokiri Sword in the crawlspace training area and buy the Deku Shield. Equip both before asking Mido to let you pass.`,`Inside the Deku Tree, obtain the Slingshot and clear the climbing wall's spiders. Break the central web by falling from sufficient height, then use burning sticks on later webs.`,`Deflect the Deku Scrubs' nuts in the required order. Stun Gohma's red eye with the Slingshot and attack before it recovers or climbs away.`],references:[{title:`Reach the Deku Tree`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/reach-the-deku-tree`},{title:`Deku Tree`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/inside-deku-tree`}]},"two-stones":{route:[`Meet Zelda, learn Saria's Song and play it for Darunia. In Dodongo's Cavern, use bomb flowers to open routes and drop bombs into the giant skull's eyes.`,`Feed King Dodongo a bomb while he inhales, slash him while stunned and move aside as he rolls. Collect the second Spiritual Stone before heading to Zora's River.`,`Win the diving game, recover Ruto's letter in Lake Hylia and show it to King Zora. Offer a bottled fish to Jabu-Jabu; carry Ruto through the dungeon and use the Boomerang on its tentacles and Barinade's protection.`],references:[{title:`Saria Revisited`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/saria-revisited`},{title:`Dodongo's Cavern`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/dodongos-cavern`},{title:`Zora's Domain`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/zora-domain`},{title:`Jabu-Jabu's Belly`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/jabu-jabus-belly`}]},"adult-link":{route:[`Return to the Temple of Time with all three stones, play the Song of Time and draw the Master Sword. As an adult, race Dampé in the graveyard to obtain the Hookshot.`,`In the Forest Temple, collect the Bow and recover the four Poe flames. Watch the paintings for Phantom Ganon's real approach, then return his energy volleys.`,`In the Fire Temple, free the Gorons for keys and obtain the Megaton Hammer. Strike Volvagia when its head emerges, then attack the exposed weak point while avoiding falling rocks.`],references:[{title:`Temple of Time`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/temple-of-time`},{title:`Forest Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/forest-temple`},{title:`Fire Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/fire-temple`}]},"water-and-shadow":{route:[`Use bottled Blue Fire in the Ice Cavern and obtain the Iron Boots. Enter the Water Temple, track the three water levels and check beneath the central tower's floating block.`,`Defeat Dark Link and obtain the Longshot. Hook Morpha's nucleus out of its water tentacle, then strike from a corner between the spike panels, out of reach of the tentacle.`,`As a child, play the Song of Storms in the windmill and explore the drained well for the Lens of Truth. As an adult, open the Shadow Temple with Din's Fire, use the Hover Boots and stun Bongo Bongo's hands before shooting its eye.`],references:[{title:`Ice Cavern`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/ice-cavern`},{title:`Water Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/water-temple`},{title:`Bottom of the Well`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/under-the-well`},{title:`Shadow Temple`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/shadow-temple`}]},spirit:{route:[`Rescue the carpenters in Gerudo Fortress and cross the Haunted Wasteland using the Lens of Truth's guide. Learn the Requiem of Spirit outside the temple.`,`Return as a child and complete Nabooru's route for the Silver Gauntlets. Come back as an adult to move the large block and explore the other half.`,`Use the Mirror Shield to direct light and reflect each witch's attack into her sister. Against Twinrova, absorb three attacks of the same element before releasing the stored energy.`],references:[{title:`Gerudo Fortress`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/carpenter-rescue`},{title:`Journey to the Desert Colossus`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/journey-desert-colossus`},{title:`Spirit Temple (Young Link)`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/spirit-temple-young`},{title:`Spirit Temple (Adult Link)`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/spirit-temple-adult`}]},finale:{route:[`Finish the six barrier trials inside Ganon's Castle, collecting the Golden Gauntlets on the way. Refill magic and healing before the tower ascent.`,`Return Ganondorf's energy ball, shoot a Light Arrow when he is stunned and cross to attack. Follow Zelda through the escape without leaving her behind at blocked doors.`,`Against Ganon, evade the swords and attack the tail. Recover the Master Sword when the flames allow it, then finish the battle with it.`],references:[{title:`Preparations Before the Final Dungeon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/final-dungeon-preparations`},{title:`Ganon's Castle: The Final Dungeon`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/ganons-castle`}]}},collections:[{route:[`Search each region as both child and adult. Some Skulltulas appear only at night; soft-soil rewards require bottled bugs rather than simply planting a bean.`,`Record a Skulltula only after collecting its token. A defeated spider whose token remains out of reach has not advanced the counter.`,`Use the heart and bottle lists to combine nearby rewards with the right age, song and equipment. Return to the Skulltula House for each earned reward tier.`],references:[{title:`Gold Skulltula Guide`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/gold-skulltula-guide`},{title:`Pieces of Heart Checklist`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/pieces-of-heart`},{title:`Soft Soil Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/soft-soil-locations`},{title:`List of Bottles`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/list-of-bottles`}],title:`Skulltulas, hearts and the two ages`},{route:[`Complete the child mask trades in order and pay the shopkeeper before borrowing the next mask. The adult trading chain is separate and ends with Biggoron's Sword.`,`For timed adult deliveries, plan the route before accepting the perishable item. Avoid warp songs that spoil the delivery.`,`Earn Epona, finish the archery and fishing rewards, and check capacity upgrades. Master Quest uses different dungeon layouts and Skulltula placements, so use a dedicated layout reference for that mode.`],references:[{title:`How to Get Biggoron's Sword`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/biggoron-sword`},{title:`Mask Trading Sequence`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/mask-trading-sequence`},{title:`How to Get Epona`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/how-to-get-epona`},{title:`List of Minigames`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/list-of-minigames`},{title:`Upgrades`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/upgrades`}],title:`Trading, minigames and equipment`}],editions:[`The illustrated fourteen-chapter guide follows the original N64 quest. Ocarina of Time 3D keeps that main route, while Master Quest rearranges dungeon puzzles. The announced remake is not covered by a verified walkthrough.`]},"a-link-to-the-past":{chapters:{},collections:[{route:[`Use the interactive map to finish the twenty-four heart pieces and four bottles. Return to previously blocked caves with the Titan's Mitt, Hookshot and Flippers.`,`Check optional equipment as well as hearts: the Magic Cape, Cane of Byrna, Magic Powder, medallions and capacity improvements have their own uses.`,`Temper the sword with the reunited blacksmiths. After the required crystal progress, escort the Super Bomb to the Pyramid and use the fairy's upgrades before the final battles.`],references:[{title:`List of Pieces of Heart`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-to-the-past/pieces-of-heart`},{title:`Magic Bottle Locations`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-to-the-past/magic-bottle-locations`},{title:`Upgrades and More`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-to-the-past/upgrades-and-more`},{title:`The Cursed Fairy in the Pyramid of Power`,url:`https://www.thonky.com/zelda-link-to-the-past/cursed-fairy`}],title:`A final circuit through both worlds`},{route:[`Complete both A Link to the Past and Four Swords on the associated save, then pay the gatekeeper at the Pyramid's eastern entrance. Bring healing, magic and Silver Arrows.`,`Clear the four branches and collect their blades. These rooms use GBA mechanics, including diving; the Super NES floor plans do not describe them.`,`Pull Arrghus II's smaller enemies away with the Hookshot. Break Helmasaur King II's masks and finish the exposed eye with a Silver Arrow. Identify the real Mothula II among its copies.`,`Against Blind II, return the detached heads to the body with sword hits. After collecting all four blades, enter the final chamber and fight the four Dark Links in succession, adapting to their added spin, jumping and rushing attacks.`],references:[{title:`GBA bonus dungeon and unlock conditions`,url:`https://zeldawiki.wiki/wiki/Palace_of_the_Four_Sword`}],title:`GBA: Palace of the Four Sword`}],editions:[`The illustrated walkthrough and its fifty-seven floor plans describe the Super NES quest. GBA-specific content is listed separately here and in the edition counters.`]}},o=`Story routes, puzzle solutions, boss tactics and collection planning. Linked references provide additional room maps and individual collectible locations.`,s=[...n,...i].sort((e,t)=>e.year-t.year||e.title.localeCompare(t.title)).map(e=>a[e.slug]?{...e,scope:o}:e),c=e=>s.find(t=>t.slug===e),l=e=>`${e.title} walkthrough: story route, 100% collection goals, edition-specific counters, credited art and saved progress.`,u=e=>[`breath-of-the-wild`,`tears-of-the-kingdom`].includes(e.slug)?`/${e.slug}`:`/series/${e.slug}`,d=(e,t)=>`${e}:${t}`;function f(e,t){try{let n=JSON.parse(e??`null`);if(!n||typeof n!=`object`||!(`version`in n)||n.version!==1||!(`steps`in n)||!Array.isArray(n.steps))return[];let r=new Set(t.chapters.flatMap(e=>e.steps.map((t,n)=>d(e.id,n))));return[...new Set(n.steps.filter(e=>typeof e==`string`&&r.has(e)))]}catch{return[]}}export{u as a,l as i,c as n,d as o,f as r,a as s,s as t};